WEBVTT

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.359
In the year 1815,

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:20.160
the English colonial official Thomas

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.199
Stamford Raffles would travel across the

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:26.640
island of Java in what is today

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.640
Indonesia.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.920
At this time, the world was torn by war.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.719
In Europe, the Napoleonic Wars were

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:41.520
raging, and the Earth's oceans had

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.360
become just another battlefront.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.480
The lush tropical island of Java had

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.760
been until recently a Dutch colony, but

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.000
the Netherlands had been conquered by

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.280
Napoleon in his advance across Europe.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.840
And so the Dutch colonies had fallen

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.199
under the control of the French.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:06.320
Now the British desired to take Java for

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.600
themselves and strike a blow at

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.520
Napoleon's overseas empire.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.040
In 1811, British Marines launched an

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.479
invasion of Java, landing among its

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.159
coral reefs and sky blue oceans,

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:26.640
clambering through its shady mangrove

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.439
forests and up its beaches of black

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:32.720
volcanic sand, climbing the steep cliffs

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.119
in the shadow of its towering volcanoes.

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:39.360
From there they overwhelmed the

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.479
inexperienced Dutch defenders and took

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.159
the island for the British Empire.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:49.040
With them came the Englishman Thomas

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.560
Stamford Raffles who later wrote about

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.920
these events.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.920
Holland had ceased to be an independent

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.360
nation and in the year 1811 the French

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.119
flag was hoisted over Java. But on the

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:07.600
17th of September of the same year, a

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.840
capitulation was entered into by which

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.080
all the dependencies fell into the hands

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.800
of Great Britain.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.280
Raffles was a lifelong sailor and had

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.000
actually been born at sea on a ship

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.640
commanded by his father off the coast of

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.520
Jamaica. He became a clerk in the

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.000
British East India Company at the age of

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.840
14 and from there became a true company

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.519
man.

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:37.440
He had spent the best part of the last

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.000
decade furthering the interests of

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.120
British colonialism in East Asia and had

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.519
even become fluent in the language of

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:47.440
Malay.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.239
When Java was captured by the British,

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:52.560
partly as a result of his skill at

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.200
languages, Raffles was granted the

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.879
position of left tenant governor.

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:02.159
At the age of just 30, Raffles found

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:04.879
himself in charge of an island a

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:08.319
thousand kilometers across, home to more

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:12.599
than 6 million people.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.120
Raffles was fascinated by Java.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.159
He remarked on its dramatic landscape of

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:26.720
soaring volcanoes and steamy

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.480
rainforests,

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.840
its fertile rice terraces and remarkable

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:35.680
culture, as he wrote home to King George

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.319
III.

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:40.000
The gracious permission which I have

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.640
received affords me an opportunity of

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.799
interesting your royal highness in favor

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:47.200
of the amiiable and ingenious people

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.920
whose country they describe. A chain of

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.080
very high mountains runs along the whole

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.280
length of Java. Even in July and August,

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.280
the atmosphere is refreshed by

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.439
occasional showers and the landscape is

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.519
at all times of the year covered with

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:05.319
the brightest green.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.560
But most of all, he was fascinated by

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.080
Java's antiquities.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.120
Everywhere among its forests and shaded

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.759
rice terraces could be seen the remains

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:20.959
of the countless temples, palaces, and

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:26.919
even whole ancient cities left in ruins.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.440
A few years later, around 1815, he

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.400
embarked on a journey around the island

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.440
with the aim of surveying these ruins

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.520
and writing a book.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.840
Although by then Java was an

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.960
overwhelmingly Muslim land, Raffles

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.840
found everywhere the remains of an older

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.759
culture hiding just beneath the surface.

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.880
As he writes in his work, the history of

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.600
Java,

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.840
the Muhammadan religion, as it present

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.080
exists on Java, seems only to have

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.240
penetrated the surface and to have taken

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.039
but little root in the heart of Javans.

00:05:09.039 --> 00:05:11.199
But the antiquities of Java consist of

00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:13.759
ruins of edififices and in particular of

00:05:13.759 --> 00:05:16.400
temples sacred to the former worship.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.800
Images of deities found within them and

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.560
scattered throughout the country, either

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.360
sculpted in stone or cast in metal.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.759
inscriptions on stone and copper in

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:30.759
ancient characters and ancient coins.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.960
Raffles was fascinated by these remains

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.440
which seemed to confirm stories he had

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.039
heard. Stories of a great empire that

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:44.320
had risen up on that island. A thriving

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.520
combination of Hinduism and Buddhism

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.000
that had flourished for centuries,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.560
spread its influence across the sea to

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.560
countless other islands in the

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.520
Indonesian archipelago and built what

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.400
may have been one of the largest empires

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.039
in Southeast Asia.

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:08.919
This was the empire of Maja Pahit.

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:12.319
The numerous and interesting remains of

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:14.720
former art and grandeur which exist in

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.479
the ruins of temples and other

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:19.039
edififices. The abundant treasures of

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:21.440
sculpture and statuary either lay

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.600
entirely buried under rubbish or were

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.919
but partially examined. Nothing

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:28.080
therefore of the ancient history of the

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.639
people of their institutions prior to

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:32.720
the introduction of Muhammadanism of

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.199
their magnificence and power could be

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:37.919
accurately known or fully relied on. The

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:40.240
grandeur of their ancestors sounds like

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.639
a fable and it is only when it can be

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:44.479
traced in monuments which cannot be

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:46.639
falsified that we are led to give credit

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:51.080
to their traditions concerning it.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:53.840
Raffles became convinced that he could

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.880
find the remnants of the civilization of

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.840
Majapahit and so he traveled the length

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:02.560
and breadth of the island and visited

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.120
every ruined site he could along the

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.800
way.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.280
He stopped at the ancient cities of

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.960
Kadiri and Singasari and found there the

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.880
crumbling remains of city walls, palaces

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:19.680
and carved statues of the Buddha

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:24.000
alongside Hindu gods.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.080
But when he got to the valley of the

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.680
Brontis River in East Java, the locals

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:33.120
advised him not to go near the ruins.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.759
They told him that a terrible curse

00:07:35.759 --> 00:07:38.479
still lingered over those crumbling

00:07:38.479 --> 00:07:41.479
stones.

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:44.160
The natives had a superstition that the

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.240
site of this ancient capital cannot be

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.000
visited without some misfortune

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.680
attaching to the party who undertake the

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.000
visit. Those whom I had with some

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.840
difficulty induced to accompany me to

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.160
the spot did not fail to assure me that

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.080
I should lose my government within the

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.160
year.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.879
Finally, Raffles visited the great

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:06.240
capital of Majapahit, which his guides

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:09.520
told him lay buried near the town of

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.919
Trrowan.

00:08:11.919 --> 00:08:15.199
At Trrowan, Raffles hoped to find a

00:08:15.199 --> 00:08:18.400
magnificent ruined city, testifying to

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.919
the former greatness of this power.

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:24.560
But when he arrived, he would be

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.800
disappointed.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:29.360
He would find little more than a scatter

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.240
of broken brick work and assorted

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.800
sculpture littering the landscape,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.240
buried in volcanic ash and shaded

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.919
beneath the towering teak trees.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:46.160
A village adjacent is called Trulan or

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.800
the light of the moon. The ruins of the

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:51.200
palace and several gateways of burnt

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.360
brick are to be seen, but the whole

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:55.760
country for many miles is thickly

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.320
covered with a stately teak forest which

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.480
appears to have been the growth of ages

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:02.160
so that it is difficult to trace the

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.959
outline of this former capital. Ruins of

00:09:04.959 --> 00:09:07.600
temples mostly executed in brick are

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.279
scattered about the country for many

00:09:09.279 --> 00:09:11.839
miles and attest to the extent and

00:09:11.839 --> 00:09:15.279
grandeur of this pride of Java. The

00:09:15.279 --> 00:09:17.600
temples are beautifully decorated with

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:19.680
representations of flowers and other

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.920
peculiar ornaments which it would be

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.560
difficult to describe.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.519
In fact, the local people turned out to

00:09:29.519 --> 00:09:32.399
be right and perhaps Raffles should have

00:09:32.399 --> 00:09:35.279
listened to their warnings.

00:09:35.279 --> 00:09:37.519
Raffles would only govern the island of

00:09:37.519 --> 00:09:40.640
Java for another year.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.240
The Napoleonic Wars soon came to an end

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.640
and the British returned the colony to

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.680
the now independent Dutch, relieving

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.959
raffles of his post.

00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:55.200
And he would go on to suffer more

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.120
misfortune in the years that followed.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.519
Just 10 years later, he would have a

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:04.240
stroke likely caused by an underlying

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.480
condition in the blood vessels of his

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:08.080
brain.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.480
This stroke would kill him the day

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:15.120
before his 45th birthday.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.160
As Raffles wandered about those ruins of

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:21.040
crumbling red brick at the sight of the

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.079
ancient city of Majapahit, he had no

00:10:24.079 --> 00:10:27.360
idea that his fate was already sealed by

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.880
the birth defect lurking in his head.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.600
But perhaps that day he thought about

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.560
life and death as he walked beneath the

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.600
shade of that teak forest and listened

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.800
to the calling of coels and minor birds

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.360
high in the trees.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.680
Perhaps he thought about the rise and

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.480
fall of empires and the changing

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:53.519
fortunes of the world. Perhaps he

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:56.240
wondered how such a power had risen up

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.519
on the island of Java and left such a

00:10:59.519 --> 00:11:02.160
mark on the memories and imaginations of

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.440
that land's people. Perhaps he asked

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.240
himself how its people had constructed

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:11.440
these temples and palaces, these walls

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.440
and reservoirs,

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.000
carved such beautiful and haunting

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.920
monuments, and then fallen all at once

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:23.320
into ruin.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.800
My name's Paul Cooper and you're

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:01.279
listening to the fall of civilizations

00:12:01.279 --> 00:12:04.320
podcast. Each episode I look at a

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.480
civilization of the past that rose to

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:09.360
glory and then collapsed into the ashes

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.600
of history.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.760
I want to ask what did they have in

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:17.360
common? What led to their fall? and what

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:20.000
did it feel like to be a person alive at

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.880
the time who witnessed the end of their

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.200
world.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.360
In this episode, I want to tell the

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.240
story of the Majapahit Empire of

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.120
medieval Indonesia.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.440
I want to show how this empire of the

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.639
islands grew up on the volcanic land of

00:12:38.639 --> 00:12:42.560
Java and how it beat the odds to survive

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:46.160
in a world of medieval superpowers.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.200
I want to show how Majapahit expanded

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.600
its influence and dominion to other

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.639
lands over the seas and undertook

00:12:54.639 --> 00:12:57.600
voyages that have few precedents in

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.399
history. And I want to show what

00:13:00.399 --> 00:13:02.800
happened to bring this Empire of the

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:08.040
Islands finally crashing down.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.560
The surface of planet Earth is a thin

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:26.160
crust of solid rock which sits over the

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.800
softer and much hotter mantle beneath

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.959
it.

00:13:30.959 --> 00:13:34.399
This crust can be as much as 80 km thick

00:13:34.399 --> 00:13:39.680
in places and as thin as 10 km in others

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.320
and it is divided into seven major

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:45.040
tectonic plates.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:48.160
The largest of these is the Pacific

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.160
plate.

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:55.519
It is a vast sheet of solid rock more

00:13:55.519 --> 00:13:59.279
than 100 million square km in size that

00:13:59.279 --> 00:14:01.440
makes up much of the floor of the

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.880
Pacific Ocean and which alone accounts

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.519
for about a fifth of Earth's total

00:14:07.519 --> 00:14:10.079
surface.

00:14:10.079 --> 00:14:12.639
The Pacific plate is made up almost

00:14:12.639 --> 00:14:16.320
entirely of oceanic crust which is

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.880
different to the continental crust that

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:22.560
we all live on. Oceanic crust is

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.279
typically much thinner but made of

00:14:25.279 --> 00:14:28.079
denser bassalt rock.

00:14:28.079 --> 00:14:30.639
For this reason, whenever it impacts

00:14:30.639 --> 00:14:33.600
with other tectonic plates, the Pacific

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.839
plate is pushed downwards into the

00:14:35.839 --> 00:14:39.279
Earth's upper mantle, creating a zone of

00:14:39.279 --> 00:14:42.800
subduction. And these subduction zones

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.839
are renowned for their violent volcanic

00:14:45.839 --> 00:14:48.839
activity.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.040
Due to its immense size and density, the

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.440
Pacific plate has the most subduction

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.959
zones of any tectonic plate. And as a

00:14:58.959 --> 00:15:01.440
result, its borders are the most

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:06.680
volcanically active areas on Earth.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:15.600
This ring of raging volcanoes stretches

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.720
in a vast horseshoe shape for more than

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:22.320
40,000 km or about the circumference of

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.440
the earth from the southern tip of South

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.480
America all around the western shore of

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.680
the Americas and then through the sea

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:35.040
down the eastern coast of Asia.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.680
To geologists, it is called the

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:41.120
CircumPacific Belt, but in popular

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.440
usage, it has come to be known by

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:49.800
another name, the Pacific Ring of Fire.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.959
The 19th century English geologist

00:16:04.959 --> 00:16:08.399
George P. Scro was one of the first to

00:16:08.399 --> 00:16:13.639
describe this far-ranging phenomenon.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.360
A striking and constant delineation of

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.240
volcanic spiracles is displayed in the

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.800
numerous archipelos which bordered the

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.519
eastern coast of Asia. Beginning from

00:16:25.519 --> 00:16:28.320
the peninsula of Kamchatka, Japan, the

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:31.600
Luchu, Philippines and Malocas form a

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:34.399
scarcely interrupted linear series of

00:16:34.399 --> 00:16:37.440
volcanic islands amongst which many

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:40.320
contain vents in habitual activity and

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.880
bearing marks of recent and extremely

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.600
violent eruptions.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:52.240
The Pacific Ring of Fire is home to 3/4

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:56.240
of all the world's volcanoes and 90% of

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.880
the earthquakes on Earth take place

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.440
along this line.

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:03.839
The Ring of Fire has given us some of

00:17:03.839 --> 00:17:07.120
the world's most iconic peaks, including

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:11.120
the elegant cone of Mount Fuji in Japan

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:13.919
and the violently explosive Mount St.

00:17:13.919 --> 00:17:17.120
Helens in the United States as well as

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:20.000
the volcanoes of Mount Tambora and

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:25.280
Krakatoa whose 1815 and 1883 eruptions

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.520
were among the largest in recorded

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.520
history

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:37.919
as it is dragged down into the depths of

00:17:37.919 --> 00:17:41.679
the planet. The subducting Pacific plate

00:17:41.679 --> 00:17:44.080
has also created some of the lowest

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.960
places on the Earth's surface, giving

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.240
rise to a series of dramatic oceanic

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:52.799
trenches.

00:17:52.799 --> 00:17:55.120
The deepest of these, known as the

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:59.039
Marana Trench, reaches a sea depth of 11

00:17:59.039 --> 00:18:04.240
km, deeper than Mount Everest is tall.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:06.480
And in the areas where the ring of fire

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.600
passes through open ocean, it has also

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.799
created a huge number of volcanic

00:18:12.799 --> 00:18:15.799
islands.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:22.160
As volcanoes erupt under the sea, magma

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.120
spews out of the planet's mantle and

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:28.720
cools on contact with cold seaater into

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:31.360
solid rock.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:34.559
Over time, whole islands form around

00:18:34.559 --> 00:18:36.480
these volcanoes.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.120
And on these islands, the lives and

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:42.320
deaths and dramas and tragedies of

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:45.360
millions of human lives have played out

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.919
throughout history.

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:53.200
Perhaps the region where the Pacific

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.080
Ring of Fire has had the most effect in

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.640
sculpting the landscape is in the area

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:04.520
of what is today Malaysia and Indonesia.

00:19:04.799 --> 00:19:07.360
Here the Ring of Fire has lifted

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:10.559
thousands of islands large and small

00:19:10.559 --> 00:19:14.320
from the sea. And this archipelago has

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:17.200
come to be known by a name that in old

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:22.000
Javanese meant simply the outer lands.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:27.400
This name is Nusan Tara.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:36.720
The archipelago today called Nusantara

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:39.840
lies across an area of ocean wider than

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:43.440
the continental United States and laid

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.400
over a map of Europe would stretch from

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:51.360
France as far east as northern India.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:54.559
The archipelago is today home to more

00:19:54.559 --> 00:19:58.960
than 700 languages, six major religions,

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:02.480
and more than 300 ethnicities.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:05.440
And since modern humans first arrived on

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.559
these islands, they have given rise to a

00:20:08.559 --> 00:20:12.720
huge variety of different peoples.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:16.640
One Chinese Buddhist monk named Faran

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:19.520
who sailed to India in the 4th century

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:22.480
in search of rare religious manuscripts

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:25.440
describes the perils and beauties of

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:28.840
this ocean.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:32.559
In this sea there are many pirates. The

00:20:32.559 --> 00:20:35.600
sea is boundless in extent. It is

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.960
impossible to know east or west and one

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:41.520
can only advance by observing the sun,

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:44.880
moon or stars. If it is dark rainy

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:47.280
weather, you have to follow the wind in

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.600
perfect uncertainty.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:52.159
During the darkness of night, one only

00:20:52.159 --> 00:20:54.880
sees the great waves striking each other

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:58.400
and shining like fire, whilst shors of

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.559
sea monsters of every description

00:21:00.559 --> 00:21:04.360
surround the ship.

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.600
Today, the complex geography of this

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:11.520
region can prove confusing to many. As

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:13.760
you listen, if you find yourself getting

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:16.320
lost in the different names of islands

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:18.960
and seas referenced in this episode,

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:21.120
it's worth remembering that you're not

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.880
alone.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:25.679
This is by far the densest region for

00:21:25.679 --> 00:21:28.400
islands anywhere in the world. And in

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:31.520
fact, the government of Indonesia itself

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.440
has struggled to come up with a

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:36.320
definitive answer to exactly how many

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:39.919
islands there are within its borders.

00:21:39.919 --> 00:21:43.600
One 2002 study using the satellite

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:46.880
images Landsat identified more than

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:51.679
18,000 islands, while another 2010 study

00:21:51.679 --> 00:21:54.480
gave a lower figure, noting that only

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:59.280
around 9,000 even have names.

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:02.559
Nearly 90% of Indonesia's islands are

00:22:02.559 --> 00:22:05.760
tiny, coming in at less than a kilometer

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:07.840
squared.

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:11.200
Other islands are massive.

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:13.840
The archipelago contains the world's

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:17.120
second largest island of Papua or New

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:21.039
Guinea, the third largest of Borneo, and

00:22:21.039 --> 00:22:24.559
the sixth largest of Sumatra.

00:22:24.559 --> 00:22:27.840
In land area, each of these is larger

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:31.039
than Japan or the size of the United

00:22:31.039 --> 00:22:35.120
Kingdom and France combined.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.760
But while this archipelago is home to

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:40.960
some enormous islands, these tend to be

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:44.080
rocky and mountainous, their interiors

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:47.760
covered in impenetrable rainforest, and

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:51.039
generally sparssely populated.

00:22:51.039 --> 00:22:53.760
It is the fifth largest island in the

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:56.320
archipelago that has had perhaps the

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:59.679
greatest impact of all. And this is the

00:22:59.679 --> 00:23:02.559
place where our story begins.

00:23:02.559 --> 00:23:08.440
the long narrow island of Java.

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:24.480
Java is a volcanic island shaped like a

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:28.320
cigar running just south of and roughly

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:31.760
parallel to the equator.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:35.600
It's little over 100 km wide north to

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:38.240
south, but stretches for more than a

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:41.679
thousand km east to west, and the center

00:23:41.679 --> 00:23:44.720
of the island is dominated by a rocky

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:49.640
spine of conical volcanoes.

00:23:49.679 --> 00:23:53.360
A medieval Javanese creation myth called

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:56.799
the Tanu Pangalaran describes how the

00:23:56.799 --> 00:23:59.520
island was once floating free in the

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.440
ocean before the gods decided to nail it

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.440
down.

00:24:11.919 --> 00:24:15.520
The island of Java was unsteady,

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:18.400
constantly moving up and down as it had

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:21.279
no great mountains, not to mention human

00:24:21.279 --> 00:24:22.960
beings.

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:25.679
For this reason, Lord Jagat Prammana

00:24:25.679 --> 00:24:28.559
arose and promptly performed yoga on the

00:24:28.559 --> 00:24:30.799
island of Java.

00:24:30.799 --> 00:24:34.240
The deity stood facing east. He churned

00:24:34.240 --> 00:24:37.360
the water and it turned into foam and

00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:39.919
turned into mountains.

00:24:39.919 --> 00:24:42.320
For this reason, we have what is called

00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:46.080
the land above the clouds. Now,

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:48.880
now the gods Brahma and Vishnu agreed

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:52.400
and made human beings. They needed lumps

00:24:52.400 --> 00:24:55.760
of clay and formed them into humans of

00:24:55.760 --> 00:24:59.400
perfect beauty.

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:07.120
Today, partly as a result of its rich

00:25:07.120 --> 00:25:10.480
volcanic soil and its heavy rainfall and

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:13.760
strong sun, Java is the world's most

00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:16.960
populous island.

00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:20.080
It is home to more than 150 million

00:25:20.080 --> 00:25:23.120
people. despite its land area being only

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:26.880
about the size of England, making it one

00:25:26.880 --> 00:25:29.679
of the most densely populated places on

00:25:29.679 --> 00:25:31.679
Earth.

00:25:31.679 --> 00:25:34.480
More people live on Java than in the

00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:38.000
whole of Russia, despite it being about

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:41.840
130 times smaller, and its capital of

00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:45.120
Jakarta recently took the top spot as

00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:50.000
the world's most populated city.

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:53.279
This reputation for abundance goes back

00:25:53.279 --> 00:25:57.080
to ancient times.

00:25:57.520 --> 00:26:00.799
The Hindu epic poem, the Ramayana,

00:26:00.799 --> 00:26:04.000
written around 2,000 years ago, already

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:09.279
mentions Java as a place of wealth.

00:26:09.279 --> 00:26:12.080
The island of Yava is decorated with

00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:15.840
seven kingdoms, gold and silver islands

00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:19.520
rich in gold mines and a cold mountain

00:26:19.520 --> 00:26:24.760
that touches the sky with its peak.

00:26:25.919 --> 00:26:29.679
Even in ancient times, the island had a

00:26:29.679 --> 00:26:32.480
global reputation.

00:26:32.480 --> 00:26:34.799
It was prominent enough in the 2n

00:26:34.799 --> 00:26:36.960
century that the Greek writer and

00:26:36.960 --> 00:26:40.159
geographer Claudius Tommy included it in

00:26:40.159 --> 00:26:42.559
his work geographia

00:26:42.559 --> 00:26:45.279
right at the farthest edge of the known

00:26:45.279 --> 00:26:47.679
world.

00:26:47.679 --> 00:26:51.679
He describes an island named Yabadu, a

00:26:51.679 --> 00:26:54.240
name which he says means the island of

00:26:54.240 --> 00:26:57.440
Bali, possibly referring to the hardy

00:26:57.440 --> 00:27:00.159
grain millet, which has been an

00:27:00.159 --> 00:27:03.120
important food stuff there for centuries

00:27:03.120 --> 00:27:07.039
before the introduction of rice.

00:27:07.039 --> 00:27:10.000
As a result of its inclusion in Tomy's

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.799
work, the island would also appear in a

00:27:12.799 --> 00:27:15.600
number of medieval and early modern

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:19.600
mapundi or maps of the world. Although

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:22.480
few Europeans could agree on where

00:27:22.480 --> 00:27:26.000
exactly the island was.

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.480
In these maps, it usually appears

00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:31.919
somewhere wedged between Africa and Asia

00:27:31.919 --> 00:27:34.880
and always as far away as it was

00:27:34.880 --> 00:27:37.840
possible to get.

00:27:37.840 --> 00:27:39.760
But for the people who lived on the

00:27:39.760 --> 00:27:42.880
island of Java, it was the very center

00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:45.520
of the world.

00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:48.559
According to Javanese legend, it was

00:27:48.559 --> 00:27:50.640
where the gods had first created

00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:53.919
humanity and taught them the secrets of

00:27:53.919 --> 00:27:55.520
civilization.

00:27:55.520 --> 00:28:00.760
As the Tantu Pangaladan recounts,

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:04.159
such were the instructions of Lord Guru

00:28:04.159 --> 00:28:08.080
to all the gods. They descended to Java.

00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:11.440
The god Brahma became a blacksmith. The

00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:14.720
earth served as his anvil, water as his

00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:18.640
tongs, light as his fire, and wind as

00:28:18.640 --> 00:28:22.880
his bellows and the sky as his hammer.

00:28:22.880 --> 00:28:24.880
Lord Wiswakarma

00:28:24.880 --> 00:28:27.440
descended as a carpenter and made a

00:28:27.440 --> 00:28:30.320
house and people followed him and made

00:28:30.320 --> 00:28:34.240
houses. The Lord Ishwara descended and

00:28:34.240 --> 00:28:37.520
taught beneficial words in particular

00:28:37.520 --> 00:28:40.399
about the 10 kinds of good conduct and

00:28:40.399 --> 00:28:44.679
the five fields of learning.

00:28:45.600 --> 00:28:49.039
Since it sits virtually on the equator,

00:28:49.039 --> 00:28:51.919
Java experiences very little variation

00:28:51.919 --> 00:28:55.200
in sunlight throughout the year.

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:58.480
In fact, its shortest day is only 48

00:28:58.480 --> 00:29:02.080
minutes shorter than its longest.

00:29:02.080 --> 00:29:04.480
The western side of the island also

00:29:04.480 --> 00:29:07.440
enjoys very dependable monsoon rains

00:29:07.440 --> 00:29:09.840
from the Indian Ocean, which combine

00:29:09.840 --> 00:29:13.279
with the extremely fertile volcanic soil

00:29:13.279 --> 00:29:15.679
so that farmers could grow all year

00:29:15.679 --> 00:29:18.720
round and could often harvest three

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:23.039
whole crops of rice each year.

00:29:23.039 --> 00:29:26.640
The 14th century Chinese source, the

00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:30.000
Sunshi or History of the Sun Dynasty

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.640
describes the great abundance of this

00:29:32.640 --> 00:29:35.640
island.

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:38.799
The country is flat and fit for

00:29:38.799 --> 00:29:41.360
agriculture. Its products are rice,

00:29:41.360 --> 00:29:44.240
hemp, and peas, there being no wheat.

00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:46.880
Salt is obtained by boiling sea water

00:29:46.880 --> 00:29:48.960
and there is an abundance of fish,

00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:51.600
turtles, poultry, ducks, goats and

00:29:51.600 --> 00:29:53.840
cattle which they kill for the purpose

00:29:53.840 --> 00:29:57.039
of eating. Their fruit are papaya,

00:29:57.039 --> 00:30:02.919
coconuts, plantains, sugarcane and taro.

00:30:03.360 --> 00:30:06.399
From about the fifth century on, this

00:30:06.399 --> 00:30:09.200
vast agricultural potential would give

00:30:09.200 --> 00:30:12.960
birth to thriving societies and these

00:30:12.960 --> 00:30:15.200
would go on to construct elaborate

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:18.799
monumental architecture.

00:30:18.799 --> 00:30:21.679
For nearly the next thousand years, most

00:30:21.679 --> 00:30:24.320
of these societies would arise in the

00:30:24.320 --> 00:30:27.200
west of Java.

00:30:27.200 --> 00:30:31.360
One king of this time named Pur Navaman

00:30:31.360 --> 00:30:33.360
left one of the earliest stone

00:30:33.360 --> 00:30:36.960
inscriptions carved into a large boulder

00:30:36.960 --> 00:30:40.640
in the Chiruten River.

00:30:40.640 --> 00:30:42.720
The powerful, illustrious and brave

00:30:42.720 --> 00:30:45.279
king, the famous Por Navaran of the

00:30:45.279 --> 00:30:48.159
Taruma Nagara Kingdom whose print of the

00:30:48.159 --> 00:30:50.960
foot souls are the same as those of God

00:30:50.960 --> 00:30:53.960
Vishnu.

00:30:57.840 --> 00:31:00.799
The inscription is accompanied by a

00:31:00.799 --> 00:31:03.760
carved imprint of both of the king's

00:31:03.760 --> 00:31:06.799
feet, symbolically stamping his

00:31:06.799 --> 00:31:11.159
ownership on the territory.

00:31:12.799 --> 00:31:16.000
By the sixth or seventh century, a power

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:19.200
known as Kling seems to have risen up in

00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:22.720
central Java and a description of it was

00:31:22.720 --> 00:31:25.919
included in the Chinese source known as

00:31:25.919 --> 00:31:29.520
the Sin Tang Shu or the new history of

00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:33.080
the Tong Dynasty.

00:31:33.840 --> 00:31:37.279
Carling is also called Java. It is

00:31:37.279 --> 00:31:39.840
situated in the southern ocean. The

00:31:39.840 --> 00:31:42.640
people make fortifications of wood and

00:31:42.640 --> 00:31:44.720
even the largest houses are covered with

00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:48.240
palm leaves. They have couches of ivory

00:31:48.240 --> 00:31:51.519
and mats of the outer skin of bamboo.

00:31:51.519 --> 00:31:54.559
The land produces tortois shell, gold

00:31:54.559 --> 00:31:58.399
and silver, rhinoceros horns and ivory.

00:31:58.399 --> 00:32:01.200
The country is very rich. They have

00:32:01.200 --> 00:32:03.200
letters and are acquainted with

00:32:03.200 --> 00:32:06.200
astronomy.

00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:09.600
These early kingdoms seem to have met

00:32:09.600 --> 00:32:12.080
with great success on the island of

00:32:12.080 --> 00:32:15.440
Java, but little has survived of their

00:32:15.440 --> 00:32:18.559
records, their literature, or their

00:32:18.559 --> 00:32:20.960
architecture.

00:32:20.960 --> 00:32:23.279
But all that would change with the

00:32:23.279 --> 00:32:29.399
founding of a kingdom known as Mataram.

00:32:40.399 --> 00:32:43.760
The name Martam comes from the Sanskrit

00:32:43.760 --> 00:32:47.519
word martr meaning mother and likely

00:32:47.519 --> 00:32:51.360
meant something like motherland.

00:32:51.360 --> 00:32:54.720
This kingdom grew up not in the west but

00:32:54.720 --> 00:32:58.240
in the highlands of central Java right

00:32:58.240 --> 00:33:00.880
in the shadow of the great volcanoes

00:33:00.880 --> 00:33:05.320
Merbu and Marappi.

00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:08.559
The people of Mataram were the first to

00:33:08.559 --> 00:33:11.440
truly take advantage of this mountainous

00:33:11.440 --> 00:33:14.320
landscape and cultivated the steep

00:33:14.320 --> 00:33:17.360
slopes of this area using concentric

00:33:17.360 --> 00:33:21.600
terraces of rice fields fed and drained

00:33:21.600 --> 00:33:24.880
by intricate systems of canals and

00:33:24.880 --> 00:33:28.919
stonelined channels.

00:33:29.360 --> 00:33:31.840
This kingdom of the mountains was

00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:35.279
originally Hindu and worshiped primarily

00:33:35.279 --> 00:33:39.039
the god Shiva, the god of creation and

00:33:39.039 --> 00:33:42.039
destruction.

00:33:42.880 --> 00:33:45.600
Living as they did on a land constantly

00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:49.039
torn apart and remade by the destructive

00:33:49.039 --> 00:33:52.159
power of the volcanoes, it's no mystery

00:33:52.159 --> 00:33:55.200
why this god would have held sway in the

00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:57.919
kingdom of Martam.

00:33:57.919 --> 00:34:00.799
But with the rise of a dynasty known as

00:34:00.799 --> 00:34:03.919
the Shilendras in the 8th century,

00:34:03.919 --> 00:34:07.039
Martam began to drift further towards a

00:34:07.039 --> 00:34:11.560
new religion, Buddhism.

00:34:16.960 --> 00:34:19.520
In this period, Mataram would become

00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:22.159
what's known to historians as an

00:34:22.159 --> 00:34:25.440
Indianized Hindu Buddhist kingdom with

00:34:25.440 --> 00:34:28.480
elements of both religions combined into

00:34:28.480 --> 00:34:31.599
a syncratic whole.

00:34:31.599 --> 00:34:34.240
These religions became so intertwined

00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:36.560
over the centuries that followed that

00:34:36.560 --> 00:34:39.679
the epic Tantu Pangaladan even recounts

00:34:39.679 --> 00:34:42.399
the story of one god who came down to

00:34:42.399 --> 00:34:45.839
earth and divided himself into two holy

00:34:45.839 --> 00:34:49.359
sages, one Buddhist and one Hindu so

00:34:49.359 --> 00:34:51.919
that he could spread both religions at

00:34:51.919 --> 00:34:55.280
the same time.

00:34:55.280 --> 00:34:59.440
Let us tell about Maampu Paleat.

00:34:59.440 --> 00:35:02.800
He returned to the island of Java. He

00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:06.240
divided his body into two and it became

00:35:06.240 --> 00:35:09.839
a shyite and a Buddhist. Off they went

00:35:09.839 --> 00:35:12.560
and arrived in Java. They headed for

00:35:12.560 --> 00:35:17.640
Gira and set up a monastery together.

00:35:17.680 --> 00:35:20.640
The kings of Java would even come to be

00:35:20.640 --> 00:35:24.240
known by the title Bura Siwa Buddha

00:35:24.240 --> 00:35:28.160
meaning the divine Lord Shiva Buddha. a

00:35:28.160 --> 00:35:30.720
royal figure in whom the two sacred

00:35:30.720 --> 00:35:34.760
beings were fused.

00:35:34.960 --> 00:35:37.359
This was in general a period of

00:35:37.359 --> 00:35:41.280
coexistence and unity. And it's in this

00:35:41.280 --> 00:35:44.560
era that some of Java's most remarkable

00:35:44.560 --> 00:35:49.000
monuments would be built.

00:35:59.599 --> 00:36:02.240
The kings of the mountain kingdom of

00:36:02.240 --> 00:36:07.040
Mataram were ambitious builders.

00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:09.920
Around the year 850, they completed

00:36:09.920 --> 00:36:13.520
construction of a great temple to Shiva,

00:36:13.520 --> 00:36:16.640
the towering Pramanan temple, which

00:36:16.640 --> 00:36:20.240
still sends its eight sturdy spires up

00:36:20.240 --> 00:36:24.960
into the skies of southern Java.

00:36:24.960 --> 00:36:28.000
It is the second largest Hindu structure

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.440
in Southeast Asia behind only anchor

00:36:31.440 --> 00:36:35.040
watt in Cambodia and it left its mark

00:36:35.040 --> 00:36:38.079
not just on the landscape but in the

00:36:38.079 --> 00:36:40.400
name of the year in which its

00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:44.599
construction was completed.

00:36:45.280 --> 00:36:48.640
By this time, the Javanese had adopted a

00:36:48.640 --> 00:36:52.079
unique system of naming each year,

00:36:52.079 --> 00:36:54.720
giving them what are known as moon

00:36:54.720 --> 00:37:00.320
chronogs or in Javanese Chundra sanka.

00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:03.040
This system used the Indian Shaka

00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:05.599
calendar which assigned numbers to the

00:37:05.599 --> 00:37:10.560
years the way we do today like 1066,

00:37:10.560 --> 00:37:14.640
1939 or 2026.

00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:17.440
But the Javanese developed this Indian

00:37:17.440 --> 00:37:22.240
calendar with their own poetic flourish.

00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:26.000
They gave each number from 0 to 10 an

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:30.160
array of possible symbols like the sun,

00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:33.359
moon, fire, and other elements which

00:37:33.359 --> 00:37:35.599
they could choose from to give the year

00:37:35.599 --> 00:37:39.280
a name that seemed the most fitting.

00:37:39.280 --> 00:37:42.560
For example, the 18th century Balan

00:37:42.560 --> 00:37:45.760
chronicle named the Babadgumi gives one

00:37:45.760 --> 00:37:50.079
year the name Gaja Aappi Anin Watu or

00:37:50.079 --> 00:37:54.000
elephant, fire, wind, stone due to a

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:56.160
particularly violent eruption of the

00:37:56.160 --> 00:37:59.440
volcano Mount Aong that took place in

00:37:59.440 --> 00:38:01.760
East Bali.

00:38:01.760 --> 00:38:04.560
Another year in which a fierce battle

00:38:04.560 --> 00:38:07.599
took place was named Paksha Shakara

00:38:07.599 --> 00:38:11.280
Babumi or the force of violence moving

00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:13.839
upon the earth.

00:38:13.839 --> 00:38:16.320
Due to this system, we can sometimes get

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.560
a sense from the names that years were

00:38:18.560 --> 00:38:21.359
given of the overriding mood in the

00:38:21.359 --> 00:38:22.960
kingdom.

00:38:22.960 --> 00:38:26.880
Sometimes a mood of joy and celebration,

00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:32.320
at others of despair and sorrow.

00:38:32.320 --> 00:38:34.880
On the year that the kings of Mataram

00:38:34.880 --> 00:38:37.680
completed the Prammanan temple, they

00:38:37.680 --> 00:38:40.480
were clearly proud of their achievement

00:38:40.480 --> 00:38:43.119
and because of its eight towering main

00:38:43.119 --> 00:38:46.160
shrines, they named the year in honor of

00:38:46.160 --> 00:38:50.720
it. In our calendar it was 856

00:38:50.720 --> 00:38:53.760
but in the Shaka calendar it was called

00:38:53.760 --> 00:38:56.960
eight mountains of the holy monks as

00:38:56.960 --> 00:39:00.640
recorded in a text known as the shavra

00:39:00.640 --> 00:39:03.640
inscription.

00:39:04.079 --> 00:39:06.400
In the time of the Shaka year, eight

00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:09.280
mountains of the holy monks, the statue

00:39:09.280 --> 00:39:12.960
of the god was finished and inaugurated.

00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:14.880
After the shiva sanctuary had been

00:39:14.880 --> 00:39:17.839
completed in its divine splendor, the

00:39:17.839 --> 00:39:20.240
course of the river was changed so that

00:39:20.240 --> 00:39:23.040
it rippled along the grounds.

00:39:23.040 --> 00:39:25.599
Then the grounds were inaugurated as

00:39:25.599 --> 00:39:29.880
temple grounds with the gods.

00:39:30.720 --> 00:39:33.200
Other temples built by the kings of

00:39:33.200 --> 00:39:36.160
Mataram, such as the sprawling temple at

00:39:36.160 --> 00:39:39.200
Seu, are thought to have been Buddhist

00:39:39.200 --> 00:39:41.440
since they were built in the form of a

00:39:41.440 --> 00:39:44.720
mandala, an important geometrical

00:39:44.720 --> 00:39:47.599
concept in Buddhism that is used to

00:39:47.599 --> 00:39:51.920
conceptualize the shape of the universe.

00:39:51.920 --> 00:39:54.880
But chief among their works is the

00:39:54.880 --> 00:39:57.119
structure that would become what is

00:39:57.119 --> 00:40:00.160
still the largest Buddhist temple in the

00:40:00.160 --> 00:40:03.160
world.

00:40:03.359 --> 00:40:05.520
It's thought that the Javanese of the

00:40:05.520 --> 00:40:09.839
time called it Bumi Shambara Budara or

00:40:09.839 --> 00:40:13.040
the mountain of combined virtues of the

00:40:13.040 --> 00:40:15.920
10 stages of Buddhahood.

00:40:15.920 --> 00:40:18.640
But today it is known by a name meaning

00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:25.079
only the great Buddha or Boro Buddhur.

00:40:26.640 --> 00:40:30.000
Boro Budur rises like a mountain from

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.200
the river plains right in the shadow of

00:40:33.200 --> 00:40:37.839
the great volcano Mount Marappi.

00:40:37.839 --> 00:40:41.040
This vast complex consists of nine

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:44.320
stacked platforms rising like a wedding

00:40:44.320 --> 00:40:48.640
cake up to a height of 35 m and topped

00:40:48.640 --> 00:40:51.440
by a central dome.

00:40:51.440 --> 00:40:54.640
One heritage worker Gerard Bolla

00:40:54.640 --> 00:40:57.119
describes the appearance of this

00:40:57.119 --> 00:41:00.920
incredible temple.

00:41:01.119 --> 00:41:04.400
Orodor the mountain of the virtues is

00:41:04.400 --> 00:41:07.119
first of all a landscape. The landscape

00:41:07.119 --> 00:41:10.000
which over a thousand years ago met the

00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:12.000
eyes of those who came on pilgrimage

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:14.800
here to seek inner peace. It has hardly

00:41:14.800 --> 00:41:18.480
changed. In the distance, two volcanoes,

00:41:18.480 --> 00:41:21.040
one ever menacing, glows red in the

00:41:21.040 --> 00:41:23.520
night. All around in the middle

00:41:23.520 --> 00:41:27.119
distance, a ring of mountains built on

00:41:27.119 --> 00:41:30.160
this same volcanic stone. Borobodor

00:41:30.160 --> 00:41:32.800
emerges from a delicate green background

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:36.599
of tropical vegetation.

00:41:37.920 --> 00:41:41.280
The design of Bora Budur like the temple

00:41:41.280 --> 00:41:45.440
at Su is an enormous mandala visible

00:41:45.440 --> 00:41:47.440
from above.

00:41:47.440 --> 00:41:50.560
But this mandala covers the area of two

00:41:50.560 --> 00:41:53.920
football pitches and guides its pilgrims

00:41:53.920 --> 00:41:56.319
up through a series of concentric

00:41:56.319 --> 00:41:59.680
walkways and stairways carved out of

00:41:59.680 --> 00:42:02.720
black volcanic stone.

00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:06.240
These are all lined with nearly 3,000

00:42:06.240 --> 00:42:10.480
carved freezes and 500 Buddha statues

00:42:10.480 --> 00:42:13.200
created by the finest craftsmen the

00:42:13.200 --> 00:42:15.760
kingdom could find.

00:42:15.760 --> 00:42:18.480
The archaeologist, Professor Raden

00:42:18.480 --> 00:42:20.960
Sokmano, who was in charge of the

00:42:20.960 --> 00:42:23.359
project to restore the great temple in

00:42:23.359 --> 00:42:27.119
modern times, describes its spiritual

00:42:27.119 --> 00:42:30.119
function.

00:42:30.960 --> 00:42:33.280
For the ardent Buddhist, it is the

00:42:33.280 --> 00:42:35.520
highest wisdom that leads to the

00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:37.680
ultimate salvation. And for the

00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:39.920
technician, the highest degree of

00:42:39.920 --> 00:42:42.880
expertise that leads to the appropriate

00:42:42.880 --> 00:42:46.880
fulfillment of his duty. In both cases,

00:42:46.880 --> 00:42:49.920
Boro Budor is the embodiment of such a

00:42:49.920 --> 00:42:53.920
deeply felt wish. It is a prayer in

00:42:53.920 --> 00:42:56.920
stone.

00:43:03.200 --> 00:43:06.319
The symbolism of this structure shaped

00:43:06.319 --> 00:43:09.119
like a mountain would likely have been

00:43:09.119 --> 00:43:13.520
obvious to the early medieval Javanese.

00:43:13.520 --> 00:43:16.240
The gods had once placed the mountains

00:43:16.240 --> 00:43:20.160
of Java to secure the island in place

00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:23.839
and bring stability to the land.

00:43:23.839 --> 00:43:27.119
Now their king did the same thing.

00:43:27.119 --> 00:43:29.119
placing his own mountain on the

00:43:29.119 --> 00:43:32.240
landscape to act as a testament to the

00:43:32.240 --> 00:43:36.079
lasting stability of his reign.

00:43:36.079 --> 00:43:40.960
And Bora Budor was built to last.

00:43:40.960 --> 00:43:43.359
It was constructed entirely without

00:43:43.359 --> 00:43:47.359
mortar or cement, carving its 2 million

00:43:47.359 --> 00:43:50.800
blocks of volcanic stone into intricate

00:43:50.800 --> 00:43:52.880
interlocking shapes to hold them

00:43:52.880 --> 00:43:54.480
together.

00:43:54.480 --> 00:43:56.560
This design has meant that it has

00:43:56.560 --> 00:43:58.640
largely survived the countless

00:43:58.640 --> 00:44:00.960
earthquakes that have taken place over

00:44:00.960 --> 00:44:03.119
the last millennium in one of the

00:44:03.119 --> 00:44:08.599
world's most seismically active zones,

00:44:08.640 --> 00:44:11.359
as well as the shifting ground beneath

00:44:11.359 --> 00:44:14.319
their feet. The builders also had the

00:44:14.319 --> 00:44:17.280
heavy rainfall of the Javanese monsoon

00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:20.800
to contend with. For this reason, they

00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:23.760
equipped the site of Bora Budur with

00:44:23.760 --> 00:44:27.520
more than 100 spouts for drainage, each

00:44:27.520 --> 00:44:30.720
carved in the shape of a giant or sea

00:44:30.720 --> 00:44:33.520
dragon, so that when it rained, water

00:44:33.520 --> 00:44:37.359
would have poured from their mouths.

00:44:37.359 --> 00:44:39.760
But the most remarkable and haunting

00:44:39.760 --> 00:44:42.319
feature of this monument is the

00:44:42.319 --> 00:44:45.680
thousands of reliefs carved all around

00:44:45.680 --> 00:44:49.000
its galleries.

00:44:54.880 --> 00:44:57.839
Many of these carvings show stories from

00:44:57.839 --> 00:45:00.560
the lives of the Buddha ascending

00:45:00.560 --> 00:45:03.520
through kilometers of galleries. And in

00:45:03.520 --> 00:45:06.400
this way, the monument is a story

00:45:06.400 --> 00:45:10.079
brought to life in stone.

00:45:10.079 --> 00:45:13.359
But alongside this religious narrative,

00:45:13.359 --> 00:45:16.800
others show scenes of simple daily life

00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:19.760
for all the different levels of Javanese

00:45:19.760 --> 00:45:22.000
society.

00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:24.480
In these carvings, we see people

00:45:24.480 --> 00:45:28.240
carrying woven baskets for winnowing and

00:45:28.240 --> 00:45:32.000
steaming rice and stirring milk rice in

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:35.200
pots. We see people working in the

00:45:35.200 --> 00:45:38.319
fields and shopping in a bustling urban

00:45:38.319 --> 00:45:40.160
marketplace.

00:45:40.160 --> 00:45:42.640
People carrying baskets of tropical

00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:46.160
fruit and nets full of fish. All of

00:45:46.160 --> 00:45:49.440
their faces looking out from the stone,

00:45:49.440 --> 00:45:52.880
frozen in a moment that passed by more

00:45:52.880 --> 00:45:56.800
than a thousand years ago.

00:45:56.800 --> 00:45:59.920
The Chinese history of Leyang describes

00:45:59.920 --> 00:46:02.400
the dress and appearance of the people

00:46:02.400 --> 00:46:06.160
of Java which can be seen in the reliefs

00:46:06.160 --> 00:46:10.040
of Boro Buddhur.

00:46:10.079 --> 00:46:11.839
Men and women have the upper part of the

00:46:11.839 --> 00:46:14.160
body naked. Their hair hangs loosely

00:46:14.160 --> 00:46:16.079
down and around their lower limbs they

00:46:16.079 --> 00:46:18.960
only use a sarong of cotton. The king

00:46:18.960 --> 00:46:21.040
and the nobles have a thin flowered

00:46:21.040 --> 00:46:22.800
cloth for covering the upper part of

00:46:22.800 --> 00:46:25.599
their body. They wear a girdle of gold

00:46:25.599 --> 00:46:28.800
and golden rings in their ears. Young

00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:30.560
girls cover themselves with a cloth of

00:46:30.560 --> 00:46:35.160
cotton and wear an embroidered girdle.

00:46:35.839 --> 00:46:38.640
In these carvings, we also get a sense

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:41.200
for courtly life.

00:46:41.200 --> 00:46:43.839
We see the king coming and going on his

00:46:43.839 --> 00:46:47.520
elephant, his courtiers and the palace

00:46:47.520 --> 00:46:49.839
women.

00:46:49.839 --> 00:46:52.240
In some carvings, we see the king and

00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:55.280
his nobles enjoying a splendid feast

00:46:55.280 --> 00:46:59.200
known as a mahammansa.

00:46:59.200 --> 00:47:03.119
One 12th century Javanese epic poem

00:47:03.119 --> 00:47:07.040
known as the bulman taka or death of

00:47:07.040 --> 00:47:10.400
Bulma describes the sumptuous sight of

00:47:10.400 --> 00:47:14.440
one of these feasts.

00:47:20.640 --> 00:47:24.000
The dishes were salted eggs, the pork

00:47:24.000 --> 00:47:27.520
neck cuts, ayong ayong and paban,

00:47:27.520 --> 00:47:30.000
vegetables in hot sauce, lickin and

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.720
chzecha, red mints of tripe with its

00:47:32.720 --> 00:47:35.440
various red salads and sizzling dripping

00:47:35.440 --> 00:47:37.359
of turtle

00:47:37.359 --> 00:47:39.920
and the boiled vegetables. Languban with

00:47:39.920 --> 00:47:42.640
marrow and tongue in rolls. Mushrooms

00:47:42.640 --> 00:47:45.119
steamed in leaves. Crisp flakes of

00:47:45.119 --> 00:47:48.000
jellyfish. Liver with rump accompanied

00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:50.640
by roasted lungs. Breast bone.

00:47:50.640 --> 00:47:53.920
Intestines on skewers with fat and hot

00:47:53.920 --> 00:47:55.680
kebabs.

00:47:55.680 --> 00:47:58.560
The banana heart was sweet. And there

00:47:58.560 --> 00:48:01.040
was no lack of prawns, crabs, salted

00:48:01.040 --> 00:48:04.079
fish, and muscles. Pickled meats,

00:48:04.079 --> 00:48:06.319
grilled meats, wuku, and various

00:48:06.319 --> 00:48:09.520
skewered meats, doves, puk birds, and

00:48:09.520 --> 00:48:12.480
wild pigeon made them clutch in all

00:48:12.480 --> 00:48:15.480
directions.

00:48:18.800 --> 00:48:22.200
ring aarab.

00:48:22.400 --> 00:48:25.760
>> Some of these 9th century carvings even

00:48:25.760 --> 00:48:29.040
depict recipes that are still enjoyed in

00:48:29.040 --> 00:48:32.559
Indonesia today. Among them, a dish

00:48:32.559 --> 00:48:36.160
called tonang, a tall cone of rice

00:48:36.160 --> 00:48:38.960
surrounded by side dishes which is still

00:48:38.960 --> 00:48:43.599
prepared for special occasions.

00:48:43.599 --> 00:48:46.079
But one particular feature of these

00:48:46.079 --> 00:48:48.480
carvings has always captured the

00:48:48.480 --> 00:48:50.800
imagination of those who visit the

00:48:50.800 --> 00:48:52.480
ruins.

00:48:52.480 --> 00:48:55.359
These are the so-called Boro Budor

00:48:55.359 --> 00:48:58.359
ships.

00:49:06.559 --> 00:49:09.680
In among the scenes of daily life are

00:49:09.680 --> 00:49:13.520
carved the shapes of five large seagoing

00:49:13.520 --> 00:49:17.280
vessels, graceful and high-sided, which

00:49:17.280 --> 00:49:20.000
show just how accomplished the Javanese

00:49:20.000 --> 00:49:25.920
had become as shipbuilders and sailors.

00:49:25.920 --> 00:49:28.319
And so it's no surprise that it was

00:49:28.319 --> 00:49:31.520
around this time that the people of Java

00:49:31.520 --> 00:49:34.079
began to gain a reputation around the

00:49:34.079 --> 00:49:39.880
world as traders and pirates.

00:49:41.359 --> 00:49:44.720
The Javanese of the Mataram period

00:49:44.720 --> 00:49:47.599
sailed in large ships that were often

00:49:47.599 --> 00:49:50.480
built from teik.

00:49:50.480 --> 00:49:53.280
This kind of wood was prized for its

00:49:53.280 --> 00:49:57.119
strength and its high oil content which

00:49:57.119 --> 00:49:59.920
gives it a natural water resistance even

00:49:59.920 --> 00:50:02.800
without varnishing and gives it a

00:50:02.800 --> 00:50:07.440
distinct rich aroma like fine leather.

00:50:07.440 --> 00:50:10.800
These ships were built without nails

00:50:10.800 --> 00:50:13.520
using only interlocking joints and

00:50:13.520 --> 00:50:16.640
wooden dowels and with ingenious

00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:19.920
arrangements of sails.

00:50:19.920 --> 00:50:23.839
The 3rd century Chinese writer Wan Chen

00:50:23.839 --> 00:50:28.079
in his work Nanju Yiu J or strange

00:50:28.079 --> 00:50:30.800
things of the southern lands describes

00:50:30.800 --> 00:50:36.200
the sight of these majestic vessels.

00:50:36.880 --> 00:50:40.559
The people sometimes rig as many as four

00:50:40.559 --> 00:50:43.920
sails which they carry in a row from bow

00:50:43.920 --> 00:50:47.599
to stern. The four sails do not face

00:50:47.599 --> 00:50:51.200
directly forward, but are set obliquely

00:50:51.200 --> 00:50:53.520
and so arranged that they can all be

00:50:53.520 --> 00:50:55.839
fixed in the same direction to receive

00:50:55.839 --> 00:50:59.119
the wind and to spill it. If it is

00:50:59.119 --> 00:51:02.480
violent, the sailors diminish or augment

00:51:02.480 --> 00:51:05.040
the surface of the sails according to

00:51:05.040 --> 00:51:08.559
the conditions. Thus these ships sail

00:51:08.559 --> 00:51:10.880
without avoiding strong winds and

00:51:10.880 --> 00:51:13.839
dashing waves by the aid of which they

00:51:13.839 --> 00:51:17.800
can make great speed.

00:51:18.079 --> 00:51:21.839
To Wan Chen and other Chinese writers,

00:51:21.839 --> 00:51:25.599
these Javanese ships were so remarkable

00:51:25.599 --> 00:51:28.559
because China itself would not develop

00:51:28.559 --> 00:51:31.680
large oceangoing vessels until around

00:51:31.680 --> 00:51:36.720
the 9th century or 600 years later.

00:51:36.720 --> 00:51:39.440
In fact, the Chinese held the ships of

00:51:39.440 --> 00:51:42.640
these islanders in such reverence that

00:51:42.640 --> 00:51:45.599
no foreign craft were permitted to sail

00:51:45.599 --> 00:51:48.319
within range of the main port of

00:51:48.319 --> 00:51:52.720
Guangong or Canton. As the 16th century

00:51:52.720 --> 00:51:58.520
Portuguese diplomat Tom Perez recounts,

00:51:59.920 --> 00:52:02.319
"They say that the Chinese made this law

00:52:02.319 --> 00:52:04.880
about not being able to go to Canton for

00:52:04.880 --> 00:52:07.839
fear of the Japanese and Malays, for it

00:52:07.839 --> 00:52:09.599
is certain that one of these people

00:52:09.599 --> 00:52:13.280
ships would route 20 Chinese ships. Such

00:52:13.280 --> 00:52:18.359
is their fear of Malays and Japanese."

00:52:20.160 --> 00:52:22.319
This fear appears to have been

00:52:22.319 --> 00:52:24.559
warranted.

00:52:24.559 --> 00:52:27.520
The inscriptions of the Cham people of

00:52:27.520 --> 00:52:31.200
Vietnam and the Camair in Cambodia

00:52:31.200 --> 00:52:34.000
frequently reference the arrival of

00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:37.119
fearsome seagoing raiders who are

00:52:37.119 --> 00:52:39.680
thought to have sailed from islands like

00:52:39.680 --> 00:52:43.280
Sumatra and Java.

00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:46.400
One inscription in the Po Nagar temple

00:52:46.400 --> 00:52:50.319
in Vietnam describes one such raid in

00:52:50.319 --> 00:52:54.040
the year 774.

00:52:55.680 --> 00:52:58.720
Ferocious, pitiles, dark-skinned men

00:52:58.720 --> 00:53:01.440
born in other countries whose food was

00:53:01.440 --> 00:53:04.000
more horrible than corpses and who were

00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:07.520
vicious and furious came in ships, took

00:53:07.520 --> 00:53:10.720
away the temple statue and set fire to

00:53:10.720 --> 00:53:13.960
the temple.

00:53:14.800 --> 00:53:18.319
The Javanese were in part able to become

00:53:18.319 --> 00:53:21.280
such successful sailors due to the

00:53:21.280 --> 00:53:24.160
extremely predictable wind patterns that

00:53:24.160 --> 00:53:28.480
take place in this part of the world.

00:53:28.480 --> 00:53:31.200
During the rainy season from December to

00:53:31.200 --> 00:53:34.559
March, the winds blow in over Java from

00:53:34.559 --> 00:53:37.680
the Asian mainland in the northwest,

00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:40.079
picking up moisture over the South China

00:53:40.079 --> 00:53:42.800
Sea and Pacific Ocean and bringing the

00:53:42.800 --> 00:53:44.640
monsoon.

00:53:44.640 --> 00:53:47.359
But during the dry season from April to

00:53:47.359 --> 00:53:50.800
September, the winds reverse direction

00:53:50.800 --> 00:53:53.280
and blow from the southeast and the

00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:57.119
deserts of Australia, bringing dry air

00:53:57.119 --> 00:54:01.200
and a lower probability of rain.

00:54:01.200 --> 00:54:03.200
This meant you could travel whichever

00:54:03.200 --> 00:54:05.680
direction you wanted so long as you

00:54:05.680 --> 00:54:10.760
wisely chose your season to sail.

00:54:12.160 --> 00:54:15.200
As their confidence grew on the waves,

00:54:15.200 --> 00:54:18.079
we have evidence that the Javanese also

00:54:18.079 --> 00:54:21.040
undertook some even more ambitious

00:54:21.040 --> 00:54:24.040
voyages.

00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:33.760
One Italian explorer who arrived in Java

00:54:33.760 --> 00:54:38.400
around 1505 named Ludovvic Deva of

00:54:38.400 --> 00:54:42.720
Bologna sailed to the island of Java and

00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:44.960
was amazed to see the captain of the

00:54:44.960 --> 00:54:48.400
ship navigate even when the North Star

00:54:48.400 --> 00:54:51.599
was no longer visible.

00:54:51.599 --> 00:54:53.200
When the chartered vessel was supplied

00:54:53.200 --> 00:54:55.280
with provisions, we took our way towards

00:54:55.280 --> 00:54:57.760
the beautiful island called Java at

00:54:57.760 --> 00:55:00.319
which we arrived in 5 days sailing

00:55:00.319 --> 00:55:02.640
towards the south. My companion asked

00:55:02.640 --> 00:55:04.240
the Christians, "Now that we have lost

00:55:04.240 --> 00:55:07.040
the North Star, how does he steer us? Is

00:55:07.040 --> 00:55:09.119
there any other North Star than this by

00:55:09.119 --> 00:55:11.359
which we steer?" The Christians asked

00:55:11.359 --> 00:55:13.119
the captain of the ship this same thing,

00:55:13.119 --> 00:55:15.520
and he showed us four or five stars,

00:55:15.520 --> 00:55:17.680
among which there was one which he said

00:55:17.680 --> 00:55:22.160
was the opposite to our north star.

00:55:22.160 --> 00:55:25.599
This was the socalled southern cross,

00:55:25.599 --> 00:55:28.319
the distinctive pattern of stars that

00:55:28.319 --> 00:55:30.800
could be seen in the southern hemisphere

00:55:30.800 --> 00:55:34.240
in the direction of the South Pole.

00:55:34.240 --> 00:55:36.960
The Europeans were amazed at this

00:55:36.960 --> 00:55:40.400
discovery. But the captain then told him

00:55:40.400 --> 00:55:43.040
that the Javanese had sailed into the

00:55:43.040 --> 00:55:46.079
south following these stars and had

00:55:46.079 --> 00:55:52.440
there come upon an icy and frozen land.

00:55:53.119 --> 00:55:55.359
He also told us that on the other side

00:55:55.359 --> 00:55:57.599
of the said island towards the south,

00:55:57.599 --> 00:55:59.520
there are some other races who navigate

00:55:59.520 --> 00:56:02.000
by the said four or five stars opposite

00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:05.200
to ours. And moreover, they gave us to

00:56:05.200 --> 00:56:07.280
understand that beyond the said island,

00:56:07.280 --> 00:56:09.760
the day does not last more than 4 hours,

00:56:09.760 --> 00:56:12.000
and that there it was colder than in any

00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:16.119
other part of the world.

00:56:16.640 --> 00:56:19.040
If this is true, it means that the

00:56:19.040 --> 00:56:22.079
Javanese had already sailed to and

00:56:22.079 --> 00:56:25.760
around Australia and set out into the

00:56:25.760 --> 00:56:28.640
Antarctic Ocean.

00:56:28.640 --> 00:56:32.000
But tantalizingly, we have only this

00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:35.520
secondhand story to go by, and the rest

00:56:35.520 --> 00:56:37.280
will have to be left to our

00:56:37.280 --> 00:56:40.280
imaginations.

00:56:40.559 --> 00:56:42.960
But as the centuries of the first

00:56:42.960 --> 00:56:45.520
millennium went on, there is a great

00:56:45.520 --> 00:56:47.839
deal more evidence that the people of

00:56:47.839 --> 00:56:50.960
Java were making their mark in even

00:56:50.960 --> 00:56:54.520
further lands.

00:56:59.040 --> 00:57:03.280
7,000 km away on the shores of East

00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:06.640
Africa, the 10th century Persian writer

00:57:06.640 --> 00:57:10.400
Bazour Iben Shari gives an account of a

00:57:10.400 --> 00:57:13.839
series of raids undertaken by a people

00:57:13.839 --> 00:57:17.520
from a faraway land that he calls the

00:57:17.520 --> 00:57:20.319
Wacwack.

00:57:20.319 --> 00:57:22.960
The Wacwack set out with a thousand

00:57:22.960 --> 00:57:26.160
ships to launch a determined attack upon

00:57:26.160 --> 00:57:28.720
the town of Kbala.

00:57:28.720 --> 00:57:31.520
But they were unable to capture it for

00:57:31.520 --> 00:57:34.640
the town was strongly fortified and was

00:57:34.640 --> 00:57:37.599
surrounded by an arm of the sea in the

00:57:37.599 --> 00:57:40.880
midst of which Kbarlo rose like a

00:57:40.880 --> 00:57:43.119
fortress.

00:57:43.119 --> 00:57:46.000
When the people of the African coast

00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:48.079
eventually came to terms with the

00:57:48.079 --> 00:57:51.119
attackers, they learned more about why

00:57:51.119 --> 00:57:54.400
they had come and how far they had

00:57:54.400 --> 00:57:56.960
traveled.

00:57:56.960 --> 00:57:59.520
The people of that country demanded why

00:57:59.520 --> 00:58:02.240
they had come to Gmbalo rather than to

00:58:02.240 --> 00:58:05.200
any other place. They replied that it

00:58:05.200 --> 00:58:06.960
was because the country possessed

00:58:06.960 --> 00:58:09.280
merchandise of value in the Wacwack

00:58:09.280 --> 00:58:12.480
country and in China such as ivory,

00:58:12.480 --> 00:58:14.880
tortoise shell, panther skins, and

00:58:14.880 --> 00:58:17.760
amberes. And also because they wanted to

00:58:17.760 --> 00:58:20.799
obtain some of the Zenge people who

00:58:20.799 --> 00:58:23.760
being strong men are able to stand heavy

00:58:23.760 --> 00:58:27.040
labor. Their voyage, they said, had

00:58:27.040 --> 00:58:29.680
lasted a year. If the story told by

00:58:29.680 --> 00:58:32.880
these people be true, this proves that

00:58:32.880 --> 00:58:35.520
the Wacwack Islands are situated

00:58:35.520 --> 00:58:39.240
opposite to China.

00:58:40.000 --> 00:58:43.200
The location of these Wacwack Islands

00:58:43.200 --> 00:58:45.760
has long been debated.

00:58:45.760 --> 00:58:48.559
One clue can be found in the Persian

00:58:48.559 --> 00:58:51.680
chronicler Iben Kodadbe, whose

00:58:51.680 --> 00:58:54.559
description has made many historians

00:58:54.559 --> 00:58:56.880
believe that they may have been the

00:58:56.880 --> 00:59:01.000
islands of Indonesia.

00:59:01.119 --> 00:59:03.520
East of China are the lands of Wacwack,

00:59:03.520 --> 00:59:05.359
which are so rich in gold that the

00:59:05.359 --> 00:59:06.960
inhabitants make the chains for their

00:59:06.960 --> 00:59:08.960
dogs and the collars for their monkeys

00:59:08.960 --> 00:59:12.160
of this metal. They manufacture tunics

00:59:12.160 --> 00:59:14.960
woven with gold. Excellent. Ebony wood

00:59:14.960 --> 00:59:17.760
is found there. Gold and ebony are

00:59:17.760 --> 00:59:21.640
exported from Wacwack.

00:59:23.200 --> 00:59:26.720
This detail of dogs wearing collars made

00:59:26.720 --> 00:59:29.760
of gold was also mentioned by early

00:59:29.760 --> 00:59:33.119
European explorers who visited Java,

00:59:33.119 --> 00:59:35.200
leading many to conclude that the

00:59:35.200 --> 00:59:39.960
Wacwack really were Javanese.

00:59:40.480 --> 00:59:43.280
If this story does relate an attack on

00:59:43.280 --> 00:59:46.319
eastern Africa by the people of Java,

00:59:46.319 --> 00:59:48.720
then it shows the extent of their ship

00:59:48.720 --> 00:59:52.240
building and seafaring prowess and that

00:59:52.240 --> 00:59:54.960
they have become a formidable threat for

00:59:54.960 --> 00:59:57.200
all the peoples who lived around the

00:59:57.200 --> 01:00:00.240
Indian Ocean.

01:00:00.240 --> 01:00:02.079
From these raids, they would have

01:00:02.079 --> 01:00:05.520
brought back gold, ivory, and slaves to

01:00:05.520 --> 01:00:07.040
Java.

01:00:07.040 --> 01:00:09.520
But in other places, they didn't simply

01:00:09.520 --> 01:00:13.799
raid and sail away.

01:00:19.040 --> 01:00:21.839
In the large island of Madagascar, just

01:00:21.839 --> 01:00:24.240
off the coast of Eastern Africa, the

01:00:24.240 --> 01:00:26.640
people's language has always puzzled

01:00:26.640 --> 01:00:29.040
linguists.

01:00:29.040 --> 01:00:32.000
The Madagascan language of Malagasi

01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:34.079
shares little in common with those of

01:00:34.079 --> 01:00:36.559
the African mainland. And it was only

01:00:36.559 --> 01:00:38.799
when the grammar and syntax were

01:00:38.799 --> 01:00:41.440
compared with Indonesian languages that

01:00:41.440 --> 01:00:45.359
a remarkable similarity was noticed.

01:00:45.359 --> 01:00:47.920
Although separated by the entire Indian

01:00:47.920 --> 01:00:51.359
Ocean, the language of Malagasi shares a

01:00:51.359 --> 01:00:53.440
grammatical structure with several

01:00:53.440 --> 01:00:56.880
Indonesian languages like Javanese. And

01:00:56.880 --> 01:00:58.720
they even have a number of different

01:00:58.720 --> 01:01:01.040
words in common.

01:01:01.040 --> 01:01:04.400
Just one example is the word for island,

01:01:04.400 --> 01:01:10.240
nosi in Malagasi and Nusa in Japanese.

01:01:10.240 --> 01:01:12.720
In fact, the closest living relative of

01:01:12.720 --> 01:01:15.440
Malagasi is thought to be a language

01:01:15.440 --> 01:01:18.160
called Manan, which originated on the

01:01:18.160 --> 01:01:21.040
south coast of Borneo.

01:01:21.040 --> 01:01:22.960
The most modern analysis of

01:01:22.960 --> 01:01:25.920
mitochondrial DNA in Madagascar has

01:01:25.920 --> 01:01:28.799
confirmed this connection and shows that

01:01:28.799 --> 01:01:31.280
the people there can trace their lineage

01:01:31.280 --> 01:01:34.480
back to about 30 mothers who arrived on

01:01:34.480 --> 01:01:39.040
the island from what is now Indonesia.

01:01:39.040 --> 01:01:41.599
This suggests a single boatload of

01:01:41.599 --> 01:01:44.240
settlers who had traveled across one of

01:01:44.240 --> 01:01:47.440
the world's widest oceans to find a new

01:01:47.440 --> 01:01:51.520
home. They also brought plants and crops

01:01:51.520 --> 01:01:53.520
with them.

01:01:53.520 --> 01:01:57.040
Botists estimate that a full 7% of the

01:01:57.040 --> 01:01:59.839
plant life on Madagascar today

01:01:59.839 --> 01:02:03.040
originated in Indonesia.

01:02:03.040 --> 01:02:06.319
These include bananas, plantains, taro,

01:02:06.319 --> 01:02:09.520
and yams. And all of these were already

01:02:09.520 --> 01:02:12.079
well established there by the medieval

01:02:12.079 --> 01:02:13.839
period.

01:02:13.839 --> 01:02:15.599
In602,

01:02:15.599 --> 01:02:19.760
another Portuguese explorer, Dio Duto,

01:02:19.760 --> 01:02:22.799
described these far-reaching journeys of

01:02:22.799 --> 01:02:26.000
the Javanese.

01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:28.079
The Javanese are all men very

01:02:28.079 --> 01:02:30.720
experienced in the art of navigation to

01:02:30.720 --> 01:02:32.559
the point that they claim to be the most

01:02:32.559 --> 01:02:35.359
ancient of all. It is certain that they

01:02:35.359 --> 01:02:37.599
formally navigated to Africa's Cape of

01:02:37.599 --> 01:02:40.160
Good Hope and were in communication with

01:02:40.160 --> 01:02:41.839
the east coast of the island of

01:02:41.839 --> 01:02:44.319
Madagascar where there are many brown

01:02:44.319 --> 01:02:47.520
and Javaneseike natives who say they are

01:02:47.520 --> 01:02:50.559
descended from them.

01:02:50.559 --> 01:02:53.200
The Javanese of this period navigated

01:02:53.200 --> 01:02:56.000
using the stars but also magnetic

01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:59.119
compasses and maps written on the bark

01:02:59.119 --> 01:03:03.480
of the paper Malbury tree.

01:03:04.480 --> 01:03:08.240
In 1512, only 20 years after Columbus

01:03:08.240 --> 01:03:11.119
had first reached the Americas and 12

01:03:11.119 --> 01:03:14.079
years after the first Europeans set foot

01:03:14.079 --> 01:03:17.440
in Brazil, a Portuguese concistador

01:03:17.440 --> 01:03:20.480
fighting on the Malay Peninsula captured

01:03:20.480 --> 01:03:24.799
a sea chart from a Javanese sailor. He

01:03:24.799 --> 01:03:27.440
was amazed to find that it had already

01:03:27.440 --> 01:03:29.599
been updated with all the new

01:03:29.599 --> 01:03:31.680
discoveries that had been made on the

01:03:31.680 --> 01:03:34.799
other side of the world. as he wrote in

01:03:34.799 --> 01:03:41.079
one letter to King Manuel I of Portugal.

01:03:41.760 --> 01:03:44.799
>> We found a large map of a Javanese pilot

01:03:44.799 --> 01:03:46.799
containing the Cape of Good Hope,

01:03:46.799 --> 01:03:50.160
Portugal and the land of Brazil, the Red

01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:52.720
Sea and the Sea of Persia, the Clove

01:03:52.720 --> 01:03:54.960
Islands, the navigation of the Chinese

01:03:54.960 --> 01:03:57.440
and Japanese, and how the kingdoms

01:03:57.440 --> 01:03:59.920
border on each other. It seems to me,

01:03:59.920 --> 01:04:02.000
sir, that this was the best thing I have

01:04:02.000 --> 01:04:04.240
ever seen. and your highness will be

01:04:04.240 --> 01:04:07.200
very pleased to see it.

01:04:07.200 --> 01:04:11.599
>> In 2003, a modern team was able to pilot

01:04:11.599 --> 01:04:14.559
a replica of an old Japanese sailing

01:04:14.559 --> 01:04:18.400
ship from Indonesia to Madagascar and

01:04:18.400 --> 01:04:21.200
around the Cape of Good Hope in South

01:04:21.200 --> 01:04:24.319
Africa. Thus proving that this journey

01:04:24.319 --> 01:04:26.720
was possible with the technology

01:04:26.720 --> 01:04:30.920
available at the time.

01:04:31.119 --> 01:04:33.760
But despite its remarkable achievements

01:04:33.760 --> 01:04:37.039
in architecture and its voyages of

01:04:37.039 --> 01:04:39.760
discovery, the Chileendra dynasty of

01:04:39.760 --> 01:04:43.440
Mataram would eventually decline and all

01:04:43.440 --> 01:04:46.079
of its grand monuments would decline

01:04:46.079 --> 01:04:49.400
with it.

01:04:56.720 --> 01:04:59.839
The reasons for the fall of Mataram are

01:04:59.839 --> 01:05:03.599
unclear since no true chronicles have

01:05:03.599 --> 01:05:06.480
survived from this time. But the

01:05:06.480 --> 01:05:09.119
kingdom's decline may have been related

01:05:09.119 --> 01:05:11.760
to a series of dramatic volcanic

01:05:11.760 --> 01:05:14.799
eruptions that occurred sometime in the

01:05:14.799 --> 01:05:19.799
10th and early 11th centuries.

01:05:21.039 --> 01:05:24.079
The people of Java have always lived

01:05:24.079 --> 01:05:27.200
with a particular paradox

01:05:27.200 --> 01:05:29.520
that the immense productivity of their

01:05:29.520 --> 01:05:32.559
land also comes from its most

01:05:32.559 --> 01:05:35.440
destructive force.

01:05:35.440 --> 01:05:37.680
Many landscapes that experience a

01:05:37.680 --> 01:05:40.880
monsoon season as heavy as Java can

01:05:40.880 --> 01:05:43.760
suffer from poor soil quality as the

01:05:43.760 --> 01:05:47.200
seasonal rains wash away top soil and

01:05:47.200 --> 01:05:50.640
leech nutrients away.

01:05:50.640 --> 01:05:53.760
But in much of Java, the hundreds of

01:05:53.760 --> 01:05:58.319
active volcanoes counteract this effect.

01:05:58.319 --> 01:06:01.039
Due to the island's particular geology,

01:06:01.039 --> 01:06:03.839
its volcanoes are especially beneficial

01:06:03.839 --> 01:06:06.400
for the soil, filling it with minerals

01:06:06.400 --> 01:06:08.799
like magnesium, potassium, and

01:06:08.799 --> 01:06:12.480
phosphorus that plants thrive on, all

01:06:12.480 --> 01:06:14.960
blasted out of the depths of the earth

01:06:14.960 --> 01:06:17.520
itself.

01:06:17.520 --> 01:06:20.720
Volcanic soil is also uniquely porous

01:06:20.720 --> 01:06:23.760
and retains moisture exceptionally well,

01:06:23.760 --> 01:06:26.720
while allowing air circulation for plant

01:06:26.720 --> 01:06:29.039
roots.

01:06:29.039 --> 01:06:32.480
But of course, a volcano is a violent

01:06:32.480 --> 01:06:34.559
phenomenon.

01:06:34.559 --> 01:06:37.280
When they erupt, they scorch the earth

01:06:37.280 --> 01:06:41.359
with pyrolastic flows, spew lava, and

01:06:41.359 --> 01:06:44.319
rain huge boulders down from the sky

01:06:44.319 --> 01:06:47.520
across a large area.

01:06:47.520 --> 01:06:51.200
This poses an obvious problem that the

01:06:51.200 --> 01:06:53.599
areas of the greatest agricultural

01:06:53.599 --> 01:06:56.640
productivity on the island were also the

01:06:56.640 --> 01:07:00.039
most dangerous.

01:07:01.760 --> 01:07:03.680
This meant that while the volcano's

01:07:03.680 --> 01:07:05.760
overall effect on the island was

01:07:05.760 --> 01:07:08.559
positive, a year in which a great

01:07:08.559 --> 01:07:11.599
eruption took place could wipe out a

01:07:11.599 --> 01:07:14.160
good proportion of any kingdom's food

01:07:14.160 --> 01:07:16.000
supplies.

01:07:16.000 --> 01:07:18.960
And of all these volcanoes, by far the

01:07:18.960 --> 01:07:21.200
most active was the one that the

01:07:21.200 --> 01:07:24.559
Javanese call by a name which means the

01:07:24.559 --> 01:07:30.520
mountain of fire or merap.

01:07:39.039 --> 01:07:43.680
Rising to nearly 3,000 m or 10,000 ft.

01:07:43.680 --> 01:07:46.400
Mount Marappi is the most active volcano

01:07:46.400 --> 01:07:49.200
in the whole of Indonesia and is

01:07:49.200 --> 01:07:51.039
considered one of the most active and

01:07:51.039 --> 01:07:53.599
dangerous in the world.

01:07:53.599 --> 01:07:55.599
It has erupted regularly for at least

01:07:55.599 --> 01:07:59.119
the last 500 years with small eruptions

01:07:59.119 --> 01:08:02.400
occurring every 2 to 3 years and larger

01:08:02.400 --> 01:08:05.760
ones every 10 to 15.

01:08:05.760 --> 01:08:08.720
Then every few hundred years the

01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:11.119
mountain explodes in a truly

01:08:11.119 --> 01:08:14.799
catastrophic fashion.

01:08:16.080 --> 01:08:19.279
The Javanese Chronicle, the Babad Tan

01:08:19.279 --> 01:08:22.799
Jawi, records the devastation caused by

01:08:22.799 --> 01:08:26.080
one eruption of the great Mount Marappi

01:08:26.080 --> 01:08:30.880
that took place in the 16th century.

01:08:30.880 --> 01:08:34.880
Then Mount Marappi erupted with fire. It

01:08:34.880 --> 01:08:37.759
made a terrifying thundering noise. A

01:08:37.759 --> 01:08:41.199
rain of ash fell. A volcanic mud flow

01:08:41.199 --> 01:08:45.359
ran down the OAC river. Big rocks rose

01:08:45.359 --> 01:08:48.960
from the flow and landed on the land.

01:08:48.960 --> 01:08:52.400
When the piles of wood on the Ganang GD

01:08:52.400 --> 01:08:54.719
mountains were set on fire, the

01:08:54.719 --> 01:08:57.759
mountains became a blaze of fire. The

01:08:57.759 --> 01:09:02.640
Gong Ki Bichchuk was beaten ceaselessly.

01:09:02.640 --> 01:09:05.359
All tried to save their lives and ran in

01:09:05.359 --> 01:09:08.759
all directions.

01:09:09.359 --> 01:09:11.520
Added to this obvious physical

01:09:11.520 --> 01:09:14.560
destruction, the Javanese also held the

01:09:14.560 --> 01:09:18.080
volcanoes in great spiritual reverence

01:09:18.080 --> 01:09:21.199
and viewed eruptions as signs and

01:09:21.199 --> 01:09:24.319
portants from the gods.

01:09:24.319 --> 01:09:26.960
After the deaths of great kings,

01:09:26.960 --> 01:09:29.440
Javanese chronicles often describe the

01:09:29.440 --> 01:09:33.839
mountains rumbling in mourning.

01:09:33.839 --> 01:09:36.640
At the death of his majesty, the wailing

01:09:36.640 --> 01:09:40.000
in the palace was as loud as thunder.

01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:42.480
Mount Marappi rumbled,

01:09:42.480 --> 01:09:44.239
joining in with the sound of a

01:09:44.239 --> 01:09:47.239
rainstorm.

01:09:48.080 --> 01:09:50.719
It was believed that the eruptions,

01:09:50.719 --> 01:09:53.120
earthquakes, and various rumblings of

01:09:53.120 --> 01:09:56.480
the land were not just seismic events,

01:09:56.480 --> 01:09:59.360
but actually one of the primary ways

01:09:59.360 --> 01:10:02.159
that the gods weighed in on the affairs

01:10:02.159 --> 01:10:04.080
of humanity.

01:10:04.080 --> 01:10:06.400
For this reason, their timing could have

01:10:06.400 --> 01:10:10.719
real life or death consequences.

01:10:10.719 --> 01:10:13.840
One chronicle recounts the story of a

01:10:13.840 --> 01:10:17.760
lucky prisoner held by a 17th century

01:10:17.760 --> 01:10:21.120
Javanese king.

01:10:21.120 --> 01:10:23.040
The king wanted to kill the prisoner

01:10:23.040 --> 01:10:26.560
Raden Masuya Kasuma. But this did not

01:10:26.560 --> 01:10:28.800
happen because every time they wanted to

01:10:28.800 --> 01:10:31.679
kill him, Mount Marrapy flared up with a

01:10:31.679 --> 01:10:34.960
terrifying noise. In the end, the man

01:10:34.960 --> 01:10:38.000
was set free and promoted and given the

01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:43.080
lordship of 1,000 rice fields.

01:10:47.760 --> 01:10:50.159
A particularly devastating eruption

01:10:50.159 --> 01:10:52.719
would not only cause immense economic

01:10:52.719 --> 01:10:55.280
damage to the kingdom, it could also be

01:10:55.280 --> 01:10:58.239
considered a clear sign that the gods

01:10:58.239 --> 01:11:01.520
were angry with the current ruler. For

01:11:01.520 --> 01:11:04.400
any king who didn't have a firm grasp on

01:11:04.400 --> 01:11:08.800
power, this could be a devastating blow.

01:11:08.800 --> 01:11:12.560
From some inscriptions left in Java, we

01:11:12.560 --> 01:11:15.120
know that as the 9th century came to an

01:11:15.120 --> 01:11:18.239
end, the kingdom of Mataram descended

01:11:18.239 --> 01:11:22.080
into civil war with three kings ruling

01:11:22.080 --> 01:11:26.199
in only two years.

01:11:26.239 --> 01:11:28.560
When the dust of this civil war settled

01:11:28.560 --> 01:11:30.960
in the year 929,

01:11:30.960 --> 01:11:34.560
a king named Rakhino Pusindok took to

01:11:34.560 --> 01:11:38.560
the throne. But curiously, it seems the

01:11:38.560 --> 01:11:41.600
kingdom of Mataram had by this point

01:11:41.600 --> 01:11:43.840
moved.

01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:46.000
All of the inscriptions issued by this

01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:49.520
king would be written in East Java, far

01:11:49.520 --> 01:11:52.239
away from its original heartlands around

01:11:52.239 --> 01:11:55.920
the volcano Mount Marappi.

01:11:55.920 --> 01:11:57.840
It seems that around the beginning of

01:11:57.840 --> 01:12:00.800
the 10th century, the entire Mataram

01:12:00.800 --> 01:12:04.480
Kingdom simply upped sticks and fled its

01:12:04.480 --> 01:12:07.760
original wealthy province, leaving its

01:12:07.760 --> 01:12:12.080
towering temples and cities abandoned.

01:12:12.080 --> 01:12:15.040
And what's perhaps most significant is

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:17.760
that no other power seems to have swept

01:12:17.760 --> 01:12:21.199
in to the empty lands. This suggests

01:12:21.199 --> 01:12:23.840
that some kind of cataclysm took place

01:12:23.840 --> 01:12:26.480
there.

01:12:32.320 --> 01:12:34.719
Archaeological evidence shows that the

01:12:34.719 --> 01:12:37.199
early 10th century layer of human

01:12:37.199 --> 01:12:40.080
occupation at the great temple of Boro

01:12:40.080 --> 01:12:43.199
Budor, for instance, is sealed by up to

01:12:43.199 --> 01:12:46.800
half a meter of volcanic ash, suggesting

01:12:46.800 --> 01:12:49.360
a major eruption.

01:12:49.360 --> 01:12:52.080
The peoples of this land were no

01:12:52.080 --> 01:12:55.600
strangers to erupting volcanoes.

01:12:55.600 --> 01:12:57.360
So we can imagine that it must have

01:12:57.360 --> 01:13:01.280
taken one of particular violence or a

01:13:01.280 --> 01:13:03.920
series of eruptions taking place in

01:13:03.920 --> 01:13:06.880
frighteningly quick succession to cause

01:13:06.880 --> 01:13:09.360
the wholesale abandonment of this

01:13:09.360 --> 01:13:12.960
kingdom and its reestablishment hundreds

01:13:12.960 --> 01:13:17.040
of kilometers to the east.

01:13:17.040 --> 01:13:20.400
One inscription known as the Puchangan

01:13:20.400 --> 01:13:23.840
stone describes a kind of disaster

01:13:23.840 --> 01:13:27.640
sweeping the land.

01:13:28.239 --> 01:13:30.000
In the time of the great catastrophe

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.560
that overwhelmed the island of Java in

01:13:32.560 --> 01:13:36.880
the Saka year 928 when King Warari came

01:13:36.880 --> 01:13:39.760
forth from Waram, the whole of Java

01:13:39.760 --> 01:13:42.000
seemed transformed into a single raging

01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:43.360
sea.

01:13:43.360 --> 01:13:45.360
Many of the foremost men of the realm

01:13:45.360 --> 01:13:48.480
perished. Chief among the dead was the

01:13:48.480 --> 01:13:51.960
divine king.

01:13:52.400 --> 01:13:55.199
Unfortunately, the exact dating of

01:13:55.199 --> 01:13:58.000
volcanic eruptions is difficult, and

01:13:58.000 --> 01:14:00.080
it's hard to say whether this was truly

01:14:00.080 --> 01:14:04.000
the cause of Mataram's downfall.

01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:07.440
But whether from volcanic causes or not,

01:14:07.440 --> 01:14:09.440
it's clear that for one reason or

01:14:09.440 --> 01:14:12.640
another, life had become unlivable for

01:14:12.640 --> 01:14:18.199
the people of Matarang in central Java.

01:14:18.320 --> 01:14:20.640
The kingdom eventually reached a level

01:14:20.640 --> 01:14:23.760
of stability in its new home in East

01:14:23.760 --> 01:14:26.880
Java, away from the destruction it had

01:14:26.880 --> 01:14:28.400
faced.

01:14:28.400 --> 01:14:31.600
But its confidence in itself and in the

01:14:31.600 --> 01:14:34.400
god's approval of its rulers had been

01:14:34.400 --> 01:14:36.960
fatally reduced.

01:14:36.960 --> 01:14:40.239
Within a century, the remains of Martam

01:14:40.239 --> 01:14:43.440
was facing destruction, now at the hands

01:14:43.440 --> 01:14:46.239
of human enemies.

01:14:46.239 --> 01:14:49.120
An invasion by a neighboring king wiped

01:14:49.120 --> 01:14:52.080
out what was left of it, and the kingdom

01:14:52.080 --> 01:14:54.800
of Mataram disappeared,

01:14:54.800 --> 01:14:57.840
living on only in the stone carvings

01:14:57.840 --> 01:15:00.320
left lining the walls of its great

01:15:00.320 --> 01:15:03.520
temples. Thousands of moments of

01:15:03.520 --> 01:15:07.280
everyday life now sealed beneath a thick

01:15:07.280 --> 01:15:12.199
layer of volcanic ash.

01:15:18.719 --> 01:15:22.159
After the fall of Mataram, a number of

01:15:22.159 --> 01:15:26.560
successor kingdoms would rise up.

01:15:26.560 --> 01:15:29.679
In the 11th century, much of Java was

01:15:29.679 --> 01:15:32.719
reunited again under the rule of a king

01:15:32.719 --> 01:15:36.560
named Ayalanga, whose name meant he who

01:15:36.560 --> 01:15:39.520
leapt over the water.

01:15:39.520 --> 01:15:43.120
He was born on the small island of Bali

01:15:43.120 --> 01:15:46.239
and crossed the sea to Java as a young

01:15:46.239 --> 01:15:48.159
man.

01:15:48.159 --> 01:15:51.199
The Puchangan stone describes how this

01:15:51.199 --> 01:15:53.679
king was spared from the destruction

01:15:53.679 --> 01:15:56.640
that swept the land during the fall of

01:15:56.640 --> 01:15:59.640
Mataram.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:02.320
>> At that time, his majesty was only 16

01:16:02.320 --> 01:16:04.719
years old, still too young to have

01:16:04.719 --> 01:16:07.360
mastered the art of war. Yet because he

01:16:07.360 --> 01:16:09.840
was the very manifestation of Vishnu,

01:16:09.840 --> 01:16:11.760
all the gods protected him from being

01:16:11.760 --> 01:16:16.120
swept away by the great destruction.

01:16:16.640 --> 01:16:19.440
Arlanga would rule successfully for

01:16:19.440 --> 01:16:22.640
several decades. But when he died, the

01:16:22.640 --> 01:16:25.440
land divided again.

01:16:25.440 --> 01:16:27.679
The kingdom that would truly give birth

01:16:27.679 --> 01:16:31.040
to Java's golden era was named

01:16:31.040 --> 01:16:33.840
Singasari.

01:16:33.840 --> 01:16:36.640
Singari derived its name from the

01:16:36.640 --> 01:16:40.800
Sanskrit word simha meaning lion. And

01:16:40.800 --> 01:16:44.400
this lion kingdom was founded by a king

01:16:44.400 --> 01:16:48.600
named Ken Angro.

01:16:53.360 --> 01:16:57.040
Ken Angro's name means the man who

01:16:57.040 --> 01:17:00.320
overturned everything. and he was a

01:17:00.320 --> 01:17:04.719
revolutionary force on Java.

01:17:04.719 --> 01:17:07.440
In the centuries since he lived, the

01:17:07.440 --> 01:17:11.360
legend of Ken Angro has grown to mythic

01:17:11.360 --> 01:17:14.960
proportions and he has inspired theater,

01:17:14.960 --> 01:17:19.760
song and poetry in Indonesia.

01:17:19.760 --> 01:17:23.360
The story of his life is largely told in

01:17:23.360 --> 01:17:26.960
a fragmentaryary chronicle known as the

01:17:26.960 --> 01:17:28.560
Paraton

01:17:28.560 --> 01:17:31.920
or the book of kings written sometime

01:17:31.920 --> 01:17:36.320
later in the 16th century.

01:17:36.320 --> 01:17:39.840
According to this chronicle, Ken Angraok

01:17:39.840 --> 01:17:42.800
was actually the son of the Hindu god

01:17:42.800 --> 01:17:46.239
Brahma who appeared to his mother, a

01:17:46.239 --> 01:17:49.840
poor woman named Ken Endok, and informed

01:17:49.840 --> 01:17:54.840
her of her immaculate conception.

01:18:00.239 --> 01:18:03.760
The god Brahma descended there and lay

01:18:03.760 --> 01:18:06.080
with Ken Endoc.

01:18:06.080 --> 01:18:08.320
This meeting took place in the fields of

01:18:08.320 --> 01:18:11.520
Lalaten. The god made a vow with the

01:18:11.520 --> 01:18:15.040
woman. You must not go to your husband

01:18:15.040 --> 01:18:19.120
again. If you lie with him, he will die

01:18:19.120 --> 01:18:22.400
and my child will be corrupted. That

01:18:22.400 --> 01:18:26.320
child is named Ken Anbrook and he will

01:18:26.320 --> 01:18:29.600
one day rule the land of Java. With

01:18:29.600 --> 01:18:34.199
that, Brahma vanished.

01:18:39.120 --> 01:18:43.440
The woman held true to her word and soon

01:18:43.440 --> 01:18:47.040
Ken Angro was born.

01:18:47.040 --> 01:18:50.480
But the family was extremely poor and

01:18:50.480 --> 01:18:54.000
couldn't provide for the little boy.

01:18:54.000 --> 01:18:57.199
His parents abandoned him in a grave.

01:18:57.199 --> 01:19:00.400
But he was found by a common thief named

01:19:00.400 --> 01:19:03.679
Lemong who was perhaps plundering the

01:19:03.679 --> 01:19:07.880
graveyard for valuables.

01:19:12.159 --> 01:19:15.600
When her time was full, she gave birth

01:19:15.600 --> 01:19:20.000
to a boy. Ken Endok abandoned him in a

01:19:20.000 --> 01:19:22.800
burial ground for children. Not long

01:19:22.800 --> 01:19:26.080
after, a thief named Len Bong wandered

01:19:26.080 --> 01:19:28.960
into the same place. There he saw

01:19:28.960 --> 01:19:32.239
something glowing. Drawn to it, he heard

01:19:32.239 --> 01:19:35.440
the sound of a child crying. When he

01:19:35.440 --> 01:19:38.400
came closer, he saw that the light was

01:19:38.400 --> 01:19:41.760
coming from the child himself. Lemong

01:19:41.760 --> 01:19:44.880
picked him up, carried him home, and

01:19:44.880 --> 01:19:49.159
raised him as his own son.

01:19:55.520 --> 01:19:58.880
Brought up by this thief, Ken Angro

01:19:58.880 --> 01:20:02.239
would learn all the tricks of his trade

01:20:02.239 --> 01:20:04.880
until he was the most accomplished thief

01:20:04.880 --> 01:20:08.080
in Java.

01:20:08.080 --> 01:20:11.440
But one day he met an Indian holy man

01:20:11.440 --> 01:20:15.440
who identified him as the son of Brahma

01:20:15.440 --> 01:20:20.480
and an embodiment of the god Vishnu.

01:20:20.480 --> 01:20:24.000
This holy man convinced Ken Angro to

01:20:24.000 --> 01:20:27.360
give up his sinful life.

01:20:27.360 --> 01:20:31.120
As a reward, Ken Angro gained a magical

01:20:31.120 --> 01:20:35.360
weapon, a kind of Javanese knife known

01:20:35.360 --> 01:20:38.320
as ais.

01:20:38.320 --> 01:20:41.360
These are long daggers often created

01:20:41.360 --> 01:20:44.719
with a distinctive rippled blade and

01:20:44.719 --> 01:20:47.920
they were worn by Javanese men as a sign

01:20:47.920 --> 01:20:51.440
of status as a talisman against various

01:20:51.440 --> 01:20:54.719
evils and of course as a practical

01:20:54.719 --> 01:20:58.080
sidearm for self-defense.

01:20:58.080 --> 01:21:00.640
One Chinese visitor to Java at the start

01:21:00.640 --> 01:21:04.719
of the 15th century named Mahuan writes

01:21:04.719 --> 01:21:09.560
about the importance of these blades.

01:21:09.920 --> 01:21:12.719
From little boys of 3 years to old men

01:21:12.719 --> 01:21:15.920
of a hundred years, they all have these

01:21:15.920 --> 01:21:18.960
knives which are all made of steel with

01:21:18.960 --> 01:21:21.440
most intricate patterns drawn in very

01:21:21.440 --> 01:21:24.400
delicate lines. For the handles, they

01:21:24.400 --> 01:21:26.880
use gold or rhinoceros horn or

01:21:26.880 --> 01:21:28.960
elephant's teeth engraved with

01:21:28.960 --> 01:21:31.360
representations of human forms or

01:21:31.360 --> 01:21:34.320
devil's faces. The craftsmanship being

01:21:34.320 --> 01:21:38.440
very fine and skillful.

01:21:40.480 --> 01:21:43.760
With this magical sword by his side, Ken

01:21:43.760 --> 01:21:47.360
Angro rose to prominence in Java and

01:21:47.360 --> 01:21:49.520
eventually through the overwhelming

01:21:49.520 --> 01:21:53.199
force of his various virtues became its

01:21:53.199 --> 01:21:58.920
king as the paraton describes.

01:22:03.520 --> 01:22:07.040
Not long afterwards, Ken Anro was

01:22:07.040 --> 01:22:11.360
acclaimed as king of Tamapel. His realm

01:22:11.360 --> 01:22:13.920
was called Singasari.

01:22:13.920 --> 01:22:16.239
His enthronement was witnessed by

01:22:16.239 --> 01:22:18.960
learned men of both the Shyite and

01:22:18.960 --> 01:22:22.000
Buddhist traditions of Keri.

01:22:22.000 --> 01:22:24.800
Those who had once shown Ken Angarok

01:22:24.800 --> 01:22:27.520
kindness in his days of hardship were

01:22:27.520 --> 01:22:30.000
summoned, granted protection, and

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:34.600
generously rewarded for their loyalty.

01:22:35.440 --> 01:22:38.440
Bilazani.

01:22:38.560 --> 01:22:41.520
>> Not everyone easily accepted the rule of

01:22:41.520 --> 01:22:43.840
this commoner.

01:22:43.840 --> 01:22:47.840
In the nearby rival kingdom of Kediri,

01:22:47.840 --> 01:22:51.520
the king was named Dandang Gendis and he

01:22:51.520 --> 01:22:57.199
refused to accept Ken Angro as his king.

01:22:57.199 --> 01:23:00.239
Dandang Gendis gathered his armies and

01:23:00.239 --> 01:23:03.600
marched to fight Ken Angro.

01:23:03.600 --> 01:23:06.800
But he was no match for the divine power

01:23:06.800 --> 01:23:11.320
of the God made man.

01:23:15.199 --> 01:23:17.840
>> He fell because he was attacked on all

01:23:17.840 --> 01:23:21.199
sides by the forces of Singasari who

01:23:21.199 --> 01:23:23.679
came on like a flood pouring down from

01:23:23.679 --> 01:23:26.639
the mountains. The army of Keri

01:23:26.639 --> 01:23:29.600
scattered like a swarm of bees, fleeing

01:23:29.600 --> 01:23:32.719
in panic, abandoning the field like

01:23:32.719 --> 01:23:35.600
startled goats, casting aside their

01:23:35.600 --> 01:23:37.120
parasolles.

01:23:37.120 --> 01:23:40.880
King Dandang Dendis withdrew from the

01:23:40.880 --> 01:23:42.719
battle and fled into the realm of the

01:23:42.719 --> 01:23:45.600
gods, rising up into the air with his

01:23:45.600 --> 01:23:49.199
horse, his grooms, his parasolbearers,

01:23:49.199 --> 01:23:51.040
and those who carried his drinking

01:23:51.040 --> 01:23:54.000
vessels and his mats. All of them

01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:57.760
ascending into the sky. Thus, Kendiri

01:23:57.760 --> 01:24:03.239
was utterly defeated by Ken Angbrook.

01:24:14.320 --> 01:24:17.280
Needless to say, this section of the

01:24:17.280 --> 01:24:20.159
Paraton Chronicle is considered to be

01:24:20.159 --> 01:24:23.040
largely mythical and reflects the

01:24:23.040 --> 01:24:28.400
propaganda of this king's new regime.

01:24:28.400 --> 01:24:31.199
But this story would be repeated across

01:24:31.199 --> 01:24:34.400
the towns and villages of Java by

01:24:34.400 --> 01:24:38.480
trained storytellers who together wo a

01:24:38.480 --> 01:24:41.760
new national myth around the figure of

01:24:41.760 --> 01:24:44.639
Ken Angro.

01:24:44.639 --> 01:24:47.520
One of the most important mediums in

01:24:47.520 --> 01:24:50.880
which this story was told was that of

01:24:50.880 --> 01:24:55.639
the Javanese shadow puppets.

01:24:59.440 --> 01:25:02.719
The exact origin of Javanese shadow

01:25:02.719 --> 01:25:05.840
puppetry is a mystery, but it's clear

01:25:05.840 --> 01:25:09.280
from a number of oblique references in

01:25:09.280 --> 01:25:11.760
Javanese literature that it was already

01:25:11.760 --> 01:25:14.480
a wellestablished practice by at least

01:25:14.480 --> 01:25:16.800
the 10th century.

01:25:16.800 --> 01:25:20.239
This form of shadow theater is known as

01:25:20.239 --> 01:25:22.560
Wyang.

01:25:22.560 --> 01:25:26.800
Wang in Javanese means shadow or ghost,

01:25:26.800 --> 01:25:29.920
but it can also mean imagination.

01:25:29.920 --> 01:25:32.639
And these plays would retell stories

01:25:32.639 --> 01:25:36.560
from the Hindu epics like the Mahabarat,

01:25:36.560 --> 01:25:40.320
local Javanese stories such as how rice

01:25:40.320 --> 01:25:43.280
came to the earth and the stories of

01:25:43.280 --> 01:25:47.480
their kings and ancestors.

01:25:47.920 --> 01:25:50.639
The Chinese visitor to Java at the

01:25:50.639 --> 01:25:53.679
beginning of the 15th century, Marwan,

01:25:53.679 --> 01:25:58.679
describes witnessing these performances.

01:25:59.440 --> 01:26:01.600
Each time the performer unrolls and

01:26:01.600 --> 01:26:03.840
exposes a section of the picture, he

01:26:03.840 --> 01:26:06.080
thrusts it forward toward the audience

01:26:06.080 --> 01:26:07.920
and speaking with a loud voice in the

01:26:07.920 --> 01:26:10.080
foreign language, he explains the

01:26:10.080 --> 01:26:12.960
derivation of this section. The crowd

01:26:12.960 --> 01:26:14.719
sits around and listens to him,

01:26:14.719 --> 01:26:17.520
sometimes laughing, sometimes crying,

01:26:17.520 --> 01:26:19.679
exactly as if the narrator were reciting

01:26:19.679 --> 01:26:23.639
one of our popular romances.

01:26:24.239 --> 01:26:27.360
These shadow plays would typically start

01:26:27.360 --> 01:26:31.199
at nightfall and go on until dawn and

01:26:31.199 --> 01:26:33.679
would be conducted behind a screen of

01:26:33.679 --> 01:26:36.960
white cotton fabric using a lamp burning

01:26:36.960 --> 01:26:40.800
with coconut oil, usually cast in metal

01:26:40.800 --> 01:26:44.719
in the form of the sacred bird Gauda.

01:26:44.719 --> 01:26:47.520
The puppets were typically made of goat

01:26:47.520 --> 01:26:51.520
hide or buffalo skin mounted on bamboo

01:26:51.520 --> 01:26:54.639
canes and placed in a trunk of banana

01:26:54.639 --> 01:26:58.320
palm lying behind the screen.

01:26:58.320 --> 01:27:01.280
The puppets had jointed limbs and were

01:27:01.280 --> 01:27:03.360
punctured all over with intricate

01:27:03.360 --> 01:27:06.239
patterns of holes that allowed the light

01:27:06.239 --> 01:27:09.280
through so that their shadows could then

01:27:09.280 --> 01:27:12.719
be cast onto a screen.

01:27:12.719 --> 01:27:14.960
These puppet shows were often

01:27:14.960 --> 01:27:17.520
accompanied by music.

01:27:17.520 --> 01:27:20.239
>> In small village performances, this

01:27:20.239 --> 01:27:22.080
could simply be the drumming of the

01:27:22.080 --> 01:27:24.480
puppeteer on the box where the puppets

01:27:24.480 --> 01:27:26.239
were kept.

01:27:26.239 --> 01:27:28.639
But in the royal court, a puppeteer

01:27:28.639 --> 01:27:31.440
would perform alongside a full orchestra

01:27:31.440 --> 01:27:35.760
of musicians known as a gamalan with a

01:27:35.760 --> 01:27:40.480
whole host of 15 instruments.

01:27:40.480 --> 01:27:43.600
These night-long plays would unfold

01:27:43.600 --> 01:27:46.719
according to strict traditions.

01:27:46.719 --> 01:27:49.040
In the hours between sunset and

01:27:49.040 --> 01:27:51.600
midnight, the puppeteer introduced the

01:27:51.600 --> 01:27:55.040
characters and set up the conflict. And

01:27:55.040 --> 01:27:57.440
then at the stroke of midnight, the

01:27:57.440 --> 01:28:00.639
drama burst out into a frenzied clash

01:28:00.639 --> 01:28:03.520
between good and evil.

01:28:03.520 --> 01:28:06.320
The Portuguese traveler and apothecary

01:28:06.320 --> 01:28:09.840
Tomé Perez, who visited Java around

01:28:09.840 --> 01:28:11.440
1513,

01:28:11.440 --> 01:28:13.760
wrote about seeing these forms of

01:28:13.760 --> 01:28:18.400
theater and shadow puppetry.

01:28:18.400 --> 01:28:21.360
The land of Java is a land of performers

01:28:21.360 --> 01:28:24.560
and masks of various Japanese kinds, and

01:28:24.560 --> 01:28:27.920
both men and women do thus. They have

01:28:27.920 --> 01:28:30.960
entertainments of dancing and stories.

01:28:30.960 --> 01:28:33.679
They mime. They wear actors dresses and

01:28:33.679 --> 01:28:36.239
all their clothes. They are certainly

01:28:36.239 --> 01:28:39.520
graceful. They have music of bells. The

01:28:39.520 --> 01:28:41.600
sound of all of them playing together is

01:28:41.600 --> 01:28:44.639
like an organ. These actors show a

01:28:44.639 --> 01:28:47.199
thousand graces like these by day and

01:28:47.199 --> 01:28:50.480
night. At night, they make shadows of

01:28:50.480 --> 01:28:53.760
various shapes.

01:28:53.760 --> 01:28:56.239
Over time, the performance of these

01:28:56.239 --> 01:28:59.199
shadow plays took on a spiritual

01:28:59.199 --> 01:29:01.280
meaning.

01:29:01.280 --> 01:29:04.480
The puppeteer or dalang was thought to

01:29:04.480 --> 01:29:06.639
become possessed by the power of the

01:29:06.639 --> 01:29:09.280
gods as he worked. And in the

01:29:09.280 --> 01:29:12.000
performance all the holy elements were

01:29:12.000 --> 01:29:13.600
represented.

01:29:13.600 --> 01:29:16.560
The banana palm representing the earth,

01:29:16.560 --> 01:29:19.679
the cloth screen, the sky, the fire in

01:29:19.679 --> 01:29:22.800
the coconut oil lamp, and of course, the

01:29:22.800 --> 01:29:25.840
interplay of light and darkness, good

01:29:25.840 --> 01:29:28.880
and evil, as the stories of gods and

01:29:28.880 --> 01:29:34.199
demons played out across the screen.

01:29:34.400 --> 01:29:36.480
These performances were considered to

01:29:36.480 --> 01:29:39.920
have real power. Some such as the

01:29:39.920 --> 01:29:43.040
Bratayuta or a Javanese version of the

01:29:43.040 --> 01:29:45.679
Indian epic the Mahabarat were

01:29:45.679 --> 01:29:48.719
considered too potent to ever perform in

01:29:48.719 --> 01:29:52.000
their entirety. As Thomas Stamford

01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:55.800
Raffles records,

01:29:56.080 --> 01:29:58.320
although the Wyang may represent any

01:29:58.320 --> 01:30:00.719
portion of the Bratuda, there is a

01:30:00.719 --> 01:30:03.120
prevalent superstition that a great war

01:30:03.120 --> 01:30:05.120
will be the inevitable consequence of

01:30:05.120 --> 01:30:07.760
performing at one sitting the whole of

01:30:07.760 --> 01:30:10.880
this poem. It is gravely asserted that a

01:30:10.880 --> 01:30:13.199
chief of Kendall tried this experiment

01:30:13.199 --> 01:30:15.120
about 50 years ago, but that the

01:30:15.120 --> 01:30:17.440
performance was no sooner completed than

01:30:17.440 --> 01:30:19.600
his country was laid to waste and

01:30:19.600 --> 01:30:22.600
destroyed.

01:30:23.440 --> 01:30:25.840
Other of these shadow plays were

01:30:25.840 --> 01:30:28.800
performed at auspicious times in order

01:30:28.800 --> 01:30:31.679
to bring about certain effects with

01:30:31.679 --> 01:30:34.960
stories of the goddess of rice told

01:30:34.960 --> 01:30:38.320
during the harvests and the great myths

01:30:38.320 --> 01:30:42.960
told during times of trouble and strife.

01:30:42.960 --> 01:30:45.840
One particular shadow play was reserved

01:30:45.840 --> 01:30:48.560
solely for times when a plague of mice

01:30:48.560 --> 01:30:51.760
or rats had descended on a village, and

01:30:51.760 --> 01:30:54.880
its goal was to convince the rodents to

01:30:54.880 --> 01:30:57.679
depart and dwell in the kingdom of

01:30:57.679 --> 01:31:01.560
vermin instead.

01:31:06.000 --> 01:31:09.000
Over

01:31:12.400 --> 01:31:15.360
the next centuries, the story of Ken

01:31:15.360 --> 01:31:18.880
Angro, the first king of Singer Sari,

01:31:18.880 --> 01:31:21.360
would be told again and again in these

01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:24.480
kinds of performances and would take on

01:31:24.480 --> 01:31:28.000
more and more fantastical elements.

01:31:28.000 --> 01:31:30.320
And for that reason, it's impossible to

01:31:30.320 --> 01:31:33.199
say definitively which parts may have a

01:31:33.199 --> 01:31:36.159
grain of truth to them. But it's likely

01:31:36.159 --> 01:31:39.920
that some elements are true. That Ken

01:31:39.920 --> 01:31:43.360
Angro was a common man of uncertain

01:31:43.360 --> 01:31:46.560
birth and lineage. That he had been a

01:31:46.560 --> 01:31:49.840
thief or brigand of some kind. That he

01:31:49.840 --> 01:31:52.000
rose to power in the kingdom in a

01:31:52.000 --> 01:31:55.440
violent upheaval and crushed the nearby

01:31:55.440 --> 01:32:00.159
kingdom of Kadiri in open battle.

01:32:00.159 --> 01:32:02.719
But after he comes to the throne, the

01:32:02.719 --> 01:32:05.840
tone of the chronicle shifts and becomes

01:32:05.840 --> 01:32:09.760
more grounded in historical reality.

01:32:09.760 --> 01:32:12.159
Many events recorded during his reign

01:32:12.159 --> 01:32:15.199
are dated. And so this second half of

01:32:15.199 --> 01:32:17.679
the chronicle is considered to contain

01:32:17.679 --> 01:32:20.000
more historically verifiable

01:32:20.000 --> 01:32:23.000
information.

01:32:27.600 --> 01:32:30.239
What we know for sure is that over the

01:32:30.239 --> 01:32:33.760
course of the 13th century, Ken Angro's

01:32:33.760 --> 01:32:37.199
new kingdom of Singari would gradually

01:32:37.199 --> 01:32:41.920
expand its power, wealth, and prestige.

01:32:41.920 --> 01:32:44.000
But it was under the reign of his

01:32:44.000 --> 01:32:46.800
greatgrandson, the fifth king of

01:32:46.800 --> 01:32:50.320
Singari, that it would grow into a true

01:32:50.320 --> 01:32:55.360
empire. His name was King Keranagara.

01:32:55.360 --> 01:32:57.600
And during his time on the throne, he

01:32:57.600 --> 01:33:00.400
would order expeditions to extend the

01:33:00.400 --> 01:33:03.040
kingdom's influence not just over most

01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:06.880
of Java, but across the sea to the large

01:33:06.880 --> 01:33:10.159
island of Borneo to the north, the small

01:33:10.159 --> 01:33:13.360
island of Bali to the east, and even

01:33:13.360 --> 01:33:16.639
conduct a successful invasion of Java's

01:33:16.639 --> 01:33:19.280
sister island of Sumatra in the

01:33:19.280 --> 01:33:21.120
northwest.

01:33:21.120 --> 01:33:24.320
Now the kingdom of Singari had grown to

01:33:24.320 --> 01:33:27.920
be a true seagoing empire and it

01:33:27.920 --> 01:33:30.480
controlled virtually all of the region's

01:33:30.480 --> 01:33:33.199
most crucial waterways.

01:33:33.199 --> 01:33:35.840
And the most important of these was the

01:33:35.840 --> 01:33:39.199
narrow sea corridor known as the

01:33:39.199 --> 01:33:43.159
straight of Malaka.

01:33:48.800 --> 01:33:52.719
The Malay Peninsula is a long body of

01:33:52.719 --> 01:33:55.920
land that stretches southeast from the

01:33:55.920 --> 01:33:58.639
southern edge of the Asian continent

01:33:58.639 --> 01:34:02.239
where Thailand meets Malaysia.

01:34:02.239 --> 01:34:05.280
And just off its southernmost point and

01:34:05.280 --> 01:34:07.280
following the line of the continental

01:34:07.280 --> 01:34:10.960
shelf is the island of Sumatra and then

01:34:10.960 --> 01:34:13.120
Java.

01:34:13.120 --> 01:34:16.560
Together, these form a sea wall of more

01:34:16.560 --> 01:34:20.480
than 3,000 km that stands between the

01:34:20.480 --> 01:34:24.159
Indian Ocean and the South Pacific and

01:34:24.159 --> 01:34:27.440
South China Sea.

01:34:27.440 --> 01:34:31.120
In this massive wall, there are only two

01:34:31.120 --> 01:34:34.239
narrow gates. The southerntherly one

01:34:34.239 --> 01:34:37.520
known as the Straits of Sunda and the

01:34:37.520 --> 01:34:42.800
northern one, the Straits of Malaka.

01:34:42.800 --> 01:34:45.760
The American sailor and writer Herman

01:34:45.760 --> 01:34:49.360
Melville writing in the mid 19th century

01:34:49.360 --> 01:34:54.400
describes the sight of these straits.

01:34:54.400 --> 01:34:57.199
Those narrow straits of Sunda stand

01:34:57.199 --> 01:35:00.800
midway in that vast rampart of islands

01:35:00.800 --> 01:35:03.440
like the central gateway opening into

01:35:03.440 --> 01:35:07.199
some vast walled empire.

01:35:07.199 --> 01:35:10.719
the inexhaustible wealth of spices and

01:35:10.719 --> 01:35:15.199
silks and jewels and gold and ivory with

01:35:15.199 --> 01:35:17.360
which the thousand islands of that

01:35:17.360 --> 01:35:20.719
oriental sea are enriched are thus

01:35:20.719 --> 01:35:24.639
guarded from the all grasping western

01:35:24.639 --> 01:35:27.639
world.

01:35:28.400 --> 01:35:30.719
For much of history, it has been the

01:35:30.719 --> 01:35:34.320
wider and deeper straight of Malaca that

01:35:34.320 --> 01:35:37.440
has been used most heavily.

01:35:37.440 --> 01:35:39.760
In fact, today it is the busiest

01:35:39.760 --> 01:35:42.480
shipping channel in the world, seeing

01:35:42.480 --> 01:35:45.440
nearly 100,000 ships pass through it

01:35:45.440 --> 01:35:48.080
each year.

01:35:48.080 --> 01:35:50.960
Around a quarter of all global trade

01:35:50.960 --> 01:35:53.920
passes through this narrow waterway,

01:35:53.920 --> 01:35:56.560
where the massive cities of Singapore

01:35:56.560 --> 01:36:01.280
and Koala Lumpur are today located.

01:36:01.280 --> 01:36:04.239
And in the 13th century during the time

01:36:04.239 --> 01:36:07.920
of the singari kingdom this waterway was

01:36:07.920 --> 01:36:13.120
no less crucial or lucrative.

01:36:13.120 --> 01:36:16.560
Around the year 1515, the Portuguese

01:36:16.560 --> 01:36:19.840
diplomat to Perez passed through the

01:36:19.840 --> 01:36:23.840
Yemen port of Aiden on the Red Sea and

01:36:23.840 --> 01:36:26.560
wrote that goods transported thousands

01:36:26.560 --> 01:36:29.199
of miles from Malaca featured

01:36:29.199 --> 01:36:32.320
prominently in the city's markets where

01:36:32.320 --> 01:36:35.360
merchants would carry them on to Egypt

01:36:35.360 --> 01:36:38.960
and from there into Europe.

01:36:38.960 --> 01:36:40.960
The merchants from Cairo bring the

01:36:40.960 --> 01:36:43.280
merchandise which comes from Italy and

01:36:43.280 --> 01:36:46.560
Greece and Damascus to Aiden. While the

01:36:46.560 --> 01:36:49.040
merchants of Aiden take back with them

01:36:49.040 --> 01:36:52.320
all the products of Malaca, cloves,

01:36:52.320 --> 01:36:56.000
nutmeg, mace, sandalwood, Brazil wood,

01:36:56.000 --> 01:37:00.480
silks, seed pearls, musk, porcelain, and

01:37:00.480 --> 01:37:02.400
other things.

01:37:02.400 --> 01:37:04.320
Control

01:37:04.320 --> 01:37:07.360
of the narrow waterway of the Malaca

01:37:07.360 --> 01:37:10.800
strait gave King Keranagardada immense

01:37:10.800 --> 01:37:14.159
power despite the relatively small size

01:37:14.159 --> 01:37:17.760
of the kingdom of Singasari.

01:37:17.760 --> 01:37:20.239
Now, anyone wishing to sail between

01:37:20.239 --> 01:37:23.360
China and India or the rest of the world

01:37:23.360 --> 01:37:26.000
either did so with Kerta Nagada's

01:37:26.000 --> 01:37:29.199
permission or had to take a detour of at

01:37:29.199 --> 01:37:33.199
least 2,000 km through rough and stormy

01:37:33.199 --> 01:37:37.520
seas around this island wall.

01:37:37.520 --> 01:37:40.639
As a result of this control, the power

01:37:40.639 --> 01:37:43.760
and wealth of Singer Sari grew

01:37:43.760 --> 01:37:46.000
dramatically.

01:37:46.000 --> 01:37:48.639
But there were much larger empires in

01:37:48.639 --> 01:37:51.840
the region who had a strong interest in

01:37:51.840 --> 01:37:54.080
making sure that the flow of goods by

01:37:54.080 --> 01:37:56.719
sea could pass through these narrow

01:37:56.719 --> 01:37:58.400
straits.

01:37:58.400 --> 01:38:01.600
And as the 13th century came to an end,

01:38:01.600 --> 01:38:05.280
the kingdom of Singari came into direct

01:38:05.280 --> 01:38:08.880
conflict with one of these much larger

01:38:08.880 --> 01:38:11.880
powers.

01:38:30.800 --> 01:38:33.280
In the year 1289,

01:38:33.280 --> 01:38:36.159
King Keranagara of the Javanese Kingdom

01:38:36.159 --> 01:38:39.119
of Singari received a group of

01:38:39.119 --> 01:38:42.400
ambassadors at his court.

01:38:42.400 --> 01:38:45.840
They came finely dressed, horty, and

01:38:45.840 --> 01:38:48.719
proud, and said that they had come to

01:38:48.719 --> 01:38:51.600
speak on behalf of the world's most

01:38:51.600 --> 01:38:54.080
powerful man.

01:38:54.080 --> 01:38:57.840
That was the Mongol Emperor of China,

01:38:57.840 --> 01:39:01.560
Kubla Khn.

01:39:07.840 --> 01:39:11.199
As we saw in our 19th episode, from

01:39:11.199 --> 01:39:13.840
their humble beginnings on the Mongolian

01:39:13.840 --> 01:39:17.520
step, over the last century, the Mongols

01:39:17.520 --> 01:39:20.159
had embarked on a remarkable series of

01:39:20.159 --> 01:39:23.600
campaigns to conquer all of China,

01:39:23.600 --> 01:39:26.719
Persia, and the Middle East, along with

01:39:26.719 --> 01:39:29.119
much of what is today Russia, and

01:39:29.119 --> 01:39:31.760
Eastern Europe.

01:39:31.760 --> 01:39:35.280
Founded by the warlord Chingis Khan, the

01:39:35.280 --> 01:39:38.080
Mongol Empire was the largest contiguous

01:39:38.080 --> 01:39:41.280
land empire in history and combined the

01:39:41.280 --> 01:39:44.239
speed and power of Mongol horsemen with

01:39:44.239 --> 01:39:47.760
the craftsmanship of Persia and the

01:39:47.760 --> 01:39:52.800
ingenuity and manpower of China.

01:39:52.800 --> 01:39:55.199
By this point, the enormous Mongol

01:39:55.199 --> 01:39:58.239
Empire had split into four separate

01:39:58.239 --> 01:40:01.520
domains. But the largest of these was

01:40:01.520 --> 01:40:04.159
still the world's biggest empire at the

01:40:04.159 --> 01:40:05.760
time.

01:40:05.760 --> 01:40:08.800
That was the one ruled from China by the

01:40:08.800 --> 01:40:12.560
grandson of Chingis Khan, the emperor

01:40:12.560 --> 01:40:15.560
Kubla.

01:40:16.159 --> 01:40:19.920
This hybrid Chinese Mongolian power was

01:40:19.920 --> 01:40:24.800
known as the Yuan dynasty.

01:40:24.800 --> 01:40:27.760
But by this time, the empire had begun

01:40:27.760 --> 01:40:30.080
to struggle.

01:40:30.080 --> 01:40:33.520
The emperor Kubli was now well into his

01:40:33.520 --> 01:40:36.800
70s and his domain was plagued by

01:40:36.800 --> 01:40:40.719
political and economic problems.

01:40:40.719 --> 01:40:43.199
The Mongol Empire had been built on

01:40:43.199 --> 01:40:47.119
conquest, but now its terrifying engine

01:40:47.119 --> 01:40:51.119
seemed to have run out of fuel. 8 years

01:40:51.119 --> 01:40:53.920
earlier, Kubla's forces had for the

01:40:53.920 --> 01:40:56.960
second time failed to capture a foothold

01:40:56.960 --> 01:41:00.400
on the islands of Japan. His invasions

01:41:00.400 --> 01:41:03.679
of Burma and Vietnam had also fizzled

01:41:03.679 --> 01:41:06.880
out with the Mongol forces struggling in

01:41:06.880 --> 01:41:09.360
the tropical heat.

01:41:09.360 --> 01:41:12.000
The aging Mongol Emperor desperately

01:41:12.000 --> 01:41:15.360
needed a victory, and he had been

01:41:15.360 --> 01:41:18.560
increasingly casting his gaze southwards

01:41:18.560 --> 01:41:21.679
across the sea and towards the wealthy

01:41:21.679 --> 01:41:24.960
island of Java.

01:41:24.960 --> 01:41:28.239
The Chinese chronicle, the Yuani, or

01:41:28.239 --> 01:41:32.080
History of Yuan, describes this strange

01:41:32.080 --> 01:41:35.679
and farway land.

01:41:35.679 --> 01:41:37.679
The customs and products of this land

01:41:37.679 --> 01:41:40.480
are not much known, but as a rule, the

01:41:40.480 --> 01:41:42.880
barbarian countries over the sea produce

01:41:42.880 --> 01:41:46.000
many rare and valuable things which

01:41:46.000 --> 01:41:48.320
fetch a high price in China. The

01:41:48.320 --> 01:41:50.639
inhabitants are strange and their nature

01:41:50.639 --> 01:41:52.480
and speech are not understood by the

01:41:52.480 --> 01:41:55.480
Chinese.

01:41:55.760 --> 01:41:59.360
By that time, Java's kingagara

01:41:59.360 --> 01:42:02.560
had been defying Kubla Khan for nearly a

01:42:02.560 --> 01:42:04.560
decade.

01:42:04.560 --> 01:42:07.520
Two previous ambassadorial visits to his

01:42:07.520 --> 01:42:10.159
court had been sent home without any

01:42:10.159 --> 01:42:13.360
tribute for the Mongol Khn, and the

01:42:13.360 --> 01:42:15.840
defiance of this small island was

01:42:15.840 --> 01:42:20.920
beginning to make the empire look weak.

01:42:23.040 --> 01:42:25.920
For this reason, in 1289,

01:42:25.920 --> 01:42:29.920
Kubla sent a new party of envoys to Java

01:42:29.920 --> 01:42:32.800
to meet with the king and give him a

01:42:32.800 --> 01:42:36.000
final ultimatum.

01:42:36.000 --> 01:42:39.119
They demanded that King Kerton swear an

01:42:39.119 --> 01:42:42.239
oath of feelalty to the Mongol Emperor,

01:42:42.239 --> 01:42:44.960
pay him a hefty tribute, and send

01:42:44.960 --> 01:42:47.040
members of his royal family to the

01:42:47.040 --> 01:42:50.000
Mongol court in China to act as

01:42:50.000 --> 01:42:51.600
hostages.

01:42:51.600 --> 01:42:54.719
But when these ambassadors arrived, they

01:42:54.719 --> 01:42:58.080
would not find King Keranagara in an

01:42:58.080 --> 01:43:01.719
agreeable mood.

01:43:02.960 --> 01:43:05.840
The Javanese of the time considered

01:43:05.840 --> 01:43:08.320
repeated requests of this kind to be

01:43:08.320 --> 01:43:10.800
exceedingly rude.

01:43:10.800 --> 01:43:14.080
To Perez writes about the proud nature

01:43:14.080 --> 01:43:18.360
of the Javanese people.

01:43:18.560 --> 01:43:21.199
The Japanese are men who if they write

01:43:21.199 --> 01:43:24.000
once and do not get a reply, do not

01:43:24.000 --> 01:43:26.800
write again. Although it may be of great

01:43:26.800 --> 01:43:29.440
importance to them, the Japanese are

01:43:29.440 --> 01:43:32.880
daring men and determined to die. They

01:43:32.880 --> 01:43:38.520
are gamblers and play for high stakes.

01:43:39.679 --> 01:43:43.679
King Keranagara was no different and he

01:43:43.679 --> 01:43:46.880
would now make a tremendous gamble for

01:43:46.880 --> 01:43:50.400
the highest stakes possible.

01:43:50.400 --> 01:43:52.960
He ordered that the Mongol ambassadors

01:43:52.960 --> 01:43:55.119
be punished.

01:43:55.119 --> 01:43:57.760
By some accounts, their faces were

01:43:57.760 --> 01:44:00.800
branded with hot irons and their ears

01:44:00.800 --> 01:44:04.719
cut off, a punishment typically reserved

01:44:04.719 --> 01:44:08.239
for bandits and pirates.

01:44:08.239 --> 01:44:10.639
We can only imagine the rage of the

01:44:10.639 --> 01:44:13.920
Mongol Emperor Kubla Khn upon hearing

01:44:13.920 --> 01:44:17.760
this news and seeing the mutilated faces

01:44:17.760 --> 01:44:20.159
of his ambassadors.

01:44:20.159 --> 01:44:23.520
The history of Yuan describes what

01:44:23.520 --> 01:44:26.920
happened next.

01:44:27.679 --> 01:44:30.159
In the second month of the 29th year of

01:44:30.159 --> 01:44:32.880
the Yuan dynasty, the emperor issued an

01:44:32.880 --> 01:44:34.880
order to the governor of Fujen,

01:44:34.880 --> 01:44:37.280
directing him to send an army to subdue

01:44:37.280 --> 01:44:39.920
Java, to collect soldiers to the number

01:44:39.920 --> 01:44:43.440
of 20,000, to send out a thousand ships,

01:44:43.440 --> 01:44:45.600
and to equip them with provisions for a

01:44:45.600 --> 01:44:49.679
year and with 40,000 bars of silver.

01:44:49.679 --> 01:44:52.239
The emperor said to them, "When you

01:44:52.239 --> 01:44:54.320
arrive at Java, you must clearly

01:44:54.320 --> 01:44:56.480
proclaim that they have lately cut the

01:44:56.480 --> 01:44:59.760
face of the imperial envoy, Mongchi, and

01:44:59.760 --> 01:45:04.119
that you have come to punish them."

01:45:05.199 --> 01:45:08.800
This expedition set sail 3 years later

01:45:08.800 --> 01:45:12.000
in the year 1292,

01:45:12.000 --> 01:45:15.760
but it was to be a difficult voyage.

01:45:15.760 --> 01:45:18.639
The history of Yuan describes the

01:45:18.639 --> 01:45:21.520
troubles they encountered on the Java

01:45:21.520 --> 01:45:23.440
Sea.

01:45:23.440 --> 01:45:26.000
The wind was strong and the sea very

01:45:26.000 --> 01:45:28.880
rough so that the ships rolled heavily

01:45:28.880 --> 01:45:31.040
and the soldiers could not eat for many

01:45:31.040 --> 01:45:34.159
days. The forces to attack Java were

01:45:34.159 --> 01:45:36.560
driven by the wind to one island and

01:45:36.560 --> 01:45:39.840
many ships were wrecked. Over a hundred

01:45:39.840 --> 01:45:42.000
men who were ill from the long beating

01:45:42.000 --> 01:45:44.480
about in the storm were unable to leave

01:45:44.480 --> 01:45:46.719
with the rest of the expedition and were

01:45:46.719 --> 01:45:49.840
left there. And today the Chinese live

01:45:49.840 --> 01:45:54.119
mixed up with the native families.

01:45:54.400 --> 01:45:56.960
Despite their troubles on the voyage,

01:45:56.960 --> 01:45:59.520
the Mongol forces eventually arrived on

01:45:59.520 --> 01:46:02.639
the shores of Java in the next year of

01:46:02.639 --> 01:46:04.560
1293,

01:46:04.560 --> 01:46:07.119
ready to punish King Keranagara for

01:46:07.119 --> 01:46:10.320
defying the empire and mistreating its

01:46:10.320 --> 01:46:12.560
ambassadors.

01:46:12.560 --> 01:46:15.199
But when they arrived, they would find

01:46:15.199 --> 01:46:18.159
their enthusiasm for revenge had been

01:46:18.159 --> 01:46:20.880
somewhat deflated.

01:46:20.880 --> 01:46:23.520
In fact, in the preceding year, the

01:46:23.520 --> 01:46:26.000
defiant kingagara

01:46:26.000 --> 01:46:29.199
had been overthrown and killed by a

01:46:29.199 --> 01:46:34.600
usurper named Ja Katon.

01:46:43.119 --> 01:46:47.440
Ja Katon was the ruler of a city called

01:46:47.440 --> 01:46:50.480
Kediri, which controlled a province

01:46:50.480 --> 01:46:54.880
covering much of central Java.

01:46:54.880 --> 01:46:57.199
For a long time, Kadiri had actually

01:46:57.199 --> 01:46:59.280
been the predominant power on the

01:46:59.280 --> 01:47:02.639
island. But after its king, Dandan

01:47:02.639 --> 01:47:05.040
Gendis had been defeated in battle by

01:47:05.040 --> 01:47:08.320
the hero Ken Angro, Kadiri had been

01:47:08.320 --> 01:47:12.639
eclipsed by the rise of Singari.

01:47:12.639 --> 01:47:15.760
Now Kadiri was a vassel of King

01:47:15.760 --> 01:47:17.760
Keranagara

01:47:17.760 --> 01:47:20.400
but it was by far the most powerful of

01:47:20.400 --> 01:47:24.080
his subjects and as a result never sat

01:47:24.080 --> 01:47:27.520
comfortably within his kingdom.

01:47:27.520 --> 01:47:31.360
The epic poem the Deshavanana describes

01:47:31.360 --> 01:47:35.679
the new ruler of Kadiri Ja Katon as

01:47:35.679 --> 01:47:40.040
cunning and malevolent.

01:47:45.840 --> 01:47:48.320
There was a vassal king, a villain known

01:47:48.320 --> 01:47:52.000
by the name of Ja Katong, who there in

01:47:52.000 --> 01:47:54.880
the land of Kadiri desired to replace

01:47:54.880 --> 01:47:57.520
the king and was outstandingly clever at

01:47:57.520 --> 01:48:00.840
laying schemes.

01:48:07.119 --> 01:48:09.920
At the time, the majority of King

01:48:09.920 --> 01:48:14.080
Keranagara's forces were away from Java,

01:48:14.080 --> 01:48:16.239
fighting to increase his territory

01:48:16.239 --> 01:48:20.159
across the sea in Sumatra. And so, Ja

01:48:20.159 --> 01:48:24.000
Katon saw his chance.

01:48:24.000 --> 01:48:27.280
According to the Paraton or Book of

01:48:27.280 --> 01:48:30.560
Kings, Jaakong was encouraged to seize

01:48:30.560 --> 01:48:34.159
the opportunity by one of his allies who

01:48:34.159 --> 01:48:39.560
sent him a thinly veiled message.

01:48:46.000 --> 01:48:50.080
The secret letter said, "My lord, I

01:48:50.080 --> 01:48:53.280
respectfully tell you if his majesty has

01:48:53.280 --> 01:48:56.880
any consideration and desire to hunt.

01:48:56.880 --> 01:48:59.600
Now his majesty has the chance to so

01:48:59.600 --> 01:49:02.800
hunt. It will be the best and the most

01:49:02.800 --> 01:49:05.840
opportune moment. There is no danger.

01:49:05.840 --> 01:49:08.639
There are no tigers, wild buffaloos, nor

01:49:08.639 --> 01:49:11.920
snakes, or even thorns. There is only

01:49:11.920 --> 01:49:17.320
one tiger, but it has no teeth.

01:49:23.840 --> 01:49:26.960
Urged on by this coded message, King

01:49:26.960 --> 01:49:30.719
Jayak rose in rebellion.

01:49:30.719 --> 01:49:33.840
His city of Kadiri was not far from the

01:49:33.840 --> 01:49:36.320
capital of Singari,

01:49:36.320 --> 01:49:38.880
but it was on the other side of a number

01:49:38.880 --> 01:49:42.639
of towering volcanic cones, mounts

01:49:42.639 --> 01:49:46.560
Kellud, Arjuna, and Kawi.

01:49:46.560 --> 01:49:49.760
to strike at Singari and depose the

01:49:49.760 --> 01:49:52.320
king. He could either march north

01:49:52.320 --> 01:49:54.400
through the easier territory of the

01:49:54.400 --> 01:49:57.679
northern plains or south through the

01:49:57.679 --> 01:50:01.360
rugged hill country riven by gorges and

01:50:01.360 --> 01:50:03.600
ravines.

01:50:03.600 --> 01:50:06.719
The cunning Ja Katon considered his

01:50:06.719 --> 01:50:11.760
options and came up with a plan.

01:50:11.760 --> 01:50:13.840
In 1292,

01:50:13.840 --> 01:50:17.119
alarming news reached King Kerton's

01:50:17.119 --> 01:50:18.800
court.

01:50:18.800 --> 01:50:20.800
Messengers would have burst into his

01:50:20.800 --> 01:50:23.840
throne room and breathlessly told him

01:50:23.840 --> 01:50:26.400
that an army had been seen rampaging

01:50:26.400 --> 01:50:29.280
through the farmland to the north,

01:50:29.280 --> 01:50:31.760
flying the distinctive white and red

01:50:31.760 --> 01:50:34.560
banners of Kadiri.

01:50:34.560 --> 01:50:37.600
They had taken the toothless tiger King

01:50:37.600 --> 01:50:42.800
Keranagara completely by surprise.

01:50:46.400 --> 01:50:48.560
Now, King Jayak Katang set out to

01:50:48.560 --> 01:50:51.920
attack. His army coming from the north

01:50:51.920 --> 01:50:54.719
consisted of bad people. They were full

01:50:54.719 --> 01:50:58.000
of flags and sounds. The area to the

01:50:58.000 --> 01:51:02.040
north was devastated.

01:51:06.480 --> 01:51:08.960
Dismayed at the destruction, the king

01:51:08.960 --> 01:51:11.920
appointed one of his son-in-laws to lead

01:51:11.920 --> 01:51:15.760
what forces he had remaining in Java. A

01:51:15.760 --> 01:51:20.520
man named Raden Vijaya.

01:51:20.639 --> 01:51:23.280
This young man marched north with the

01:51:23.280 --> 01:51:26.320
remains of the royal army and met

01:51:26.320 --> 01:51:30.320
Jaakatong's rampaging forces in battle.

01:51:30.320 --> 01:51:33.920
As one Javanese inscription carved at a

01:51:33.920 --> 01:51:38.639
place called Kudadu describes,

01:51:38.639 --> 01:51:42.480
when King Jaya Katon's troops reached

01:51:42.480 --> 01:51:46.159
the village of Jasun Wong Kal, King

01:51:46.159 --> 01:51:49.760
Kerta Nagara sent his son-in-law Raden

01:51:49.760 --> 01:51:53.679
Wijaya to fight the enemy. After the

01:51:53.679 --> 01:51:56.880
battle, the enemy fled while suffering a

01:51:56.880 --> 01:52:00.480
great loss. Seemingly they disappeared

01:52:00.480 --> 01:52:03.480
forever.

01:52:05.440 --> 01:52:08.639
Raden Vagaya had succeeded in the north

01:52:08.639 --> 01:52:10.800
and defended his father-in-law's

01:52:10.800 --> 01:52:14.159
kingdom, which he was set to one day

01:52:14.159 --> 01:52:16.159
inherit.

01:52:16.159 --> 01:52:20.000
But now the true strategy of Jaong was

01:52:20.000 --> 01:52:22.480
revealed.

01:52:22.480 --> 01:52:25.599
While this loud northern force had been

01:52:25.599 --> 01:52:27.599
burning and sacking their way through

01:52:27.599 --> 01:52:30.800
the north of the kingdom, a much larger

01:52:30.800 --> 01:52:33.760
second force had also advanced in the

01:52:33.760 --> 01:52:36.880
south. This army moved much more

01:52:36.880 --> 01:52:39.119
stealthily through the ravines and

01:52:39.119 --> 01:52:42.080
valleys of the central highlands

01:52:42.080 --> 01:52:47.000
as the paraton describes.

01:52:50.639 --> 01:52:54.400
Then a large army descended from Kadiri

01:52:54.400 --> 01:52:56.880
coming from the banks of the Axa River

01:52:56.880 --> 01:52:59.599
heading towards Lour.

01:52:59.599 --> 01:53:02.159
They were not allowed to carry flags or

01:53:02.159 --> 01:53:04.320
make any noise.

01:53:04.320 --> 01:53:06.719
Upon arrival at Sidabana,

01:53:06.719 --> 01:53:11.080
they headed straight for Singasari.

01:53:14.560 --> 01:53:17.880
be son.

01:53:18.880 --> 01:53:22.159
>> This force would go completely unnoticed

01:53:22.159 --> 01:53:24.159
and they apparently arrived at the

01:53:24.159 --> 01:53:27.599
kingdom's capital of Coutaraja while

01:53:27.599 --> 01:53:32.599
King Keranagara was drunk.

01:53:34.000 --> 01:53:37.599
Drinking in Java was a serious business

01:53:37.599 --> 01:53:39.679
and a large number of alcoholic

01:53:39.679 --> 01:53:42.480
beverages were consumed for pleasure,

01:53:42.480 --> 01:53:46.000
especially on special occasions.

01:53:46.000 --> 01:53:49.199
One Javanese poem known as the Sumana

01:53:49.199 --> 01:53:52.639
Santa describes the drinks available at

01:53:52.639 --> 01:53:56.719
an idealized wedding.

01:53:56.719 --> 01:53:59.760
The drinks poured continuously from rock

01:53:59.760 --> 01:54:02.719
crystal pitches like fountains of palm

01:54:02.719 --> 01:54:06.159
syrup. Sugar cane, wine, and rice beer

01:54:06.159 --> 01:54:09.119
were drunk one after the other like holy

01:54:09.119 --> 01:54:12.080
water and meat welling up from glass

01:54:12.080 --> 01:54:15.080
vessels.

01:54:16.960 --> 01:54:19.840
>> But the influence of tantric Buddhism

01:54:19.840 --> 01:54:22.159
meant that drinking was more than just

01:54:22.159 --> 01:54:25.599
for fun. In fact, it was at times a

01:54:25.599 --> 01:54:28.719
spiritual practice and even a royal

01:54:28.719 --> 01:54:30.480
duty.

01:54:30.480 --> 01:54:32.960
The king was required to take part in

01:54:32.960 --> 01:54:36.480
ceremonies known as chakra puja which

01:54:36.480 --> 01:54:38.800
involved the drawing of geometric

01:54:38.800 --> 01:54:42.000
designs on the earth with colored powder

01:54:42.000 --> 01:54:46.800
after which the ritual could take place.

01:54:46.800 --> 01:54:49.920
The historian Miranda Shaw describes the

01:54:49.920 --> 01:54:55.159
unfolding of one of these rituals.

01:54:55.920 --> 01:54:58.239
An elaborate array of offerings and

01:54:58.239 --> 01:55:00.639
foods are laid out. The participants

01:55:00.639 --> 01:55:02.719
dawn special insignia like bone

01:55:02.719 --> 01:55:05.520
ornaments and crowns and use musical

01:55:05.520 --> 01:55:07.840
instruments of archaic design such as

01:55:07.840 --> 01:55:10.159
skull drums, thighbone trumpets, and

01:55:10.159 --> 01:55:12.800
conch horns for inducing heightened

01:55:12.800 --> 01:55:15.840
awareness. Practitioners sit in a circle

01:55:15.840 --> 01:55:18.480
and partake of sacramental meat and wine

01:55:18.480 --> 01:55:20.960
served in skull cups. The feast

01:55:20.960 --> 01:55:23.280
culminates in the performance of tantric

01:55:23.280 --> 01:55:25.599
dances and music that must never be

01:55:25.599 --> 01:55:29.320
disclosed to outsiders.

01:55:30.159 --> 01:55:32.960
While this ceremony was a crucial part

01:55:32.960 --> 01:55:36.639
of King Keranagara's royal calendar, the

01:55:36.639 --> 01:55:40.400
timing couldn't have been worse.

01:55:40.400 --> 01:55:43.599
Jaakatong's concealed force arrived

01:55:43.599 --> 01:55:47.280
outside the city walls without warning.

01:55:47.280 --> 01:55:50.080
They took the garrison by surprise and

01:55:50.080 --> 01:55:52.719
poured over the walls of the city while

01:55:52.719 --> 01:55:56.400
the king was thus engaged.

01:55:56.400 --> 01:55:59.760
The city was taken and King Keranagaram

01:55:59.760 --> 01:56:03.080
was killed.

01:56:08.480 --> 01:56:12.400
The king's son-in-law, Raden Vaya, was

01:56:12.400 --> 01:56:14.800
still celebrating his victory in the

01:56:14.800 --> 01:56:18.000
north, and he must have been distraught

01:56:18.000 --> 01:56:21.440
when the news reached him. He had won

01:56:21.440 --> 01:56:25.199
his battle, but lost the war, and now

01:56:25.199 --> 01:56:27.920
everything he had stood to inherit had

01:56:27.920 --> 01:56:34.199
also been taken by the usurper Ja Katon.

01:56:35.520 --> 01:56:38.400
Raden Vagaya now retreated to the

01:56:38.400 --> 01:56:41.280
rainforests of the northeast and left

01:56:41.280 --> 01:56:44.480
the capital and the throne in the hands

01:56:44.480 --> 01:56:48.320
of the rebel Ja Katon.

01:56:48.320 --> 01:56:51.199
The city of Kusarajjo, the heart of the

01:56:51.199 --> 01:56:54.400
Singosari kingdom was looted and

01:56:54.400 --> 01:56:57.760
depopulated and many of its people taken

01:56:57.760 --> 01:57:00.960
back to Kadiri.

01:57:00.960 --> 01:57:03.760
Others simply fled into the safety of

01:57:03.760 --> 01:57:08.760
the countryside and never returned.

01:57:08.960 --> 01:57:12.000
Some stonemasons working on a new temple

01:57:12.000 --> 01:57:14.800
in the city simply dropped their tools

01:57:14.800 --> 01:57:17.360
in the middle of carving their reliefs

01:57:17.360 --> 01:57:20.639
and never came back to finish them.

01:57:20.639 --> 01:57:23.840
After that, the city was left to crumble

01:57:23.840 --> 01:57:27.040
and be taken over by the encroaching

01:57:27.040 --> 01:57:30.040
forest.

01:57:30.480 --> 01:57:34.159
Now the dispossessed prince Raden Vagaya

01:57:34.159 --> 01:57:38.320
and the rebel usurper Ja Katon faced off

01:57:38.320 --> 01:57:41.280
against one another. But it seems

01:57:41.280 --> 01:57:43.760
neither side of this civil war was

01:57:43.760 --> 01:57:46.639
confident in victory.

01:57:46.639 --> 01:57:48.880
Raden vagaya wasn't strong enough to

01:57:48.880 --> 01:57:51.679
march south and take his enemy's capital

01:57:51.679 --> 01:57:53.520
of Kadiri.

01:57:53.520 --> 01:57:56.239
And meanwhile, Jaakong couldn't leave

01:57:56.239 --> 01:57:59.599
his city and risk losing his shaky grasp

01:57:59.599 --> 01:58:02.159
on the throne.

01:58:02.159 --> 01:58:05.040
Both parties entered into an uneasy

01:58:05.040 --> 01:58:06.719
negotiation.

01:58:06.719 --> 01:58:09.760
And eventually, the rebel king settled

01:58:09.760 --> 01:58:14.239
for buying off Raden Vaga.

01:58:14.239 --> 01:58:17.040
In exchange for laying down his arms,

01:58:17.040 --> 01:58:19.199
the prince would be granted a piece of

01:58:19.199 --> 01:58:22.000
land, and there he would be allowed to

01:58:22.000 --> 01:58:25.679
build a city.

01:58:25.679 --> 01:58:28.560
Rod and Vaga, now completely out of

01:58:28.560 --> 01:58:31.679
other options and stranded in the wild

01:58:31.679 --> 01:58:36.880
rainforest, had no choice but to agree.

01:58:36.880 --> 01:58:39.840
But it must have been with no small

01:58:39.840 --> 01:58:44.119
amount of bitterness.

01:58:45.280 --> 01:58:48.080
The prince must have felt bitter too

01:58:48.080 --> 01:58:50.480
when he reached the piece of land that

01:58:50.480 --> 01:58:55.119
Ja Katang had granted him. It was a wild

01:58:55.119 --> 01:58:58.000
overgrown jungle in the middle of a

01:58:58.000 --> 01:59:01.040
sparsely inhabited area known as the

01:59:01.040 --> 01:59:03.599
Tardic Forest.

01:59:03.599 --> 01:59:06.560
But his fate was sealed, and he

01:59:06.560 --> 01:59:09.040
swallowed his bitterness and ordered his

01:59:09.040 --> 01:59:11.840
people to begin clearing the land for

01:59:11.840 --> 01:59:15.880
construction and farming.

01:59:17.679 --> 01:59:21.040
The old growth forests of Java were

01:59:21.040 --> 01:59:24.719
dense and wild, fed by the volcanic

01:59:24.719 --> 01:59:27.199
soil.

01:59:27.199 --> 01:59:30.000
Colorful hornvilles roosted in the

01:59:30.000 --> 01:59:32.880
treetops, while hidden high among the

01:59:32.880 --> 01:59:36.400
branches, gibbons greeted the rising sun

01:59:36.400 --> 01:59:40.560
with their long mournful songs.

01:59:40.560 --> 01:59:44.080
Troops of long-tailed macac monkeys

01:59:44.080 --> 01:59:47.520
leapt through the trees, while sambar

01:59:47.520 --> 01:59:49.920
deer crept through the shade of the

01:59:49.920 --> 01:59:54.000
forest. Great pythons lay coiled in the

01:59:54.000 --> 01:59:57.599
trees, and dangerous animals like the

01:59:57.599 --> 02:00:01.440
Javan leopard and wild boar lurked

02:00:01.440 --> 02:00:06.040
hidden in the green undergrowth.

02:00:06.320 --> 02:00:08.639
Everywhere could be heard the creaking

02:00:08.639 --> 02:00:11.760
of cicardas and frogs calling to one

02:00:11.760 --> 02:00:14.960
another from hidden pools.

02:00:14.960 --> 02:00:18.159
At sunset, fruit bats rose in their

02:00:18.159 --> 02:00:21.520
thousands from their hidden caves, while

02:00:21.520 --> 02:00:24.000
fireflies would have been visible at

02:00:24.000 --> 02:00:26.800
night.

02:00:26.800 --> 02:00:29.280
The trees were the most ancient life of

02:00:29.280 --> 02:00:31.119
the forest.

02:00:31.119 --> 02:00:34.560
Towering hardwoods like teik, ebony, and

02:00:34.560 --> 02:00:37.280
tamarind would have risen here,

02:00:37.280 --> 02:00:40.239
interspersed with bamboo groves,

02:00:40.239 --> 02:00:44.080
strangler figs, palms, and tangled lyana

02:00:44.080 --> 02:00:47.760
vines, all competing for every shaft of

02:00:47.760 --> 02:00:50.000
sunlight.

02:00:50.000 --> 02:00:52.639
But when they began cutting down this

02:00:52.639 --> 02:00:56.320
forest, Raden Vaga's men found that a

02:00:56.320 --> 02:00:59.119
particular kind of tree grew there in

02:00:59.119 --> 02:01:01.760
great quantities.

02:01:01.760 --> 02:01:04.560
This was the tree that grows a fruit

02:01:04.560 --> 02:01:08.480
which in Indonesia is called maja and is

02:01:08.480 --> 02:01:11.599
known elsewhere as a wood apple,

02:01:11.599 --> 02:01:16.000
elephant apple or Indian quint.

02:01:16.000 --> 02:01:19.199
These maja fruits are pear-shaped and

02:01:19.199 --> 02:01:22.080
the size of a large grapefruit with a

02:01:22.080 --> 02:01:25.360
thick hard woody rind that needs to be

02:01:25.360 --> 02:01:28.719
cracked with a hammer.

02:01:28.719 --> 02:01:31.840
Inside is an orangey yellow pulp that

02:01:31.840 --> 02:01:35.199
gives off the scent of roses but tastes

02:01:35.199 --> 02:01:37.520
sweet and bitter a little like

02:01:37.520 --> 02:01:39.840
marmalade.

02:01:39.840 --> 02:01:42.960
The word for bitter in Japanese is

02:01:42.960 --> 02:01:46.159
parit. And due to the large numbers of

02:01:46.159 --> 02:01:48.560
these maja fruits growing in this

02:01:48.560 --> 02:01:52.159
region, the people named this place Maja

02:01:52.159 --> 02:01:56.480
Parit or Bitter Wood apple as the

02:01:56.480 --> 02:02:00.599
Paraton describes.

02:02:06.880 --> 02:02:08.719
When the mades were building the

02:02:08.719 --> 02:02:12.000
village, a hungry man lacking supplies

02:02:12.000 --> 02:02:14.480
while cutting down the forest ate a

02:02:14.480 --> 02:02:17.679
marajger fruit. He found it bitter and

02:02:17.679 --> 02:02:19.679
threw away all the mara fruit he had

02:02:19.679 --> 02:02:23.119
picked. The majger fruit there became

02:02:23.119 --> 02:02:26.239
known for its bitter taste and the place

02:02:26.239 --> 02:02:29.719
was then named.

02:02:32.639 --> 02:02:35.639
abide

02:02:37.360 --> 02:02:40.480
>> for Raden Vajaya and his people. The

02:02:40.480 --> 02:02:43.199
name Maja Pahit was a perfect

02:02:43.199 --> 02:02:46.239
encapsulation of the bitterness of their

02:02:46.239 --> 02:02:48.480
situation.

02:02:48.480 --> 02:02:51.360
They had lost a kingdom and gained a

02:02:51.360 --> 02:02:56.080
plot of wild jungle in return and all

02:02:56.080 --> 02:03:00.960
because of the treachery of Ja Katon.

02:03:00.960 --> 02:03:03.360
They all must have shared a single

02:03:03.360 --> 02:03:07.360
desire to throw out the rebel king and

02:03:07.360 --> 02:03:12.119
unite Java once more.

02:03:12.320 --> 02:03:16.480
Their chance would come in the year 1293

02:03:16.480 --> 02:03:19.119
when the sails of the Mongol fleet

02:03:19.119 --> 02:03:23.320
appeared on the horizon.

02:03:38.239 --> 02:03:41.119
The Mongol fleet that had been sent to

02:03:41.119 --> 02:03:44.400
punish the people of Java was led by a

02:03:44.400 --> 02:03:48.639
commander named Sherbi.

02:03:48.639 --> 02:03:50.800
When he heard of the death of King

02:03:50.800 --> 02:03:53.679
Keranagara, he must have found himself

02:03:53.679 --> 02:03:57.119
in a quandry. His emperor demanded

02:03:57.119 --> 02:04:00.080
vengeance, and he and his men had sailed

02:04:00.080 --> 02:04:02.960
for months to get there. He must have

02:04:02.960 --> 02:04:07.119
feared leaving empty-handed.

02:04:07.119 --> 02:04:09.520
It was while he was puzzling over this

02:04:09.520 --> 02:04:13.040
situation that Sherbi was approached by

02:04:13.040 --> 02:04:16.080
a messenger from the bitter lord of the

02:04:16.080 --> 02:04:18.880
new city of Majapahit,

02:04:18.880 --> 02:04:23.280
the dispossessed prince Raden Vagaya.

02:04:23.280 --> 02:04:26.639
The Chinese history of Yuan describes

02:04:26.639 --> 02:04:31.719
the deal that the Mongols struck

02:04:32.480 --> 02:04:35.119
at that time. and Java carried on an old

02:04:35.119 --> 02:04:37.599
feud with the neighboring country and

02:04:37.599 --> 02:04:39.520
the old king of Java had already been

02:04:39.520 --> 02:04:41.040
killed.

02:04:41.040 --> 02:04:43.440
The son-in-law of the former Raden

02:04:43.440 --> 02:04:47.119
Vijaya had attacked Jaakaton but could

02:04:47.119 --> 02:04:50.239
not overcome him. He therefore retired

02:04:50.239 --> 02:04:53.199
to Maja Pahit. And when he heard that

02:04:53.199 --> 02:04:56.080
Sheibi and his army had arrived, he sent

02:04:56.080 --> 02:04:58.719
envoys with an account of his rivers and

02:04:58.719 --> 02:05:01.599
seap ports and a map of the country,

02:05:01.599 --> 02:05:04.080
offering his submission and asking for

02:05:04.080 --> 02:05:05.920
assistance.

02:05:05.920 --> 02:05:11.239
She then advanced with all his forces.

02:05:12.159 --> 02:05:14.880
For the Mongols, the arrangement was a

02:05:14.880 --> 02:05:18.639
neat way to solve their problem.

02:05:18.639 --> 02:05:21.280
They would help Raden Vaga overthrow the

02:05:21.280 --> 02:05:24.320
rebel Ja Katang and place him on the

02:05:24.320 --> 02:05:27.280
throne as a kind of puppet king,

02:05:27.280 --> 02:05:30.000
swearing allegiance to the Mongols in

02:05:30.000 --> 02:05:32.000
China.

02:05:32.000 --> 02:05:35.360
Then Sherb could return to Kubla Khan

02:05:35.360 --> 02:05:38.080
and say that he had brought the defiant

02:05:38.080 --> 02:05:42.719
little island back under control.

02:05:42.719 --> 02:05:46.080
But among Raden Vajaya's men, it must

02:05:46.080 --> 02:05:50.080
have been a controversial proposal.

02:05:50.080 --> 02:05:53.360
The Javanese were a proud people, and

02:05:53.360 --> 02:05:56.639
few had any desire to be ruled by the

02:05:56.639 --> 02:06:00.719
faroff Mongol Emperor.

02:06:00.719 --> 02:06:04.000
Some may even have called Raden Vaga a

02:06:04.000 --> 02:06:07.520
coward and a traitor.

02:06:07.520 --> 02:06:11.119
But all this time he was hatching a plot

02:06:11.119 --> 02:06:14.679
of his own.

02:06:15.040 --> 02:06:18.400
The later chronicle of the Paraton

02:06:18.400 --> 02:06:21.679
describes the ensuing war referring to

02:06:21.679 --> 02:06:26.199
the Mongols as Tatas.

02:06:34.719 --> 02:06:37.440
The Tata army came out from the north

02:06:37.440 --> 02:06:39.840
while the Majapahit armies came out from

02:06:39.840 --> 02:06:41.520
the east.

02:06:41.520 --> 02:06:44.800
King Jayakong was confused, unsure which

02:06:44.800 --> 02:06:48.159
to guard. Then he was attacked heavily

02:06:48.159 --> 02:06:51.440
from the north by the Tata army.

02:06:51.440 --> 02:06:54.000
King Jay Katang, who was fighting to the

02:06:54.000 --> 02:06:57.040
north, armed with a shield, was attacked

02:06:57.040 --> 02:06:59.679
together by the Tata people and was

02:06:59.679 --> 02:07:02.079
finally caught and imprisoned by the

02:07:02.079 --> 02:07:05.079
Tatas.

02:07:13.040 --> 02:07:16.320
The Mongols had now become kingmakers in

02:07:16.320 --> 02:07:20.480
Java. The 13th century Persian historian

02:07:20.480 --> 02:07:24.159
Abdullah Wasaf describes how they put

02:07:24.159 --> 02:07:29.560
Radan Vaya on the Javanese throne.

02:07:29.599 --> 02:07:32.560
His majesty Kublai put the old king's

02:07:32.560 --> 02:07:35.119
son-in-law Vijaya on the steps of the

02:07:35.119 --> 02:07:38.320
throne. He bestowed on him a ceremonial

02:07:38.320 --> 02:07:41.360
dress of honor and conferred on him much

02:07:41.360 --> 02:07:44.320
grace. And in exchange for the payment

02:07:44.320 --> 02:07:47.280
of tribute and taxes of pearls and gold,

02:07:47.280 --> 02:07:51.880
he left the island in his hands.

02:07:54.639 --> 02:07:57.280
The Mongol Emperor Kubli must have been

02:07:57.280 --> 02:08:00.400
ecstatic when he heard the news.

02:08:00.400 --> 02:08:02.800
Finally, here was a victory he could

02:08:02.800 --> 02:08:05.360
show to his people.

02:08:05.360 --> 02:08:07.920
The wealthy island of Java would now be

02:08:07.920 --> 02:08:11.040
added to his imperial domain along with

02:08:11.040 --> 02:08:14.480
its control of major shipping lanes. And

02:08:14.480 --> 02:08:16.639
perhaps now the fortunes of his

02:08:16.639 --> 02:08:19.440
teetering empire would finally turn

02:08:19.440 --> 02:08:21.199
around.

02:08:21.199 --> 02:08:25.679
But that was not to be the case.

02:08:25.679 --> 02:08:28.560
That's because the new king Raden Vaya

02:08:28.560 --> 02:08:31.760
had no intention of ruling Java as a

02:08:31.760 --> 02:08:35.280
vassel of Kubla Khan. And the moment he

02:08:35.280 --> 02:08:38.239
got to power, he turned on the Mongol

02:08:38.239 --> 02:08:40.960
forces who had helped him seize the

02:08:40.960 --> 02:08:42.560
throne.

02:08:42.560 --> 02:08:46.239
The Chinese history of Yuan gives a tur

02:08:46.239 --> 02:08:51.719
account of this disastrous turnaround.

02:08:52.400 --> 02:08:54.719
Raden Vagaya asked permission to return

02:08:54.719 --> 02:08:57.760
to his country in order to prepare a new

02:08:57.760 --> 02:09:00.159
letter of submission to the emperor and

02:09:00.159 --> 02:09:02.000
to take the precious articles in his

02:09:02.000 --> 02:09:04.800
possession back to court.

02:09:04.800 --> 02:09:07.840
Shui consented to this and sent two

02:09:07.840 --> 02:09:11.520
officers with 200 men to go with him.

02:09:11.520 --> 02:09:14.800
But on the way, Raden Vagaya killed the

02:09:14.800 --> 02:09:18.239
two officers and revolted again.

02:09:18.239 --> 02:09:20.320
After which he availed himself of the

02:09:20.320 --> 02:09:22.719
circumstance that the main army was

02:09:22.719 --> 02:09:28.199
returning to attack it from both sides.

02:09:29.520 --> 02:09:31.760
The Mongol army believed their mission

02:09:31.760 --> 02:09:34.400
to be complete and were already packing

02:09:34.400 --> 02:09:37.119
their ships to leave.

02:09:37.119 --> 02:09:40.239
The seasonal winds were about to change

02:09:40.239 --> 02:09:43.119
direction, and if they didn't move fast,

02:09:43.119 --> 02:09:45.599
they might become stranded on Java for

02:09:45.599 --> 02:09:48.159
another 6 months.

02:09:48.159 --> 02:09:51.199
When Raden Vaga's soldiers burst out of

02:09:51.199 --> 02:09:54.880
the forest in ambush, firing arrows and

02:09:54.880 --> 02:09:57.599
darts from their blow guns, the Mongol

02:09:57.599 --> 02:10:00.639
Yuan troops were taken completely by

02:10:00.639 --> 02:10:02.960
surprise.

02:10:02.960 --> 02:10:06.880
The Javanese epic poem Bulman Taka

02:10:06.880 --> 02:10:11.800
describes a battle of this kind.

02:10:12.880 --> 02:10:15.599
They were thrown into disarray and in

02:10:15.599 --> 02:10:18.560
fear the demon army fled and many of the

02:10:18.560 --> 02:10:20.560
demons and their leaders were struck

02:10:20.560 --> 02:10:23.280
dead. They withdrew in haste to the

02:10:23.280 --> 02:10:26.400
shelter of the fort but were pursued.

02:10:26.400 --> 02:10:28.880
Others shuddering sought a way of

02:10:28.880 --> 02:10:31.920
resisting but lacked the strength and

02:10:31.920 --> 02:10:35.440
hit by arrows floundered about and all

02:10:35.440 --> 02:10:39.119
of them left in fear and ran away. The

02:10:39.119 --> 02:10:41.760
whole fort was in uproar and all shouted

02:10:41.760 --> 02:10:45.040
in confusion. The fires glowed and

02:10:45.040 --> 02:10:47.280
blazed up frightfully like an erupting

02:10:47.280 --> 02:10:50.280
volcano.

02:10:54.880 --> 02:10:57.840
Thousands were killed and the remains of

02:10:57.840 --> 02:11:01.199
the Mongol army fled in disarray back to

02:11:01.199 --> 02:11:04.880
the ships as the history of Yuan

02:11:04.880 --> 02:11:07.880
describes.

02:11:11.119 --> 02:11:12.960
Sheep was left behind and was cut off

02:11:12.960 --> 02:11:15.199
from the rest of the army. He was forced

02:11:15.199 --> 02:11:16.960
to fight his way back to the ships for a

02:11:16.960 --> 02:11:19.599
distance of more than 100 miles. At

02:11:19.599 --> 02:11:21.760
last, he embarked again and reached

02:11:21.760 --> 02:11:24.960
China on a voyage of 68 days. Of his

02:11:24.960 --> 02:11:30.599
soldiers, more than 3,000 men had died.

02:11:32.719 --> 02:11:35.679
When news of this betrayal reached the

02:11:35.679 --> 02:11:39.360
emperor Kubla Khn, we can only imagine

02:11:39.360 --> 02:11:41.440
his rage.

02:11:41.440 --> 02:11:44.800
He ordered the general sherb to receive

02:11:44.800 --> 02:11:48.719
17 lashes and commanded a third of his

02:11:48.719 --> 02:11:51.679
property to be confiscated as punishment

02:11:51.679 --> 02:11:54.320
for his failure.

02:11:54.320 --> 02:11:56.400
He ordered his ministers to begin

02:11:56.400 --> 02:11:59.440
immediate preparations for a fullscale

02:11:59.440 --> 02:12:02.320
invasion of Java with an even larger

02:12:02.320 --> 02:12:07.040
army of 100,000 men. But these plans

02:12:07.040 --> 02:12:10.880
would never come to fruition.

02:12:10.880 --> 02:12:13.679
The disaster in Java would be the last

02:12:13.679 --> 02:12:17.280
campaign of Kubla Khan's reign and he

02:12:17.280 --> 02:12:21.599
died the next year in February of 1294

02:12:21.599 --> 02:12:25.360
at the age of 78.

02:12:25.360 --> 02:12:28.239
After that, the Mongol Yuan dynasty

02:12:28.239 --> 02:12:30.560
would enter into a steady and

02:12:30.560 --> 02:12:33.920
irrevocable decline and would collapse

02:12:33.920 --> 02:12:37.199
entirely little more than 70 years

02:12:37.199 --> 02:12:39.520
later.

02:12:39.520 --> 02:12:43.199
One great empire was coming to an end.

02:12:43.199 --> 02:12:45.840
But in its collapse, it gave way for the

02:12:45.840 --> 02:12:48.639
rise of what was now the undisputed

02:12:48.639 --> 02:12:52.800
major power on the island of Java and in

02:12:52.800 --> 02:12:56.719
the archipelago of Nusan Tar, the new

02:12:56.719 --> 02:13:01.719
power of Maja Parahit

02:13:06.880 --> 02:13:11.119
on the 15th day of the month of Kartika,

02:13:11.119 --> 02:13:13.679
the 8th month of the Hindu calendar.

02:13:13.679 --> 02:13:16.400
Raden Vagaya was crowned king in the

02:13:16.400 --> 02:13:19.679
palace of Majapahit.

02:13:19.679 --> 02:13:22.480
What had once been a stretch of wild

02:13:22.480 --> 02:13:25.599
jungle was now the beating heart of

02:13:25.599 --> 02:13:28.719
Java's most powerful kingdom.

02:13:28.719 --> 02:13:31.599
The Chinese history of Sun describes the

02:13:31.599 --> 02:13:34.400
appearance of the kings of Java. And

02:13:34.400 --> 02:13:37.119
from this we might imagine how this new

02:13:37.119 --> 02:13:39.599
king looked on the day of his

02:13:39.599 --> 02:13:42.599
coronation.

02:13:43.920 --> 02:13:47.760
The king has hair in a knot upon the top

02:13:47.760 --> 02:13:51.440
of his head. He wears golden bells, a

02:13:51.440 --> 02:13:55.360
silk robe, and shoes of leather. He sits

02:13:55.360 --> 02:13:58.800
on a square couch and his functionaries

02:13:58.800 --> 02:14:02.079
who see him daily salute him three times

02:14:02.079 --> 02:14:06.079
on going away. When he goes out, he

02:14:06.079 --> 02:14:09.520
rides on an elephant or sits in a

02:14:09.520 --> 02:14:13.599
carriage and from 5 to 700 soldiers

02:14:13.599 --> 02:14:16.480
follow him. When the people see the

02:14:16.480 --> 02:14:19.679
king, they squat down until he has

02:14:19.679 --> 02:14:22.679
passed.

02:14:30.000 --> 02:14:32.719
Raden vagaya would rule as the king of

02:14:32.719 --> 02:14:37.040
Majapahit for 16 years. But his reign

02:14:37.040 --> 02:14:41.320
would be a troubled one.

02:14:44.719 --> 02:14:47.360
From the earliest days of his rule, he

02:14:47.360 --> 02:14:50.880
faced rebellions, many of them from men

02:14:50.880 --> 02:14:54.000
who had fought alongside him against Ja

02:14:54.000 --> 02:14:57.599
Katang and the Mongols.

02:14:57.599 --> 02:14:59.920
Many of these disagreements were sparked

02:14:59.920 --> 02:15:02.000
over the question of who would become

02:15:02.000 --> 02:15:05.599
the king's Maha party, a powerful and

02:15:05.599 --> 02:15:08.000
influential position that combined

02:15:08.000 --> 02:15:10.880
elements of a prime minister and head

02:15:10.880 --> 02:15:13.599
general and essentially acted as the

02:15:13.599 --> 02:15:16.960
king's right hand.

02:15:16.960 --> 02:15:20.079
Whatever his skills as a diplomat, it

02:15:20.079 --> 02:15:22.560
seems Raden Vagaya struggled to manage

02:15:22.560 --> 02:15:25.199
the ambitions of the men who served

02:15:25.199 --> 02:15:27.360
under him.

02:15:27.360 --> 02:15:29.520
For this reason, he spent much of his

02:15:29.520 --> 02:15:32.400
rule putting down rebellions all over

02:15:32.400 --> 02:15:34.320
Java.

02:15:34.320 --> 02:15:37.040
In an effort to cement the legitimacy of

02:15:37.040 --> 02:15:39.599
his new dynasty, he would marry the

02:15:39.599 --> 02:15:41.760
remaining three daughters of his dead

02:15:41.760 --> 02:15:44.719
father-in-law, Curtenagara, and ensure

02:15:44.719 --> 02:15:47.520
that the royal line of succession would

02:15:47.520 --> 02:15:51.119
pass entirely through him. But still the

02:15:51.119 --> 02:15:54.239
problems persisted and the new kingdom

02:15:54.239 --> 02:15:59.320
teetered on the brink of destruction.

02:16:00.000 --> 02:16:04.400
When Raden Vagaya died in the year 1309,

02:16:04.400 --> 02:16:08.159
he must have hoped that his only son Ja

02:16:08.159 --> 02:16:11.199
would set things right.

02:16:11.199 --> 02:16:13.440
But due to the apparently deficient

02:16:13.440 --> 02:16:17.280
nature of Gygra's character, this would

02:16:17.280 --> 02:16:20.960
not be the case.

02:16:24.480 --> 02:16:27.440
King Gienegra would rule for nearly 20

02:16:27.440 --> 02:16:30.800
years after the death of his father. But

02:16:30.800 --> 02:16:34.399
he was a widely disliked character.

02:16:34.399 --> 02:16:36.319
So much so that the author of the

02:16:36.319 --> 02:16:39.439
chronicle the paraton would give him the

02:16:39.439 --> 02:16:44.160
nickname Kala Gt meaning weak villain.

02:16:44.160 --> 02:16:46.880
Meanwhile, the Javanese folk tradition

02:16:46.880 --> 02:16:49.200
has remembered him by the name Bajang

02:16:49.200 --> 02:16:53.120
Ratu or dwarf king, referencing either

02:16:53.120 --> 02:16:56.000
his short stature or simply the

02:16:56.000 --> 02:17:00.920
uninspiring nature of his rule.

02:17:01.200 --> 02:17:04.319
Gienegra faced multiple attempts on his

02:17:04.319 --> 02:17:07.599
life and widespread rebellions, even

02:17:07.599 --> 02:17:10.800
worse than his fathers. The most serious

02:17:10.800 --> 02:17:15.439
of which was led by a man named Kouti.

02:17:15.439 --> 02:17:18.160
This uprising became so dangerous that

02:17:18.160 --> 02:17:20.399
the king was forced to abandon his

02:17:20.399 --> 02:17:23.519
capital for a time. And it's during this

02:17:23.519 --> 02:17:26.880
time of upheaval that a man would walk

02:17:26.880 --> 02:17:30.080
onto the historical stage who would turn

02:17:30.080 --> 02:17:33.040
around the fortunes of this new and

02:17:33.040 --> 02:17:35.280
struggling kingdom.

02:17:35.280 --> 02:17:37.920
He was a soldier who led the king's

02:17:37.920 --> 02:17:41.200
bodyguard during the Couti rebellion and

02:17:41.200 --> 02:17:43.679
gained a position of trust in the royal

02:17:43.679 --> 02:17:45.359
court.

02:17:45.359 --> 02:17:50.519
His name was Gaja Mada.

02:17:56.559 --> 02:17:59.439
Gaja Mada's name came from the old

02:17:59.439 --> 02:18:03.920
Javanese word gaja meaning elephant and

02:18:03.920 --> 02:18:06.479
ma which is a difficult to translate

02:18:06.479 --> 02:18:09.519
word describing a state of furious

02:18:09.519 --> 02:18:11.439
intoxication.

02:18:11.439 --> 02:18:14.240
This probably alluded to the period of a

02:18:14.240 --> 02:18:17.519
few weeks every year when male elephants

02:18:17.519 --> 02:18:20.800
enter their breeding cycle called must

02:18:20.800 --> 02:18:25.599
and their testosterone levels explode.

02:18:25.599 --> 02:18:28.399
During this time, a bull elephant seeps

02:18:28.399 --> 02:18:31.679
liquid from a gland around its ears and

02:18:31.679 --> 02:18:34.080
becomes extremely aggressive and

02:18:34.080 --> 02:18:36.399
dangerous.

02:18:36.399 --> 02:18:39.280
Elephants had long been used for warfare

02:18:39.280 --> 02:18:42.639
in Java. They formed the centerpiece of

02:18:42.639 --> 02:18:46.000
any army and allowed royals and generals

02:18:46.000 --> 02:18:48.319
to command the battlefield from an

02:18:48.319 --> 02:18:51.760
elevated position.

02:18:51.760 --> 02:18:54.240
Although prehistoric fossils of native

02:18:54.240 --> 02:18:57.280
elephants have been found in Java, this

02:18:57.280 --> 02:18:59.760
species had long been extinct by this

02:18:59.760 --> 02:19:02.719
point. And during the medieval period,

02:19:02.719 --> 02:19:04.880
elephants were imported from other

02:19:04.880 --> 02:19:07.880
lands.

02:19:07.920 --> 02:19:10.639
They were enormous, expensive, and

02:19:10.639 --> 02:19:13.439
prestigious. Their tusks sometimes

02:19:13.439 --> 02:19:16.080
adorned with metal implements to make

02:19:16.080 --> 02:19:18.960
them even more deadly and their sides

02:19:18.960 --> 02:19:21.760
often oiled before going into battle to

02:19:21.760 --> 02:19:24.080
prevent the enemy from climbing on their

02:19:24.080 --> 02:19:26.080
backs.

02:19:26.080 --> 02:19:28.319
So this commander's name would have

02:19:28.319 --> 02:19:31.760
generated images of strength, vitality,

02:19:31.760 --> 02:19:35.599
and an unstoppable force. and by all

02:19:35.599 --> 02:19:40.519
accounts it would be a good fit.

02:19:43.280 --> 02:19:46.160
Although the elephant general Gaja Mada

02:19:46.160 --> 02:19:47.920
would eventually rise through the new

02:19:47.920 --> 02:19:50.479
kingdom of Majapahit to become one of

02:19:50.479 --> 02:19:53.280
its most influential statesmen, his

02:19:53.280 --> 02:19:57.040
birth was relatively unexceptional.

02:19:57.040 --> 02:19:59.840
We know little about his early life, but

02:19:59.840 --> 02:20:02.560
he was likely born into a poor family in

02:20:02.560 --> 02:20:06.080
the area around the city of Majapi, and

02:20:06.080 --> 02:20:08.560
his father was possibly killed in the

02:20:08.560 --> 02:20:11.760
war with the Mongols.

02:20:11.760 --> 02:20:14.720
But he would prove his worth and become

02:20:14.720 --> 02:20:16.960
the head of the king's elite royal

02:20:16.960 --> 02:20:20.399
bodyguard, the Bayara.

02:20:20.399 --> 02:20:22.560
After successfully protecting the king

02:20:22.560 --> 02:20:25.280
through the Kouti rebellion, Gajamada

02:20:25.280 --> 02:20:27.200
would be rewarded with the governorship

02:20:27.200 --> 02:20:29.680
of a small province.

02:20:29.680 --> 02:20:33.359
Finally, he would be named Maha Parti or

02:20:33.359 --> 02:20:37.880
the right hand of the king.

02:20:38.560 --> 02:20:42.240
The epic poem the Desha Varana describes

02:20:42.240 --> 02:20:44.720
this warrior statesman in the following

02:20:44.720 --> 02:20:47.720
terms.

02:20:52.640 --> 02:20:54.960
Gaja Mada is the excellent party of

02:20:54.960 --> 02:20:58.560
Maja, an officer valiant, discerning in

02:20:58.560 --> 02:21:00.640
tactics with a firm foundation in

02:21:00.640 --> 02:21:02.960
loyalty and devotion to the king.

02:21:02.960 --> 02:21:05.840
Eloquent and skilled in speech, polite

02:21:05.840 --> 02:21:08.399
and patient, constantly exerting

02:21:08.399 --> 02:21:11.520
himself, unremitting, he watches over

02:21:11.520 --> 02:21:13.840
the king's position as supreme ruler of

02:21:13.840 --> 02:21:17.000
the world.

02:21:23.200 --> 02:21:27.040
King Jane was clearly a man ills suited

02:21:27.040 --> 02:21:30.479
to rule. But with Gaja Mada's help, he

02:21:30.479 --> 02:21:33.040
was able to keep hold of his kingdom by

02:21:33.040 --> 02:21:35.840
his fingernails. And it's in the last

02:21:35.840 --> 02:21:38.720
decade of his reign that a visitor from

02:21:38.720 --> 02:21:42.240
a far off land arrived on the shores of

02:21:42.240 --> 02:21:44.880
Java.

02:21:44.880 --> 02:21:47.280
He was a traveler from the northern

02:21:47.280 --> 02:21:50.800
Italian region of Friulia, then a

02:21:50.800 --> 02:21:53.680
territory of the Holy Roman Empire. And

02:21:53.680 --> 02:21:59.080
his name was Odorich of Pordinon.

02:22:07.280 --> 02:22:10.160
Around the year 1318,

02:22:10.160 --> 02:22:13.359
Odorich had departed from Venice and

02:22:13.359 --> 02:22:15.920
spent the next decade or so traveling

02:22:15.920 --> 02:22:19.280
all over Asia, passing through Persia

02:22:19.280 --> 02:22:21.760
and seeing the ruins of the ancient city

02:22:21.760 --> 02:22:24.240
of Percepilus.

02:22:24.240 --> 02:22:26.399
He then sailed through the strait of

02:22:26.399 --> 02:22:29.680
Hormuz to India and from there through

02:22:29.680 --> 02:22:33.200
the straits of Malaca to Borneo, Sumatra

02:22:33.200 --> 02:22:36.319
and Java.

02:22:36.319 --> 02:22:38.880
When he returned home, he dictated the

02:22:38.880 --> 02:22:41.200
memoirs of his travels in a work

02:22:41.200 --> 02:22:44.720
entitled the relatio de miraabilus

02:22:44.720 --> 02:22:48.960
oriental tatarorum or the account of the

02:22:48.960 --> 02:22:52.560
marvels of the eastern tartas.

02:22:52.560 --> 02:22:55.120
In this text he provides a remarkable

02:22:55.120 --> 02:22:59.200
snapshot of life in Java around the year

02:22:59.200 --> 02:23:02.200
1320.

02:23:03.439 --> 02:23:07.120
There is an island which is called Java

02:23:07.120 --> 02:23:11.280
which is a good 3,000 mi around. The

02:23:11.280 --> 02:23:14.720
king of this island has under him seven

02:23:14.720 --> 02:23:18.399
crowned kings as vassels. This island is

02:23:18.399 --> 02:23:21.359
very populous and is the second best of

02:23:21.359 --> 02:23:24.880
all islands that be on the earth. One

02:23:24.880 --> 02:23:28.960
finds there cloves, pepper, nutmeg, and

02:23:28.960 --> 02:23:31.200
many other precious spices that they

02:23:31.200 --> 02:23:33.520
grind there and all manner of

02:23:33.520 --> 02:23:38.200
necessities in great quantity.

02:23:39.439 --> 02:23:41.920
Odric was particularly impressed by the

02:23:41.920 --> 02:23:44.800
royal palace of Geneagra which was

02:23:44.800 --> 02:23:48.080
richly decorated in gold mined from the

02:23:48.080 --> 02:23:52.040
volcanic mountain ranges.

02:23:52.319 --> 02:23:54.880
The king of this island lives in a

02:23:54.880 --> 02:23:58.080
marvelous and very large palace. Its

02:23:58.080 --> 02:24:00.319
steps are of gold and silver

02:24:00.319 --> 02:24:02.000
alternately.

02:24:02.000 --> 02:24:05.280
The paving tiles are likewise one gold

02:24:05.280 --> 02:24:08.319
and the next silver. The walls are

02:24:08.319 --> 02:24:11.439
covered with plates of gold and there

02:24:11.439 --> 02:24:14.560
are mounted men sculpted out of gold on

02:24:14.560 --> 02:24:16.960
them with golden circles around their

02:24:16.960 --> 02:24:19.760
heads like the diadems we make for the

02:24:19.760 --> 02:24:22.880
figures of saints. And these circles are

02:24:22.880 --> 02:24:25.600
full of precious stones. To put it

02:24:25.600 --> 02:24:28.560
briefly, this is the richest and

02:24:28.560 --> 02:24:31.120
loveliest palace that there be in the

02:24:31.120 --> 02:24:34.439
whole world.

02:24:35.439 --> 02:24:38.399
Odorich also records that many still

02:24:38.399 --> 02:24:40.880
remembered the war with the Mongol Yuan

02:24:40.880 --> 02:24:44.720
dynasty of China now nearly 30 years in

02:24:44.720 --> 02:24:47.960
the past.

02:24:48.000 --> 02:24:51.120
The great Khn of Cath who is the

02:24:51.120 --> 02:24:54.000
sovereign emperor of all the Tartas has

02:24:54.000 --> 02:24:56.960
often made war with this king and often

02:24:56.960 --> 02:24:59.840
brought battle to him. But this king has

02:24:59.840 --> 02:25:03.800
always defeated him.

02:25:04.319 --> 02:25:06.640
But despite the glowing report of

02:25:06.640 --> 02:25:09.439
Odorich and the ongoing help of the

02:25:09.439 --> 02:25:12.880
elephant general Gaja Mada, Jay Negra's

02:25:12.880 --> 02:25:17.399
reign was a poor one.

02:25:18.800 --> 02:25:21.840
He was so insecure in his rule that he

02:25:21.840 --> 02:25:24.000
at one point seems to have considered

02:25:24.000 --> 02:25:27.439
marrying two of his own sisters named

02:25:27.439 --> 02:25:31.600
Diar Wyatt and Diar Gitar to ensure that

02:25:31.600 --> 02:25:34.399
no rivals could arise from the royal

02:25:34.399 --> 02:25:36.560
line.

02:25:36.560 --> 02:25:39.520
When opposition to this plan exploded in

02:25:39.520 --> 02:25:42.160
the court and their mother loudly

02:25:42.160 --> 02:25:45.760
protested, King Jane gave up on this

02:25:45.760 --> 02:25:49.040
idea. But he still forbade his sisters

02:25:49.040 --> 02:25:53.640
from marrying anyone else.

02:25:59.760 --> 02:26:03.520
King Genegra had two sisters born of the

02:26:03.520 --> 02:26:05.120
same mother.

02:26:05.120 --> 02:26:07.040
He did not permit them to be married to

02:26:07.040 --> 02:26:09.200
others, wishing to keep them for

02:26:09.200 --> 02:26:10.960
himself.

02:26:10.960 --> 02:26:14.080
Therefore, no prince dared remain openly

02:26:14.080 --> 02:26:16.080
at Majapahit.

02:26:16.080 --> 02:26:19.439
Any man who appeared was driven away,

02:26:19.439 --> 02:26:22.319
lest he seek their hands, and the other

02:26:22.319 --> 02:26:28.120
nobles kept themselves hidden in fear.

02:26:29.760 --> 02:26:32.760
The

02:26:33.040 --> 02:26:36.160
>> Genegra confined these two princesses

02:26:36.160 --> 02:26:39.040
for years in the women's quarters of the

02:26:39.040 --> 02:26:42.240
palace and prevented anyone from seeing

02:26:42.240 --> 02:26:44.399
them.

02:26:44.399 --> 02:26:47.840
It was a microcosm of a rule that seems

02:26:47.840 --> 02:26:50.880
to have been at every turn paranoid,

02:26:50.880 --> 02:26:55.160
petty, and authoritarian.

02:26:55.680 --> 02:26:57.520
Over the course of his reign, the

02:26:57.520 --> 02:27:01.840
kingdom of Majapahit would falter.

02:27:01.840 --> 02:27:05.040
The island of Bali, just a short hop

02:27:05.040 --> 02:27:07.600
over the Sunda Strait, slipped out of

02:27:07.600 --> 02:27:10.720
his control around this time. And people

02:27:10.720 --> 02:27:13.120
must have feared that the whole kingdom

02:27:13.120 --> 02:27:15.920
would now disintegrate and the land

02:27:15.920 --> 02:27:20.880
would return to destructive civil war.

02:27:20.880 --> 02:27:24.640
But that was not to be the case.

02:27:24.640 --> 02:27:27.439
That's because of a woman who had made

02:27:27.439 --> 02:27:31.760
her name standing up to King Gygra,

02:27:31.760 --> 02:27:33.840
the mother of the two imprisoned

02:27:33.840 --> 02:27:35.600
princesses.

02:27:35.600 --> 02:27:40.680
A woman named Dia Guyatry.

02:27:53.359 --> 02:27:57.439
>> Diar was a title that in old Javanese

02:27:57.439 --> 02:28:00.240
was given to princes and princesses of

02:28:00.240 --> 02:28:04.319
the royal line. And diaratri had been

02:28:04.319 --> 02:28:06.080
the youngest daughter of king

02:28:06.080 --> 02:28:11.280
kertonagara the last king of singari.

02:28:11.280 --> 02:28:13.840
She had also been the most senior wife

02:28:13.840 --> 02:28:18.000
of the founder of Majaet Raden Vagaya

02:28:18.000 --> 02:28:20.640
and all her life she had been a quiet

02:28:20.640 --> 02:28:23.520
force behind the lives of these great

02:28:23.520 --> 02:28:25.680
men.

02:28:25.680 --> 02:28:28.080
As a girl, she had watched her father

02:28:28.080 --> 02:28:31.280
brand the face of the Mongol envoys and

02:28:31.280 --> 02:28:34.080
then saw her home of Singer Sari

02:28:34.080 --> 02:28:38.399
destroyed by the rebellion of Ja Katang.

02:28:38.399 --> 02:28:40.720
She had fled through the rice fields to

02:28:40.720 --> 02:28:46.399
safety while her home burned behind her.

02:28:46.399 --> 02:28:48.240
As a young woman, she had watched the

02:28:48.240 --> 02:28:51.600
war with the Mongols unfold, then seen

02:28:51.600 --> 02:28:53.760
her husband found the kingdom of

02:28:53.760 --> 02:28:56.880
Majapahit, which now stood as his

02:28:56.880 --> 02:28:59.200
lasting legacy.

02:28:59.200 --> 02:29:02.560
By now, she was a widow in her 50s and

02:29:02.560 --> 02:29:05.600
had retired to become a Buddhist nun in

02:29:05.600 --> 02:29:08.080
a forest monastery on the slope of a

02:29:08.080 --> 02:29:11.520
nearby mountain. But she was still known

02:29:11.520 --> 02:29:15.120
by the title Raja Putney, a word which

02:29:15.120 --> 02:29:18.720
means wife of kings and which gave her

02:29:18.720 --> 02:29:23.960
the prestige of a royal matriarch.

02:29:24.000 --> 02:29:28.080
The bumbling king Gienegra was her late

02:29:28.080 --> 02:29:31.280
husband's son by another less senior

02:29:31.280 --> 02:29:34.960
wife. And we can only imagine how Diar

02:29:34.960 --> 02:29:38.160
Guyatri felt now watching from her

02:29:38.160 --> 02:29:41.120
monastery as he veered the empire from

02:29:41.120 --> 02:29:44.319
crisis to crisis and kept her two

02:29:44.319 --> 02:29:49.040
daughters under lock and key.

02:29:49.040 --> 02:29:51.280
She must have feared that the legacy

02:29:51.280 --> 02:29:54.399
that she and Raden Vaga had built was

02:29:54.399 --> 02:29:57.120
about to be destroyed.

02:29:57.120 --> 02:30:02.399
But she refused to let that happen.

02:30:02.399 --> 02:30:05.439
to help her free her daughters, reclaim

02:30:05.439 --> 02:30:08.720
the kingdom, and put it back on course.

02:30:08.720 --> 02:30:11.040
This royal matriarch would enlist the

02:30:11.040 --> 02:30:13.760
help of the man who had recently been

02:30:13.760 --> 02:30:16.479
rising in prominence in the kingdom of

02:30:16.479 --> 02:30:18.479
Majapet.

02:30:18.479 --> 02:30:20.880
The raging elephant who had become

02:30:20.880 --> 02:30:24.560
indispensable to the feckless king.

02:30:24.560 --> 02:30:27.200
The soldier and statesman who went by

02:30:27.200 --> 02:30:30.960
the name Gaja Mada.

02:30:30.960 --> 02:30:33.439
In the year 1328,

02:30:33.439 --> 02:30:36.960
it seems they took their chance.

02:30:36.960 --> 02:30:39.960
According

02:30:44.720 --> 02:30:47.120
to the official story related in the

02:30:47.120 --> 02:30:50.880
royal chronicle, the paraton, that year,

02:30:50.880 --> 02:30:53.359
King Gienegra was suffering from an

02:30:53.359 --> 02:30:56.720
unpleasant condition, a painful boil or

02:30:56.720 --> 02:30:59.680
swelling of some kind. And when he

02:30:59.680 --> 02:31:03.040
summoned his doctor, a man named Tanka,

02:31:03.040 --> 02:31:04.960
he apparently forgot that he had

02:31:04.960 --> 02:31:08.160
previously insulted or taken advantage

02:31:08.160 --> 02:31:11.280
of this man's wife.

02:31:11.280 --> 02:31:14.720
Enraged at this, the doctor Tanka took

02:31:14.720 --> 02:31:20.920
his revenge. As the paraton records,

02:31:26.960 --> 02:31:29.680
Tanka's wife spread word that the king

02:31:29.680 --> 02:31:33.200
had treated her dishonorably.

02:31:33.200 --> 02:31:36.800
Tanka was summoned before Gaja.

02:31:36.800 --> 02:31:40.399
At that time, King Genegra was suffering

02:31:40.399 --> 02:31:42.880
from a swelling and could not leave his

02:31:42.880 --> 02:31:44.640
chambers.

02:31:44.640 --> 02:31:46.399
Tanka was ordered to perform an

02:31:46.399 --> 02:31:49.040
operation with a sharp lancet and he

02:31:49.040 --> 02:31:52.080
approached beside the royal bed.

02:31:52.080 --> 02:31:54.720
Tanka stabbed the king's boil once, then

02:31:54.720 --> 02:31:57.040
again with the blade, but the weapon

02:31:57.040 --> 02:31:59.760
would not burst it for the king wore

02:31:59.760 --> 02:32:04.160
around his neck an amulet of protection.

02:32:04.160 --> 02:32:06.800
Then the king was asked to set this

02:32:06.800 --> 02:32:08.560
aside.

02:32:08.560 --> 02:32:11.200
He took off the charm and laid it beside

02:32:11.200 --> 02:32:13.040
the bed.

02:32:13.040 --> 02:32:16.240
Tanka stabbed him again and this time

02:32:16.240 --> 02:32:19.120
the blade burst the boil,

02:32:19.120 --> 02:32:22.080
but Tanka continued stabbing him and he

02:32:22.080 --> 02:32:24.800
did not stop until the king died there

02:32:24.800 --> 02:32:28.359
upon the bed.

02:32:39.600 --> 02:32:43.040
The doctor turned assassin Tanka was

02:32:43.040 --> 02:32:46.479
swiftly killed by Gaja Mada which meant

02:32:46.479 --> 02:32:49.040
perhaps conveniently that his side of

02:32:49.040 --> 02:32:52.720
the story could never be told.

02:32:52.720 --> 02:32:55.439
As historians, we can never actually

02:32:55.439 --> 02:32:58.560
know what happened in that room. But the

02:32:58.560 --> 02:33:01.280
slightly fanciful story involving a

02:33:01.280 --> 02:33:04.560
magical amulet and a vengeful doctor has

02:33:04.560 --> 02:33:07.120
left many historians wondering if the

02:33:07.120 --> 02:33:10.800
true story wasn't a simpler one that

02:33:10.800 --> 02:33:14.880
Gajamada and the Daaja queen Dariatry

02:33:14.880 --> 02:33:17.680
had simply plotted together to kill the

02:33:17.680 --> 02:33:23.000
king framing the poor doctor.

02:33:23.040 --> 02:33:25.600
Whether they had planned the whole thing

02:33:25.600 --> 02:33:28.240
or just seized the opportunity on a

02:33:28.240 --> 02:33:31.359
stroke of good luck, Gajamada and the

02:33:31.359 --> 02:33:34.160
Daaja matriarch Diaratri

02:33:34.160 --> 02:33:37.840
went on to seize control of the kingdom.

02:33:37.840 --> 02:33:40.479
And it seems King Genegra was

02:33:40.479 --> 02:33:43.600
sufficiently disliked that few people

02:33:43.600 --> 02:33:46.479
were all that concerned about what might

02:33:46.479 --> 02:33:49.920
actually have happened to him.

02:33:49.920 --> 02:33:53.280
But the royal matriarch and the general

02:33:53.280 --> 02:33:57.520
prime minister faced a problem.

02:33:57.520 --> 02:34:00.479
Gaja Mada himself had risen from humble

02:34:00.479 --> 02:34:03.280
beginnings. And as a commoner, he had

02:34:03.280 --> 02:34:06.000
absolutely no legitimacy to rule under

02:34:06.000 --> 02:34:10.080
Javanese law. And while Dioratri was

02:34:10.080 --> 02:34:12.000
officially the next in line to the

02:34:12.000 --> 02:34:15.120
throne, she had already taken a vow to

02:34:15.120 --> 02:34:18.080
become a Buddhist nun, a position that

02:34:18.080 --> 02:34:20.640
prevented her from holding any positions

02:34:20.640 --> 02:34:23.200
of earthly power.

02:34:23.200 --> 02:34:26.399
And she had no sons who might take the

02:34:26.399 --> 02:34:28.880
throne.

02:34:28.880 --> 02:34:31.200
In fact, the histories record that she

02:34:31.200 --> 02:34:33.280
had only given birth to her two

02:34:33.280 --> 02:34:34.800
daughters

02:34:34.800 --> 02:34:37.520
who were now allowed to leave the palace

02:34:37.520 --> 02:34:41.359
for the first time in years.

02:34:41.359 --> 02:34:44.319
The Desha Varana describes these women

02:34:44.319 --> 02:34:49.240
in conventionally poetic terms.

02:34:54.080 --> 02:34:56.720
And then the king giant Nagara was left

02:34:56.720 --> 02:34:59.760
behind as king of Maja with his

02:34:59.760 --> 02:35:02.399
princesses his youngest sisters who were

02:35:02.399 --> 02:35:05.359
the daughters of the worthy Raja Patney

02:35:05.359 --> 02:35:07.439
the incomparable.

02:35:07.439 --> 02:35:09.520
They were both of the greatest beauty

02:35:09.520 --> 02:35:12.080
surpassing the women of heaven. The

02:35:12.080 --> 02:35:14.080
elder was princess of Jana and the

02:35:14.080 --> 02:35:18.600
younger ruled as princess of Da.

02:35:25.200 --> 02:35:28.160
The Raja

02:35:28.160 --> 02:35:31.200
soon appointed her young daughter Diar

02:35:31.200 --> 02:35:37.399
Git to rule as queen in her place.

02:35:40.880 --> 02:35:44.000
Verily in the shaka year moon arrows two

02:35:44.000 --> 02:35:47.280
form the princess of jwana succeeded in

02:35:47.280 --> 02:35:49.920
maja pahit as queen. It was the

02:35:49.920 --> 02:35:52.319
disposition of the great raja patney

02:35:52.319 --> 02:35:54.240
that she should be the auspicious leader

02:35:54.240 --> 02:35:57.520
of the world distinguished from others.

02:35:57.520 --> 02:35:59.200
It was she who made her ruler and

02:35:59.200 --> 02:36:03.399
watched over all her affairs.

02:36:09.760 --> 02:36:13.280
The princess soon took to the throne and

02:36:13.280 --> 02:36:16.080
with her mother watching over her, she

02:36:16.080 --> 02:36:18.800
would be a far more capable ruler than

02:36:18.800 --> 02:36:22.640
her feckless brother.

02:36:22.640 --> 02:36:25.520
She would take a royal name that meant

02:36:25.520 --> 02:36:28.720
the exalted goddess of the three worlds

02:36:28.720 --> 02:36:32.080
who the glory of Vishnu radiates.

02:36:32.080 --> 02:36:36.760
Tribuana vija tuna

02:36:45.680 --> 02:36:49.359
tribuana was her mother's daughter. She

02:36:49.359 --> 02:36:51.760
was a natural stateswoman and was able

02:36:51.760 --> 02:36:53.920
to stabilize the kingdom after the

02:36:53.920 --> 02:36:56.000
period of poor leadership that had

02:36:56.000 --> 02:36:58.160
preceded her.

02:36:58.160 --> 02:37:00.080
and she seems to have learned from the

02:37:00.080 --> 02:37:03.840
mistakes of both her father and brother.

02:37:03.840 --> 02:37:05.840
Early in her reign, she faced a

02:37:05.840 --> 02:37:09.120
rebellion by two men named Sardang and

02:37:09.120 --> 02:37:12.800
Keta, and a conflict arose in her court

02:37:12.800 --> 02:37:15.040
over which of her generals would lead

02:37:15.040 --> 02:37:18.080
her army into battle.

02:37:18.080 --> 02:37:20.560
These kinds of political disputes had

02:37:20.560 --> 02:37:24.880
plagued the last two kings, but Tribuana

02:37:24.880 --> 02:37:28.560
resolved it in a simple way.

02:37:28.560 --> 02:37:30.880
Rather than show favor to one general

02:37:30.880 --> 02:37:33.840
over the other, she simply led the army

02:37:33.840 --> 02:37:39.720
herself. As the desana describes

02:37:45.200 --> 02:37:48.720
in Shaka fire's arrow sons, their

02:37:48.720 --> 02:37:51.600
enemies were destroyed. Sadeng and Kita

02:37:51.600 --> 02:37:54.000
were defeated, overcome by her personal

02:37:54.000 --> 02:37:57.040
retinue. Further in the Shaka year,

02:37:57.040 --> 02:38:00.080
arrows, seasons, eyes, naval. The king

02:38:00.080 --> 02:38:02.560
of Bali was evil and base. He was

02:38:02.560 --> 02:38:04.720
attacked with an army, broken and

02:38:04.720 --> 02:38:07.280
completely crushed. Every kind of

02:38:07.280 --> 02:38:09.760
evildoer was fearful and made off

02:38:09.760 --> 02:38:12.760
quickly.

02:38:18.240 --> 02:38:20.880
Tribuana's early successes on the

02:38:20.880 --> 02:38:23.600
battlefield gave her a taste for

02:38:23.600 --> 02:38:25.120
conquest.

02:38:25.120 --> 02:38:28.000
And over her rule, this queen of Java

02:38:28.000 --> 02:38:31.040
would embark on a massive expansion of

02:38:31.040 --> 02:38:32.560
Majapahit

02:38:32.560 --> 02:38:35.680
to spread its influence all over the

02:38:35.680 --> 02:38:38.680
archipelago.

02:38:38.800 --> 02:38:41.520
To embark on this mission, she appointed

02:38:41.520 --> 02:38:44.960
as her Maha Party or prime minister the

02:38:44.960 --> 02:38:47.200
general who had done more than perhaps

02:38:47.200 --> 02:38:50.000
anyone else to keep the young kingdom

02:38:50.000 --> 02:38:52.640
together and who had worked with her

02:38:52.640 --> 02:38:56.399
mother to depose the previous king.

02:38:56.399 --> 02:38:59.840
This was the rampaging elephant himself,

02:38:59.840 --> 02:39:03.319
Gaja Mada.

02:39:05.520 --> 02:39:08.800
By all accounts, Gajamada rose to this

02:39:08.800 --> 02:39:10.560
challenge.

02:39:10.560 --> 02:39:13.439
Spurred on by his warlike queen, the

02:39:13.439 --> 02:39:16.160
Paraton records him swearing a

02:39:16.160 --> 02:39:19.280
remarkable oath of conquest before the

02:39:19.280 --> 02:39:23.399
entire royal court.

02:39:25.520 --> 02:39:29.120
Gaja Mada swore, "Until I have conquered

02:39:29.120 --> 02:39:32.960
the entire Nusantara archipelago, I will

02:39:32.960 --> 02:39:36.960
eat no spices nor take any rest. If I

02:39:36.960 --> 02:39:39.200
have conquered the Gorum Islands and the

02:39:39.200 --> 02:39:42.399
island of Saram, the kingdom of Tanjang

02:39:42.399 --> 02:39:46.080
Pura, the kingdoms of Haru and Pahang,

02:39:46.080 --> 02:39:50.240
the Don Pu regency, the island of Bali,

02:39:50.240 --> 02:39:53.600
the lands of Sunda along with the Tumi

02:39:53.600 --> 02:39:57.280
and Palem Bang of Sumatra. Then and only

02:39:57.280 --> 02:40:03.439
then will I eat spices and take my rest.

02:40:03.439 --> 02:40:06.439
Over

02:40:06.479 --> 02:40:09.600
the next three decades, Gaja would lead

02:40:09.600 --> 02:40:13.520
the armies of Majapit across the seas

02:40:13.520 --> 02:40:16.080
and would bring ever more lands under

02:40:16.080 --> 02:40:20.160
the influence and control of the empire.

02:40:20.160 --> 02:40:23.760
The Italian traveler Ludovviko Deva

02:40:23.760 --> 02:40:26.080
describes the weapons of the Javanese

02:40:26.080 --> 02:40:28.640
that he saw when he visited sometime

02:40:28.640 --> 02:40:32.880
later around 1505.

02:40:32.880 --> 02:40:35.040
They carry bows and the greater part

02:40:35.040 --> 02:40:38.160
darts of cane. Some also use blowpipes

02:40:38.160 --> 02:40:40.560
with which they throw poison darts and

02:40:40.560 --> 02:40:42.399
they throw them with the mouth and

02:40:42.399 --> 02:40:44.479
however little they draw blood, the

02:40:44.479 --> 02:40:47.760
wounded person dies.

02:40:47.760 --> 02:40:50.640
The 12th century Javanese poem, the

02:40:50.640 --> 02:40:54.399
Bulman Taka, describes an idealized army

02:40:54.399 --> 02:40:57.600
marching to battle and gives a sense for

02:40:57.600 --> 02:40:59.520
what it would have been like to see the

02:40:59.520 --> 02:41:02.880
forces of Gajamada landing on the shores

02:41:02.880 --> 02:41:06.479
of each island in turn and preparing for

02:41:06.479 --> 02:41:09.479
war.

02:41:10.000 --> 02:41:12.880
Their weapons were spears and lances,

02:41:12.880 --> 02:41:16.240
and there were also thousands of bows.

02:41:16.240 --> 02:41:18.880
Then came the riding elephants, and

02:41:18.880 --> 02:41:21.280
their weapons were spears, lances,

02:41:21.280 --> 02:41:24.319
javelins, and clubs. Many heroes were

02:41:24.319 --> 02:41:27.280
mounted on horses. Skilled riders in

02:41:27.280 --> 02:41:30.399
horseback combat. The spears and very

02:41:30.399 --> 02:41:32.640
sharp knives when worldled glowed

02:41:32.640 --> 02:41:35.920
brightly. Men came bearing lances and

02:41:35.920 --> 02:41:38.880
shields, and others with slingshots.

02:41:38.880 --> 02:41:42.080
Their casings shone, wrapped in silk and

02:41:42.080 --> 02:41:44.880
gilded, and their various jackets were

02:41:44.880 --> 02:41:49.800
like clouds traveling over the earth.

02:41:55.359 --> 02:41:59.439
The Majapet forces of Queen Tribuana

02:41:59.439 --> 02:42:02.240
Vijay Tungadevi crossed the sea to the

02:42:02.240 --> 02:42:05.200
east and reconquered the small island of

02:42:05.200 --> 02:42:09.120
Bali in 1343.

02:42:09.120 --> 02:42:12.000
After that they went northwest and

02:42:12.000 --> 02:42:14.640
absorbed most of the coastal regions of

02:42:14.640 --> 02:42:17.680
the larger island of Sumatra into her

02:42:17.680 --> 02:42:20.880
growing empire.

02:42:20.880 --> 02:42:23.040
Other kingdoms were incorporated

02:42:23.040 --> 02:42:26.000
peacefully into the empire as tributary

02:42:26.000 --> 02:42:29.040
subjects such as the large island of

02:42:29.040 --> 02:42:32.880
Sulai whose name means iron island on

02:42:32.880 --> 02:42:35.359
account of the high quality iron it

02:42:35.359 --> 02:42:40.760
produced and exported around the region.

02:42:42.080 --> 02:42:45.359
The later poem, the Desha Varna, lists

02:42:45.359 --> 02:42:48.240
at length all of the island territories

02:42:48.240 --> 02:42:51.200
that were either conquered by Maja Pahit

02:42:51.200 --> 02:42:54.080
or agreed to pay it tribute without a

02:42:54.080 --> 02:42:57.080
fight.

02:42:57.439 --> 02:42:59.520
The islands and lesser islands in the

02:42:59.520 --> 02:43:01.040
first place coming under the territory

02:43:01.040 --> 02:43:03.600
of the Malay islands are Jambi and

02:43:03.600 --> 02:43:07.439
Palamang, Keritang, Tiba and Dharmasa.

02:43:07.439 --> 02:43:11.600
Following Candice, Kawas, Manang, Kabwa,

02:43:11.600 --> 02:43:16.080
Sak, Rekan, Campa and Pane, Campe, Haru

02:43:16.080 --> 02:43:19.280
and Mandahiling, Tumihang, Pac and

02:43:19.280 --> 02:43:21.840
Barat, Luas and Samudra, as well as

02:43:21.840 --> 02:43:24.880
Lamuri, Batan, Lampong and Barus. Those

02:43:24.880 --> 02:43:26.479
are the main ones among the Malay

02:43:26.479 --> 02:43:29.120
islands. All these countries are subject

02:43:29.120 --> 02:43:32.359
and obedient.

02:43:33.760 --> 02:43:37.200
The great queen Tribuana Vijay Tungadevi

02:43:37.200 --> 02:43:41.040
would rule for 22 years and her reign

02:43:41.040 --> 02:43:45.920
saw the rise of Majapay to a true

02:43:45.920 --> 02:43:50.760
or an empire of the sea.

02:43:51.840 --> 02:43:54.240
But she must have known that her reign

02:43:54.240 --> 02:43:58.279
couldn't last forever.

02:44:08.960 --> 02:44:12.800
In 1350, her mother, the great royal

02:44:12.800 --> 02:44:17.120
matriarch Diar Guyry died, most likely

02:44:17.120 --> 02:44:20.560
in her forest monastery after a long and

02:44:20.560 --> 02:44:25.760
accomplished life. Her daughter Tribuana

02:44:25.760 --> 02:44:28.479
had been ruling ostensibly on behalf of

02:44:28.479 --> 02:44:31.439
her mother, and it seems that once the

02:44:31.439 --> 02:44:35.040
old woman died, her situation would also

02:44:35.040 --> 02:44:38.000
become untenable.

02:44:38.000 --> 02:44:41.200
But luckily, by this time she had had a

02:44:41.200 --> 02:44:44.080
son who was now the first in the royal

02:44:44.080 --> 02:44:48.560
line, and he had just come of age at 16

02:44:48.560 --> 02:44:56.040
years old. His name was Hyam Wuruk.

02:45:00.080 --> 02:45:02.960
When this young prince Hayam Wuruk came

02:45:02.960 --> 02:45:04.960
to the throne, he would have been

02:45:04.960 --> 02:45:07.840
crowned with enormous ceremony and

02:45:07.840 --> 02:45:10.000
celebration.

02:45:10.000 --> 02:45:12.720
The historian Herald Vanderinda

02:45:12.720 --> 02:45:16.000
describes the rituals associated with a

02:45:16.000 --> 02:45:19.800
Javanese coronation.

02:45:20.080 --> 02:45:22.800
At sunset on the eve of the first day of

02:45:22.800 --> 02:45:25.439
the first month of the year, priests

02:45:25.439 --> 02:45:27.520
entered the inner pavilion of the royal

02:45:27.520 --> 02:45:30.399
palace followed by acolytes chanting

02:45:30.399 --> 02:45:34.240
sacred Sanskrit texts. King Haim Wuruk

02:45:34.240 --> 02:45:37.120
sat on a throne in the amazing pavilion

02:45:37.120 --> 02:45:40.000
where mattedhaired rishi hermits and

02:45:40.000 --> 02:45:42.880
religious leaders sprinkled holy water

02:45:42.880 --> 02:45:45.760
over him to wash away the evils of the

02:45:45.760 --> 02:45:49.680
past. As darkness descended, oil lamps

02:45:49.680 --> 02:45:51.920
were lit around the palace. A

02:45:51.920 --> 02:45:54.640
spectacular sight.

02:45:54.640 --> 02:45:58.319
At the striking of a gong, Gaja Mada led

02:45:58.319 --> 02:46:00.960
the senior ministers to a large pavilion

02:46:00.960 --> 02:46:03.359
in front of the palace gates before a

02:46:03.359 --> 02:46:06.760
growing crowd.

02:46:12.800 --> 02:46:16.800
Hayamuruk was a multi-talented king.

02:46:16.800 --> 02:46:19.200
He was apparently an accomplished singer

02:46:19.200 --> 02:46:22.640
and dancer and a lover of shadow puppet

02:46:22.640 --> 02:46:24.319
plays.

02:46:24.319 --> 02:46:27.359
The poet of the Desha Wanana describes

02:46:27.359 --> 02:46:29.840
the auspicious omens that took place

02:46:29.840 --> 02:46:32.800
upon the birth of this prince as the

02:46:32.800 --> 02:46:35.760
island's great volcanoes rumbled their

02:46:35.760 --> 02:46:38.760
approval.

02:46:39.200 --> 02:46:42.000
At his birth in the Shaki year, season's

02:46:42.000 --> 02:46:44.479
arrow sons, the prince was already

02:46:44.479 --> 02:46:46.240
destined to be king.

02:46:46.240 --> 02:46:48.000
The signs of his miraculous and

02:46:48.000 --> 02:46:50.080
extraordinary nature were that the earth

02:46:50.080 --> 02:46:52.560
quaked and rumbled. There was a rain of

02:46:52.560 --> 02:46:55.120
ash. Thunder and lightning zigzagged

02:46:55.120 --> 02:46:57.680
through the sky. Mount Kampud erupted

02:46:57.680 --> 02:46:59.840
and the wretched evildoers around it

02:46:59.840 --> 02:47:01.760
were annihilated and died without a

02:47:01.760 --> 02:47:04.960
gasp. Such is the nature of his reign

02:47:04.960 --> 02:47:07.279
that the whole of the land of Java has

02:47:07.279 --> 02:47:09.120
been humbled and bows down in

02:47:09.120 --> 02:47:12.120
submission.

02:47:13.600 --> 02:47:16.399
Like her mother before her, Tribuana did

02:47:16.399 --> 02:47:18.560
not completely vanish from political

02:47:18.560 --> 02:47:20.640
life when she stepped away from her

02:47:20.640 --> 02:47:22.319
throne.

02:47:22.319 --> 02:47:24.479
Throughout the rest of her life, she

02:47:24.479 --> 02:47:27.200
would act as a counselor and advisor for

02:47:27.200 --> 02:47:30.319
her son, and together they would usher

02:47:30.319 --> 02:47:33.359
in what is widely regarded as the golden

02:47:33.359 --> 02:47:38.520
age of the empire of Majapet.

02:47:38.880 --> 02:47:42.080
When Hyam Wooduk came to the throne, he

02:47:42.080 --> 02:47:45.200
inherited a capital city of no little

02:47:45.200 --> 02:47:47.680
magnificence.

02:47:47.680 --> 02:47:50.160
Over the preceding decades, it had been

02:47:50.160 --> 02:47:52.960
the site of constant construction and

02:47:52.960 --> 02:47:56.080
now bloomed with palaces and temples

02:47:56.080 --> 02:47:58.720
complete with pillared audience halls

02:47:58.720 --> 02:48:00.800
and pavilions.

02:48:00.800 --> 02:48:04.720
In this era, all roads led to Majapahit

02:48:04.720 --> 02:48:07.520
and its status as a crossroads of Java

02:48:07.520 --> 02:48:10.479
wasn't just a metaphor.

02:48:10.479 --> 02:48:14.160
The epic poem Desa Vanana describes the

02:48:14.160 --> 02:48:17.560
royal palace.

02:48:18.560 --> 02:48:20.479
Let us describe the layout of the all

02:48:20.479 --> 02:48:23.359
inspiring royal palace. Its wall is of

02:48:23.359 --> 02:48:25.760
red brick. It goes right around and is

02:48:25.760 --> 02:48:28.399
thick and high. On the western side, the

02:48:28.399 --> 02:48:30.720
palace mouth faces onto the great square

02:48:30.720 --> 02:48:32.880
in the midst of deep encircling with

02:48:32.880 --> 02:48:35.359
booty trees in rows and neatly shaped,

02:48:35.359 --> 02:48:38.399
all thick with festoons. On the north is

02:48:38.399 --> 02:48:40.720
the ceremonial gate, splendid and

02:48:40.720 --> 02:48:43.600
extraordinary. Its doors of iron adorned

02:48:43.600 --> 02:48:46.240
with countless designs. To the south of

02:48:46.240 --> 02:48:48.960
this is the crossroads, otherworldly in

02:48:48.960 --> 02:48:52.120
its elegance.

02:48:53.359 --> 02:48:56.880
From these crossroads, great highways

02:48:56.880 --> 02:48:59.600
snaked off into the country in all

02:48:59.600 --> 02:49:01.760
directions.

02:49:01.760 --> 02:49:04.240
It was part of the usual ceremony of

02:49:04.240 --> 02:49:07.120
kingship that the king of Majapahit

02:49:07.120 --> 02:49:09.760
would routinely make journeys around the

02:49:09.760 --> 02:49:13.840
whole of Java, meeting his citizens and

02:49:13.840 --> 02:49:17.120
seeing the sites of the land, visiting

02:49:17.120 --> 02:49:21.040
villages, holy shrines, and reminding

02:49:21.040 --> 02:49:26.560
vassal kingdoms about who was in charge.

02:49:26.560 --> 02:49:29.680
It was on one of these journeys that

02:49:29.680 --> 02:49:33.840
King Hayam Wuruk brought his court poet,

02:49:33.840 --> 02:49:37.279
a man named Propanka who would go on to

02:49:37.279 --> 02:49:41.920
be the author of the poem Desavanana.

02:49:41.920 --> 02:49:45.840
Propanka speaks of the honor in his poem

02:49:45.840 --> 02:49:50.160
describing himself in the third person.

02:49:50.160 --> 02:49:53.040
In the Shaka moon snake son in the month

02:49:53.040 --> 02:49:55.359
of Badra Pada at the fullness of the

02:49:55.359 --> 02:49:58.080
moon, King Hayamuruk went on a journey

02:49:58.080 --> 02:50:00.720
to Lama to take note of all there was to

02:50:00.720 --> 02:50:03.600
see. All the princes of Java with their

02:50:03.600 --> 02:50:05.920
wives again went with the king with

02:50:05.920 --> 02:50:08.399
servants and vehicles. Officials and

02:50:08.399 --> 02:50:10.960
officers from the whole of Majapahit and

02:50:10.960 --> 02:50:12.640
in particular the king's priests and

02:50:12.640 --> 02:50:15.279
court poets accompanied him. So this man

02:50:15.279 --> 02:50:17.600
by the pen name of Propanka joined in

02:50:17.600 --> 02:50:19.680
the pursuit of beauty attending at the

02:50:19.680 --> 02:50:23.160
feet of the king.

02:50:24.319 --> 02:50:27.120
According to his own account, Propanka

02:50:27.120 --> 02:50:29.520
seems to have embarked on writing the

02:50:29.520 --> 02:50:32.880
desana because he felt unable to write

02:50:32.880 --> 02:50:35.680
the kind of poetry that the more senior

02:50:35.680 --> 02:50:38.720
court poets were producing.

02:50:38.720 --> 02:50:41.520
usually heroic epics about the Hindu

02:50:41.520 --> 02:50:44.800
gods as he describes in the following

02:50:44.800 --> 02:50:47.800
extract.

02:50:47.920 --> 02:50:50.000
His motive was after all to follow the

02:50:50.000 --> 02:50:51.920
king wherever he went in the hope of

02:50:51.920 --> 02:50:53.920
being favored. But he still does not

02:50:53.920 --> 02:50:56.240
know how to achieve poetic effects and

02:50:56.240 --> 02:50:58.319
is most unlikely to succeed in composing

02:50:58.319 --> 02:51:01.040
a song on the writing tablet. And this

02:51:01.040 --> 02:51:02.720
is the reason why he describes all the

02:51:02.720 --> 02:51:04.880
places passed through and sets out their

02:51:04.880 --> 02:51:09.160
names in order along the road.

02:51:10.000 --> 02:51:13.200
Ironically, the Dash of Varna is today

02:51:13.200 --> 02:51:15.040
one of the most famous pieces of

02:51:15.040 --> 02:51:18.240
literature to survive from the Javanese

02:51:18.240 --> 02:51:21.200
golden era and it is by far the most

02:51:21.200 --> 02:51:24.399
useful to historians.

02:51:24.399 --> 02:51:27.279
Today, the poem is a remarkable source

02:51:27.279 --> 02:51:30.800
that captures a snapshot of life on Java

02:51:30.800 --> 02:51:34.080
during the reign of Hyam Wuruk. And for

02:51:34.080 --> 02:51:37.200
all of this, we have the poet Propanka's

02:51:37.200 --> 02:51:42.160
apparent inferiority complex to thank.

02:51:42.160 --> 02:51:44.880
Along their journey, Propanka watched

02:51:44.880 --> 02:51:47.920
the king carefully and noted down the

02:51:47.920 --> 02:51:52.399
beauty of the land they passed through.

02:51:52.399 --> 02:51:55.439
At Dampar and at Patanjungan, the king

02:51:55.439 --> 02:51:57.279
relaxed and made his way along the

02:51:57.279 --> 02:51:59.600
beach. To the east his path followed the

02:51:59.600 --> 02:52:01.760
level sands, which was so firm that the

02:52:01.760 --> 02:52:03.920
carriages could drive over them. He made

02:52:03.920 --> 02:52:06.000
a halt on the banks of a lake thick with

02:52:06.000 --> 02:52:08.479
white and red lotuses in flour, and was

02:52:08.479 --> 02:52:10.319
absorbed in watching the giant shrimps

02:52:10.319 --> 02:52:12.240
moving about in the limpid water,

02:52:12.240 --> 02:52:16.080
clearly visible in the depths.

02:52:16.080 --> 02:52:18.800
But the royal journey wasn't always an

02:52:18.800 --> 02:52:22.040
easy one.

02:52:23.359 --> 02:52:26.000
In his text, we get a sense for the

02:52:26.000 --> 02:52:28.960
challenges of moving over land during

02:52:28.960 --> 02:52:32.240
the rainy season.

02:52:32.240 --> 02:52:34.479
>> The road just at the point where it runs

02:52:34.479 --> 02:52:36.560
northward from the sea over its whole

02:52:36.560 --> 02:52:39.359
length was rough and narrow. On top of

02:52:39.359 --> 02:52:41.760
this, it rained so that the steep places

02:52:41.760 --> 02:52:43.359
became slippery and some of the

02:52:43.359 --> 02:52:45.439
carriages came loose and collided with

02:52:45.439 --> 02:52:48.600
each other.

02:52:48.960 --> 02:52:51.600
Due to these challenges, travel by road

02:52:51.600 --> 02:52:54.560
was largely only possible during the dry

02:52:54.560 --> 02:52:57.840
season. For the rest of the year, goods

02:52:57.840 --> 02:53:01.279
were transported by river, taking rice

02:53:01.279 --> 02:53:04.720
and other export crops downstream to the

02:53:04.720 --> 02:53:09.040
great port cities on barges.

02:53:09.040 --> 02:53:11.439
These boats would then sail back up the

02:53:11.439 --> 02:53:14.720
rivers with luxury goods imported from

02:53:14.720 --> 02:53:18.399
China, India, and elsewhere.

02:53:18.399 --> 02:53:21.120
These port cities were the beating heart

02:53:21.120 --> 02:53:24.479
of the Majapahit Empire. And the large

02:53:24.479 --> 02:53:27.439
numbers of Chinese coins found in their

02:53:27.439 --> 02:53:30.240
archaeological sites testify to the

02:53:30.240 --> 02:53:34.840
booming trade that went on.

02:53:35.680 --> 02:53:38.399
At each of these ports, the sales of

02:53:38.399 --> 02:53:41.200
hundreds of ships would be visible,

02:53:41.200 --> 02:53:43.520
coming and going with countless trade

02:53:43.520 --> 02:53:46.640
goods. And among these, the most

02:53:46.640 --> 02:53:49.439
lucrative were the spices grown on the

02:53:49.439 --> 02:53:51.840
islands of the archipelago that were

02:53:51.840 --> 02:53:55.359
prized all around the world, such as

02:53:55.359 --> 02:53:59.200
pepper, cardamom, and ginger.

02:53:59.200 --> 02:54:02.880
But the rarest of all were cloves and

02:54:02.880 --> 02:54:05.880
nutmeg.

02:54:12.720 --> 02:54:15.279
Cloves and nutmeg were brought to

02:54:15.279 --> 02:54:18.560
Majapahit on large ships that sailed

02:54:18.560 --> 02:54:21.200
from a small group of islands which are

02:54:21.200 --> 02:54:24.640
called the islands of Maluku and would

02:54:24.640 --> 02:54:30.200
come to be known as the spice islands.

02:54:31.600 --> 02:54:34.240
While cloves were grown all over these

02:54:34.240 --> 02:54:37.840
islands, nutmeg was extremely limited in

02:54:37.840 --> 02:54:39.359
cultivation,

02:54:39.359 --> 02:54:42.479
occurring only on 10 islands in the tiny

02:54:42.479 --> 02:54:45.920
archipelago of Banda.

02:54:45.920 --> 02:54:49.040
Wild nutmeg had long been harvested by

02:54:49.040 --> 02:54:51.120
the peoples native to the Bander

02:54:51.120 --> 02:54:53.760
Islands, but it was a particularly

02:54:53.760 --> 02:54:57.120
difficult plant to cultivate.

02:54:57.120 --> 02:55:00.240
Nutmeg seeds will fail to germinate if

02:55:00.240 --> 02:55:02.319
they aren't planted in soil within a

02:55:02.319 --> 02:55:05.359
week, making them difficult to transport

02:55:05.359 --> 02:55:08.640
by sea. And the particular environment

02:55:08.640 --> 02:55:11.359
of volcanic soil that they evolved in

02:55:11.359 --> 02:55:13.200
means that they are fragile and

02:55:13.200 --> 02:55:17.840
difficult to nurture to full size.

02:55:17.840 --> 02:55:20.240
As a result of these difficulties, the

02:55:20.240 --> 02:55:23.279
Bander Islanders claimed that nutmeg was

02:55:23.279 --> 02:55:26.160
simply a gift of the gods and could not

02:55:26.160 --> 02:55:29.600
be cultivated by human hands.

02:55:29.600 --> 02:55:31.600
Instead, they would travel to the parts

02:55:31.600 --> 02:55:34.080
of the forest where it grew wild to

02:55:34.080 --> 02:55:37.600
collect its prized seeds. And they kept

02:55:37.600 --> 02:55:40.319
the location of these groves a carefully

02:55:40.319 --> 02:55:43.800
guarded secret.

02:55:44.080 --> 02:55:46.880
But despite its extreme rarity, the

02:55:46.880 --> 02:55:48.960
fragrant nutmeg seeds that these

02:55:48.960 --> 02:55:51.920
islanders harvested traveled all around

02:55:51.920 --> 02:55:54.000
the world.

02:55:54.000 --> 02:55:56.640
The spice would reach Constantinople in

02:55:56.640 --> 02:55:59.520
the sixth century and instantly became a

02:55:59.520 --> 02:56:02.080
sought after commodity and mark of

02:56:02.080 --> 02:56:03.680
luxury.

02:56:03.680 --> 02:56:06.160
Nutmeg would even be mentioned as a

02:56:06.160 --> 02:56:09.920
spice to flavor English ale in Chaucer's

02:56:09.920 --> 02:56:12.399
Canterbury Tales, which was written

02:56:12.399 --> 02:56:16.800
during the time of the Majapahit Empire.

02:56:16.800 --> 02:56:19.200
At times, nutmeg would sell on the other

02:56:19.200 --> 02:56:21.600
side of the world for more than an

02:56:21.600 --> 02:56:26.040
equivalent weight of gold.

02:56:29.200 --> 02:56:32.160
As a result of this global trade, the

02:56:32.160 --> 02:56:34.560
rulers of the Bander Islands would come

02:56:34.560 --> 02:56:37.040
to be known around the region as the

02:56:37.040 --> 02:56:40.960
Orurang Kaya or rich men. And the

02:56:40.960 --> 02:56:43.760
entirety of this trade passed through

02:56:43.760 --> 02:56:48.279
the major ports of Majapahit.

02:56:48.880 --> 02:56:51.520
To transport these goods across the seas

02:56:51.520 --> 02:56:54.960
and oceans, the sailors of Majapahit

02:56:54.960 --> 02:57:01.120
voyaged in large vessels known as Jongs.

02:57:01.120 --> 02:57:03.359
These were the descendants of the Bora

02:57:03.359 --> 02:57:05.600
Budor ships that had sailed to

02:57:05.600 --> 02:57:08.160
Madagascar and Eastern Africa in the

02:57:08.160 --> 02:57:10.240
preceding centuries.

02:57:10.240 --> 02:57:12.640
And by this time, some of these ships

02:57:12.640 --> 02:57:15.359
had reportedly grown to phenomenal

02:57:15.359 --> 02:57:18.359
proportions.

02:57:19.200 --> 02:57:21.680
Reports on the true size of these

02:57:21.680 --> 02:57:25.040
vessels vary, but some sources record

02:57:25.040 --> 02:57:30.000
jongs that reached a size of 80 m long.

02:57:30.000 --> 02:57:32.560
They were built with layered hulls that

02:57:32.560 --> 02:57:35.359
made them exceptionally strong and were

02:57:35.359 --> 02:57:38.240
able to transport a thousand soldiers

02:57:38.240 --> 02:57:42.319
and more than a,000 tons of cargo.

02:57:42.319 --> 02:57:45.120
The sight of these massive jongs

02:57:45.120 --> 02:57:47.920
astonished European explorers when they

02:57:47.920 --> 02:57:51.040
arrived in the archipelago in the 16th

02:57:51.040 --> 02:57:53.200
century.

02:57:53.200 --> 02:57:56.319
One Portuguese admiral and explorer

02:57:56.319 --> 02:57:59.120
Alphonso de Alba wrote about

02:57:59.120 --> 02:58:01.120
encountering one of these enormous

02:58:01.120 --> 02:58:05.399
vessels in 1511.

02:58:06.000 --> 02:58:08.399
The whole fre went back along the coast

02:58:08.399 --> 02:58:10.399
in the same order as they had first

02:58:10.399 --> 02:58:13.120
come. And when they were in the latitude

02:58:13.120 --> 02:58:16.160
of the powder island, they cighted two

02:58:16.160 --> 02:58:19.760
very large junks and gave chase to them.

02:58:19.760 --> 02:58:22.319
One of these, which was from India,

02:58:22.319 --> 02:58:24.960
surrendered immediately. But the other

02:58:24.960 --> 02:58:29.080
junk would not do so.

02:58:31.279 --> 02:58:34.640
The Portuguese gave chase to the massive

02:58:34.640 --> 02:58:37.920
Javanese ship and made several attempts

02:58:37.920 --> 02:58:40.800
to board it, but these were all

02:58:40.800 --> 02:58:43.359
unsuccessful.

02:58:43.359 --> 02:58:46.000
The Europeans even opened fire on the

02:58:46.000 --> 02:58:48.800
Jong with their cannons, but found that

02:58:48.800 --> 02:58:51.359
the three or four layers of wood with

02:58:51.359 --> 02:58:54.080
which the Javanese built their ships

02:58:54.080 --> 02:58:57.680
simply absorbed the cannon fire and the

02:58:57.680 --> 02:59:01.200
vast vessel sailed on.

02:59:01.200 --> 02:59:04.720
In a letter written sometime later, one

02:59:04.720 --> 02:59:08.080
of the Portuguese captains, Ferno Perez

02:59:08.080 --> 02:59:11.359
de Andrada, describes the massive

02:59:11.359 --> 02:59:15.160
Javanese ship.

02:59:16.160 --> 02:59:19.120
The junk was the largest seen by men of

02:59:19.120 --> 02:59:21.840
these parts so far. It carried a

02:59:21.840 --> 02:59:24.240
thousand fighting men on board. And your

02:59:24.240 --> 02:59:26.160
lordship can believe me that it was an

02:59:26.160 --> 02:59:29.120
amazing thing to see because beside it,

02:59:29.120 --> 02:59:31.840
our own vessel, the Anuniada, did not

02:59:31.840 --> 02:59:34.720
look like a ship at all. We attacked it

02:59:34.720 --> 02:59:37.120
with bombards, but even the shots of the

02:59:37.120 --> 02:59:39.200
largest cannon did not pierce it below

02:59:39.200 --> 02:59:40.960
the waterline.

02:59:40.960 --> 02:59:43.920
It was so monstrous that no man had ever

02:59:43.920 --> 02:59:47.399
seen the like.

02:59:48.720 --> 02:59:51.200
Eventually, the smaller and more

02:59:51.200 --> 02:59:54.240
maneuverable Portuguese ships were able

02:59:54.240 --> 02:59:57.279
to disable the larger Jong by breaking

02:59:57.279 --> 03:00:00.479
its two massive rudders.

03:00:00.479 --> 03:00:03.600
This finally brought the men on board to

03:00:03.600 --> 03:00:05.359
surrender.

03:00:05.359 --> 03:00:07.680
The Europeans were so impressed with the

03:00:07.680 --> 03:00:10.640
size of these Javanese Jongs that they

03:00:10.640 --> 03:00:13.439
sailed one of them all the way back home

03:00:13.439 --> 03:00:15.760
where it was used for a time as a

03:00:15.760 --> 03:00:18.399
warship in the fleet guarding the

03:00:18.399 --> 03:00:22.080
Gibralta Strait.

03:00:22.080 --> 03:00:24.960
Although we have little reliable data on

03:00:24.960 --> 03:00:27.680
when the ships of the Javanese reached

03:00:27.680 --> 03:00:30.560
such a massive scale, it is reasonable

03:00:30.560 --> 03:00:32.560
to assume that they were at least

03:00:32.560 --> 03:00:35.120
approaching that size during the reign

03:00:35.120 --> 03:00:38.080
of Hyam Wuruk when the power of

03:00:38.080 --> 03:00:43.080
Majapahit was at its peak.

03:00:43.760 --> 03:00:46.319
These enormous ships would have been the

03:00:46.319 --> 03:00:50.240
crucial backbone of the Majapahit Empire

03:00:50.240 --> 03:00:53.520
with their enormous capacity for cargo

03:00:53.520 --> 03:00:56.240
and their ability to transport thousands

03:00:56.240 --> 03:00:59.760
of men, horses, and even elephants from

03:00:59.760 --> 03:01:02.319
island to island wherever they were

03:01:02.319 --> 03:01:04.399
needed.

03:01:04.399 --> 03:01:06.560
And of course they would have made a

03:01:06.560 --> 03:01:09.680
powerful statement about the power and

03:01:09.680 --> 03:01:15.479
prestige of the empire of Majapahit.

03:01:16.399 --> 03:01:19.120
By now, the Majapahit sphere of

03:01:19.120 --> 03:01:21.920
influence stretched over the sea for

03:01:21.920 --> 03:01:25.120
thousands of kilometers, and they had

03:01:25.120 --> 03:01:27.600
monopolized the lucrative spice routes

03:01:27.600 --> 03:01:30.319
from the Malaku Islands so that their

03:01:30.319 --> 03:01:33.040
wealth would have swelled to previously

03:01:33.040 --> 03:01:36.479
unimagined heights.

03:01:36.479 --> 03:01:39.200
Over this period, Majapahit began to

03:01:39.200 --> 03:01:42.240
take on the form of what has been called

03:01:42.240 --> 03:01:46.760
a Mandala Empire.

03:01:53.120 --> 03:01:56.479
In Sanskrit, the word mandala means

03:01:56.479 --> 03:01:59.680
circle and it has come to describe a

03:01:59.680 --> 03:02:02.800
style of traditional geometric pattern

03:02:02.800 --> 03:02:05.680
used to represent a kind of map of the

03:02:05.680 --> 03:02:08.000
universe

03:02:08.000 --> 03:02:10.080
reflected in the shapes of the Buddhist

03:02:10.080 --> 03:02:13.520
temples at Seu and Borau Budur. These

03:02:13.520 --> 03:02:16.720
are designed to help an adherent achieve

03:02:16.720 --> 03:02:19.920
a state of meditation.

03:02:19.920 --> 03:02:21.920
Although the forms of these mandalas

03:02:21.920 --> 03:02:24.880
differ, many show the sacred mountain

03:02:24.880 --> 03:02:27.680
meu at the center of the world,

03:02:27.680 --> 03:02:32.479
sometimes surrounded by the world ocean.

03:02:32.479 --> 03:02:35.359
Around this is a square palace with four

03:02:35.359 --> 03:02:38.640
gates and then a circle representing the

03:02:38.640 --> 03:02:41.600
continents outside it. The heavens and

03:02:41.600 --> 03:02:43.760
the world of the gods forming the

03:02:43.760 --> 03:02:46.880
outside of the pattern.

03:02:46.880 --> 03:02:49.200
The mandala presents the vision of a

03:02:49.200 --> 03:02:52.160
world ordered in a strict hierarchy

03:02:52.160 --> 03:02:55.120
radiating out from the center. And so

03:02:55.120 --> 03:02:57.520
it's no surprise it has long been used

03:02:57.520 --> 03:03:02.240
as a way of visualizing royal power.

03:03:02.240 --> 03:03:05.279
As early as the 4th century BC, the

03:03:05.279 --> 03:03:08.160
Indian writer Killilia in his work the

03:03:08.160 --> 03:03:10.960
Arth Shastra described what he called

03:03:10.960 --> 03:03:15.279
the Raja Mandala or Mandala of kings in

03:03:15.279 --> 03:03:18.240
which a powerful ruler will bring other

03:03:18.240 --> 03:03:22.720
less powerful ones under his control.

03:03:22.720 --> 03:03:24.800
This idea has become popular among

03:03:24.800 --> 03:03:27.520
modern historians seeking to understand

03:03:27.520 --> 03:03:30.160
how Southeast Asian states of this time

03:03:30.160 --> 03:03:32.640
were organized and there's some evidence

03:03:32.640 --> 03:03:34.720
that this is also how the Javanese of

03:03:34.720 --> 03:03:36.640
the time would have thought of their

03:03:36.640 --> 03:03:39.279
world.

03:03:39.279 --> 03:03:42.640
The epic poem the desavan describes the

03:03:42.640 --> 03:03:45.600
structure of the Majapayah Empire like

03:03:45.600 --> 03:03:48.640
the solar system with power radiating

03:03:48.640 --> 03:03:51.359
out from the center like the rays of the

03:03:51.359 --> 03:03:54.359
sun.

03:03:59.920 --> 03:04:01.920
The royal compound at Maja the

03:04:01.920 --> 03:04:04.479
incomparable is as sun and the moon and

03:04:04.479 --> 03:04:06.640
the courtyards of the many quarters each

03:04:06.640 --> 03:04:08.880
with its own particular charm are rays

03:04:08.880 --> 03:04:11.279
of light in relation to it. Like the

03:04:11.279 --> 03:04:13.439
stars and planets are the various

03:04:13.439 --> 03:04:16.240
remaining cities. Daha the foremost and

03:04:16.240 --> 03:04:17.680
the other islands and all the

03:04:17.680 --> 03:04:19.600
surrounding countries which seek refuge

03:04:19.600 --> 03:04:24.279
and in numbers come into the presence.

03:04:31.760 --> 03:04:34.880
It's still an open question exactly how

03:04:34.880 --> 03:04:38.160
much power Majapahit exerted over its

03:04:38.160 --> 03:04:40.880
vassal states.

03:04:40.880 --> 03:04:44.160
Some empires like the Roman Empire ruled

03:04:44.160 --> 03:04:47.279
with direct control.

03:04:47.279 --> 03:04:49.680
When they conquered a new area, they

03:04:49.680 --> 03:04:52.640
erased previous forms of government and

03:04:52.640 --> 03:04:55.760
social structures. and imposed their own

03:04:55.760 --> 03:04:58.720
on absorbed territories.

03:04:58.720 --> 03:05:00.800
But we don't see much evidence of that

03:05:00.800 --> 03:05:05.000
in the case of Majapahit.

03:05:05.040 --> 03:05:07.439
Subordinate kings and rulers on the

03:05:07.439 --> 03:05:10.479
outer islands certainly paid symbolic

03:05:10.479 --> 03:05:14.640
homage to the king in Majapah.

03:05:14.640 --> 03:05:16.880
They likely provided an agreed upon

03:05:16.880 --> 03:05:19.600
tribute each year and a certain number

03:05:19.600 --> 03:05:22.560
of soldiers and ships for any military

03:05:22.560 --> 03:05:26.000
action undertaken by the empire.

03:05:26.000 --> 03:05:28.080
But beyond that, it's likely that the

03:05:28.080 --> 03:05:30.560
lords of each island and tributary

03:05:30.560 --> 03:05:33.040
kingdom continued to exert more or less

03:05:33.040 --> 03:05:37.600
total control over their own affairs.

03:05:37.600 --> 03:05:41.920
This arrangement suited everyone well.

03:05:41.920 --> 03:05:44.479
Cultural identities on each individual

03:05:44.479 --> 03:05:47.279
island were relatively distinct and

03:05:47.279 --> 03:05:49.680
deeply entrenched.

03:05:49.680 --> 03:05:51.760
Local languages and customs were

03:05:51.760 --> 03:05:54.399
different on each island, and few people

03:05:54.399 --> 03:05:56.720
around the region wanted to be directly

03:05:56.720 --> 03:06:00.240
ruled by a Javanese governor or to have

03:06:00.240 --> 03:06:02.560
Javanese troops stationed in their

03:06:02.560 --> 03:06:04.880
hometowns.

03:06:04.880 --> 03:06:07.200
And for the Majapayah, appointing

03:06:07.200 --> 03:06:09.600
governors and stationing troops to put

03:06:09.600 --> 03:06:12.319
down rebellions and uprisings would have

03:06:12.319 --> 03:06:15.760
been an unwelcome expense.

03:06:15.760 --> 03:06:18.560
The Mandala structure was cheap and

03:06:18.560 --> 03:06:20.399
efficient.

03:06:20.399 --> 03:06:22.880
While times were good and the empire was

03:06:22.880 --> 03:06:25.760
strong, it ensured a maximum level of

03:06:25.760 --> 03:06:28.960
compliance and cooperation from subjects

03:06:28.960 --> 03:06:32.319
with the lightest possible touch and

03:06:32.319 --> 03:06:34.720
allowed everyone to profit from the

03:06:34.720 --> 03:06:37.359
great traffic of trade that flowed along

03:06:37.359 --> 03:06:41.960
the great arteries of the sea.

03:06:42.880 --> 03:06:45.040
From the center of the mandala in

03:06:45.040 --> 03:06:48.640
Majapahit, fleets of Jong ships sailed

03:06:48.640 --> 03:06:51.439
back and forth among the islands,

03:06:51.439 --> 03:06:54.080
bringing trade and tribute back to its

03:06:54.080 --> 03:06:57.359
booming ports.

03:06:57.359 --> 03:07:00.640
But as with any empire, sometimes its

03:07:00.640 --> 03:07:04.720
subjects had to be kept in line, as the

03:07:04.720 --> 03:07:08.840
Deshavan describes.

03:07:15.920 --> 03:07:17.920
The other countries, all that were under

03:07:17.920 --> 03:07:20.000
the care of Java, obeyed the king's

03:07:20.000 --> 03:07:22.160
commands, and each was true in what it

03:07:22.160 --> 03:07:24.960
did. Furthermore, any that transgressed

03:07:24.960 --> 03:07:27.359
his commands was attacked and wiped out

03:07:27.359 --> 03:07:28.960
completely by the squadrons of the

03:07:28.960 --> 03:07:33.240
various valiant naval officers.

03:07:47.680 --> 03:07:50.560
One such example occurred in the year

03:07:50.560 --> 03:07:52.479
1375

03:07:52.479 --> 03:07:55.040
when one of the subject kings of the

03:07:55.040 --> 03:07:59.040
empire seemed to get ideas above his

03:07:59.040 --> 03:08:02.040
station.

03:08:09.840 --> 03:08:12.720
The troublesome king in question was a

03:08:12.720 --> 03:08:15.840
man named Aditya Vamman who had been put

03:08:15.840 --> 03:08:18.560
in power by Majapahit on the large

03:08:18.560 --> 03:08:22.000
island of Sumatra, a short hop over the

03:08:22.000 --> 03:08:25.040
sea from Java.

03:08:25.040 --> 03:08:29.279
Aditioan was something of a narcissist.

03:08:29.279 --> 03:08:31.520
He was fond of commissioning massive

03:08:31.520 --> 03:08:34.479
statues of himself, larger than any that

03:08:34.479 --> 03:08:36.560
have been uncovered of other kings in

03:08:36.560 --> 03:08:39.439
the region, and over the preceding years

03:08:39.439 --> 03:08:42.720
he had begun to act in an insubordinate

03:08:42.720 --> 03:08:45.120
manner.

03:08:45.120 --> 03:08:47.760
At one point, he had a stone tablet

03:08:47.760 --> 03:08:51.680
inscribed that showed a list of kings,

03:08:51.680 --> 03:08:54.399
and he had the insulence to place his

03:08:54.399 --> 03:08:59.600
own name above King Hyam Woods.

03:08:59.600 --> 03:09:02.080
This all would have caused rumbles of

03:09:02.080 --> 03:09:07.399
constonnation at the court of Majapahed.

03:09:07.439 --> 03:09:11.279
But Aditio would go too far when he sent

03:09:11.279 --> 03:09:13.920
his own envoys to the court of the

03:09:13.920 --> 03:09:17.600
emperor of China, bypassing his king

03:09:17.600 --> 03:09:20.000
completely.

03:09:20.000 --> 03:09:24.240
One Javanese epic poem, the Parata Yuda,

03:09:24.240 --> 03:09:26.880
describes the rage of the demon king

03:09:26.880 --> 03:09:29.520
Ravena, upon getting news of the death

03:09:29.520 --> 03:09:32.560
of his sons. But we might imagine it a

03:09:32.560 --> 03:09:34.960
fitting description of Hayam Wuruk's

03:09:34.960 --> 03:09:38.319
reaction when he heard that Aditya had

03:09:38.319 --> 03:09:40.880
been going over his head and making

03:09:40.880 --> 03:09:43.840
overtures to China without consulting

03:09:43.840 --> 03:09:46.399
him.

03:09:46.399 --> 03:09:49.600
The monarch was furiously enraged. He

03:09:49.600 --> 03:09:52.399
gnored his mustaches, his countenance

03:09:52.399 --> 03:09:55.840
was inflamed, and his bosom red as the

03:09:55.840 --> 03:09:59.760
waari flower. Sweat exuded from every

03:09:59.760 --> 03:10:03.200
paw. The angles of his mouth trembled.

03:10:03.200 --> 03:10:05.600
His eyelashes stuck together. He

03:10:05.600 --> 03:10:08.720
vaunted. He called aloud. He challenged

03:10:08.720 --> 03:10:13.800
all his enemies to meet him at once.

03:10:14.720 --> 03:10:16.960
Hayam Wuruk summoned the Chinese

03:10:16.960 --> 03:10:19.680
ambassador to Sumatra and after

03:10:19.680 --> 03:10:22.319
lambasting him apparently had the man

03:10:22.319 --> 03:10:25.439
beheaded and his head sent back to China

03:10:25.439 --> 03:10:28.800
in a bag.

03:10:28.800 --> 03:10:31.200
In perhaps a sign of the power of

03:10:31.200 --> 03:10:34.399
Majapahit at this time the Chinese

03:10:34.399 --> 03:10:37.600
didn't respond in kind.

03:10:37.600 --> 03:10:40.240
Instead, they bashfully apologized for

03:10:40.240 --> 03:10:42.640
their mistake and would eventually send

03:10:42.640 --> 03:10:46.080
a gift of fine fabrics and a batch of

03:10:46.080 --> 03:10:48.880
paper money to the Javanese court to

03:10:48.880 --> 03:10:51.200
make amends.

03:10:51.200 --> 03:10:54.399
But from the vain king Aditioan,

03:10:54.399 --> 03:10:58.160
no apology would suffice.

03:10:58.160 --> 03:11:01.600
King Hayam Wuruk amassed his army, as

03:11:01.600 --> 03:11:05.040
many as 300 warships and according to

03:11:05.040 --> 03:11:08.720
the chronicles, 200,000 soldiers to

03:11:08.720 --> 03:11:11.840
crush this upstart king.

03:11:11.840 --> 03:11:13.840
And although we don't hear what happened

03:11:13.840 --> 03:11:17.520
to him, Aditioan never appears in any

03:11:17.520 --> 03:11:20.560
other written records or inscriptions

03:11:20.560 --> 03:11:23.560
again.

03:11:24.479 --> 03:11:28.640
Now Hayam Wuruk was on the war path.

03:11:28.640 --> 03:11:32.080
After crushing Aditioan, the Majapahit

03:11:32.080 --> 03:11:34.960
fleet rounded on another problematic

03:11:34.960 --> 03:11:36.800
vassel.

03:11:36.800 --> 03:11:39.920
This man ruled the walled settlement of

03:11:39.920 --> 03:11:43.040
Singapura, now the modern city of

03:11:43.040 --> 03:11:48.319
Singapore, and his name was Paramevara.

03:11:48.319 --> 03:11:51.840
After a month-long siege, the Majapahed

03:11:51.840 --> 03:11:54.399
forces broke through the walls and

03:11:54.399 --> 03:11:57.840
slaughtered the inhabitants.

03:11:57.840 --> 03:12:00.640
To this day, legend has it that the

03:12:00.640 --> 03:12:04.479
ironrich reddish clay soil of Singapore

03:12:04.479 --> 03:12:07.279
was stained that color by the blood

03:12:07.279 --> 03:12:11.279
spilled during this massacre.

03:12:11.279 --> 03:12:14.960
Paramea, the king of Singapura, fled

03:12:14.960 --> 03:12:19.200
north to the area of the Malaca Strait,

03:12:19.200 --> 03:12:21.680
but he would remain a thorn in the side

03:12:21.680 --> 03:12:27.720
of Majapah for some time to come.

03:12:41.279 --> 03:12:44.160
The Aditia incident shows that the

03:12:44.160 --> 03:12:47.520
empire of Majapahit was held together by

03:12:47.520 --> 03:12:50.960
trade and diplomacy and the promise of

03:12:50.960 --> 03:12:54.319
mutual peace and prosperity.

03:12:54.319 --> 03:12:57.439
But it was also very much backed by the

03:12:57.439 --> 03:13:00.800
threat of force.

03:13:00.800 --> 03:13:03.520
Over this period, the royal capital

03:13:03.520 --> 03:13:05.600
would flourish.

03:13:05.600 --> 03:13:08.880
But this golden age of Majapahit could

03:13:08.880 --> 03:13:11.840
not last forever and its end would come

03:13:11.840 --> 03:13:14.880
about after the death of its last great

03:13:14.880 --> 03:13:19.479
king Hayam Wuruk.

03:13:31.439 --> 03:13:35.040
King Hayam Wuruk died likely in the year

03:13:35.040 --> 03:13:36.960
1389

03:13:36.960 --> 03:13:39.680
and with him the light began to leave

03:13:39.680 --> 03:13:43.960
the court of Majapah.

03:13:44.880 --> 03:13:48.399
The great statesman and general Gajamada

03:13:48.399 --> 03:13:52.479
had died 25 years earlier and Hayam

03:13:52.479 --> 03:13:55.439
Wuruk's mother queen Tribuana Vijay

03:13:55.439 --> 03:13:58.800
Tungadevi had also died a decade or so

03:13:58.800 --> 03:14:01.359
after that.

03:14:01.359 --> 03:14:03.439
There now seems to have been something

03:14:03.439 --> 03:14:07.439
of a vacuum of talent in the Majapahit

03:14:07.439 --> 03:14:10.439
court.

03:14:10.880 --> 03:14:12.960
Exacerbating the problem was the

03:14:12.960 --> 03:14:16.479
complexity of Javanese succession laws

03:14:16.479 --> 03:14:18.560
which had developed to deal with the

03:14:18.560 --> 03:14:21.439
fact that kings of this time always had

03:14:21.439 --> 03:14:23.600
multiple wives.

03:14:23.600 --> 03:14:26.560
In ideal circumstances, the law would

03:14:26.560 --> 03:14:29.680
unambiguously favor one successor over

03:14:29.680 --> 03:14:32.479
another, and there would be no confusion

03:14:32.479 --> 03:14:35.439
about who would take the throne.

03:14:35.439 --> 03:14:39.279
But fate had dealt Hyamuruk a bad hand

03:14:39.279 --> 03:14:43.560
when it came to his succession.

03:14:48.239 --> 03:14:50.560
He had failed to have a son by his

03:14:50.560 --> 03:14:53.680
principal wife and so his closest legal

03:14:53.680 --> 03:14:56.880
heir was therefore a woman named Kusumov

03:14:56.880 --> 03:14:59.920
Vardini, his daughter by a lower ranking

03:14:59.920 --> 03:15:01.680
wife.

03:15:01.680 --> 03:15:05.359
She had married a man named Vikramordina

03:15:05.359 --> 03:15:07.920
and so it seemed likely that he would

03:15:07.920 --> 03:15:11.040
become king despite having only married

03:15:11.040 --> 03:15:13.680
into the royal family.

03:15:13.680 --> 03:15:16.880
The Dashaner describes this couple in

03:15:16.880 --> 03:15:20.319
glowing terms.

03:15:20.319 --> 03:15:22.800
>> They have as daughter Princess Kusuma

03:15:22.800 --> 03:15:25.520
Wadani, a blameless young princess who's

03:15:25.520 --> 03:15:27.200
paid homage in the royal compound of

03:15:27.200 --> 03:15:30.080
Cabalan and is of the utmost charm.

03:15:30.080 --> 03:15:32.000
Prince Wikramama Wadana will be her

03:15:32.000 --> 03:15:34.000
proper match as everyone says they will

03:15:34.000 --> 03:15:35.760
be like a god and goddess when they

03:15:35.760 --> 03:15:37.840
marry later, bringing happiness to

03:15:37.840 --> 03:15:41.239
people's hearts.

03:15:42.160 --> 03:15:46.399
But Hayam Wuruk did also have a son by a

03:15:46.399 --> 03:15:49.680
secondary less senior wife.

03:15:49.680 --> 03:15:52.000
In the histories, he is known only by

03:15:52.000 --> 03:15:55.840
the title Bra Vabumi or the lord of a

03:15:55.840 --> 03:15:59.200
place called Virumi.

03:15:59.200 --> 03:16:01.920
Being a man and the direct descendant of

03:16:01.920 --> 03:16:05.279
Hyam Wuruk also gave him a strong claim

03:16:05.279 --> 03:16:08.080
to the throne despite his mother being

03:16:08.080 --> 03:16:12.560
of a lower rank than Kusumo Vines.

03:16:12.560 --> 03:16:16.160
And this situation of two people having

03:16:16.160 --> 03:16:19.600
a comparable claim was a recipe for

03:16:19.600 --> 03:16:22.080
disaster.

03:16:22.080 --> 03:16:24.479
Hyam Muruk seems to have sensed the

03:16:24.479 --> 03:16:28.239
danger while he was still alive.

03:16:28.239 --> 03:16:30.800
In an attempt to remedy the situation

03:16:30.800 --> 03:16:33.439
and cool off the rivalry between these

03:16:33.439 --> 03:16:36.800
two men, he divided the empire into the

03:16:36.800 --> 03:16:40.000
western court, the capital of Majapet,

03:16:40.000 --> 03:16:43.040
and the eastern court, where the lord of

03:16:43.040 --> 03:16:46.800
Virumi held sway.

03:16:46.800 --> 03:16:48.960
The exact details of this arrangement

03:16:48.960 --> 03:16:51.600
are unknown, but it was a clear and

03:16:51.600 --> 03:16:54.000
obvious rift, now splitting the

03:16:54.000 --> 03:16:58.720
kingdom's Javanese heartlands in two.

03:16:58.720 --> 03:17:01.120
The situation seems to have gotten so

03:17:01.120 --> 03:17:03.680
bad that at one point the Chinese

03:17:03.680 --> 03:17:06.800
chronicle, the Ming Shilu, notes that

03:17:06.800 --> 03:17:09.040
the two different courts were each

03:17:09.040 --> 03:17:10.960
sending their envoys to meet

03:17:10.960 --> 03:17:12.960
independently with the emperor's

03:17:12.960 --> 03:17:15.960
ambassadors.

03:17:16.239 --> 03:17:19.040
Like the rumblings and earthquakes

03:17:19.040 --> 03:17:22.160
before a great eruption, the signs of

03:17:22.160 --> 03:17:24.960
trouble must have been obvious to anyone

03:17:24.960 --> 03:17:27.120
who was paying attention.

03:17:27.120 --> 03:17:30.000
And in the years that followed, the rift

03:17:30.000 --> 03:17:33.840
would tear apart the land of Java and

03:17:33.840 --> 03:17:37.960
the empire it ruled.

03:17:48.160 --> 03:17:51.439
The name for the conflicts that follows

03:17:51.439 --> 03:17:54.080
is found in the chronicle of the

03:17:54.080 --> 03:17:56.399
Paraton.

03:17:56.399 --> 03:17:59.920
There it is called the regreg, a word

03:17:59.920 --> 03:18:03.840
that in Javanese means bit by bit and

03:18:03.840 --> 03:18:06.160
can be used to describe something

03:18:06.160 --> 03:18:10.080
falling apart piece by piece.

03:18:10.080 --> 03:18:14.160
As we will see, this was a fitting name

03:18:14.160 --> 03:18:16.479
as the conflict would bring about the

03:18:16.479 --> 03:18:19.200
steady coming apart of the Mandala

03:18:19.200 --> 03:18:21.600
Empire of Majapet

03:18:21.600 --> 03:18:24.319
that had held together over the last

03:18:24.319 --> 03:18:27.040
century.

03:18:27.200 --> 03:18:30.640
The paraton describes the conflict that

03:18:30.640 --> 03:18:33.640
unfolded.

03:18:38.239 --> 03:18:41.600
>> They came to blows. There was division

03:18:41.600 --> 03:18:44.880
and men died in the division.

03:18:44.880 --> 03:18:47.920
After 3 years, there then arose again

03:18:47.920 --> 03:18:51.200
the regreg war. Both sides prepared

03:18:51.200 --> 03:18:53.920
themselves. All the lords asked

03:18:53.920 --> 03:18:57.680
themselves, "Whom shall I follow?"

03:18:57.680 --> 03:19:02.279
Then the fighting began.

03:19:07.120 --> 03:19:11.520
The regreg war would rage for 2 years

03:19:11.520 --> 03:19:14.239
and over this time neither side could

03:19:14.239 --> 03:19:16.960
gain the upper hand.

03:19:16.960 --> 03:19:20.080
The para raton describes the back and

03:19:20.080 --> 03:19:24.760
forth nature of the fighting.

03:19:26.479 --> 03:19:29.840
First the western palace was defeated.

03:19:29.840 --> 03:19:32.239
Their lords were hardpressed.

03:19:32.239 --> 03:19:35.279
In distress they wished to flee. Then

03:19:35.279 --> 03:19:38.160
they said, "Do not flee yet. Let us

03:19:38.160 --> 03:19:41.600
fight them." Then the eastern palace was

03:19:41.600 --> 03:19:44.600
defeated.

03:19:46.560 --> 03:19:49.520
The strength of the Mandala Empire

03:19:49.520 --> 03:19:52.239
system was in how light a hold it

03:19:52.239 --> 03:19:55.120
exerted on its vassels.

03:19:55.120 --> 03:19:57.600
It was a cheap and efficient way to run

03:19:57.600 --> 03:20:01.359
an imperial system. But this strength in

03:20:01.359 --> 03:20:04.800
times of stability became a weakness

03:20:04.800 --> 03:20:08.920
when times got hard.

03:20:11.200 --> 03:20:13.520
For the kings who swore allegiance to

03:20:13.520 --> 03:20:16.880
Majapay, it was all too easy when the

03:20:16.880 --> 03:20:19.600
empire was distracted to simply turn

03:20:19.600 --> 03:20:24.560
away and quietly stop paying its fees or

03:20:24.560 --> 03:20:27.359
sending it troops.

03:20:27.359 --> 03:20:30.080
With the power of Majapahit's fleet and

03:20:30.080 --> 03:20:33.359
army now focused entirely on the war

03:20:33.359 --> 03:20:36.800
between its western and eastern courts,

03:20:36.800 --> 03:20:40.160
many of its formerly most loyal subjects

03:20:40.160 --> 03:20:44.399
simply slipped out of its grasp.

03:20:44.399 --> 03:20:46.960
One of these subjects was in the region

03:20:46.960 --> 03:20:51.120
of Malayu, which during the Regreg War

03:20:51.120 --> 03:20:53.359
drifted under the sovereignty of the

03:20:53.359 --> 03:20:56.640
powerful kingdom of Aayutaya in what is

03:20:56.640 --> 03:21:00.040
now Thailand.

03:21:02.720 --> 03:21:05.920
On the island of Sumatra, a Chinese

03:21:05.920 --> 03:21:09.920
pirate named Chen Zooi from Guangdong

03:21:09.920 --> 03:21:12.479
even took advantage of the chaos caused

03:21:12.479 --> 03:21:16.000
by the regreg war to seize control of

03:21:16.000 --> 03:21:19.840
the wealthy port city of Palumbang.

03:21:19.840 --> 03:21:23.359
This man would run Palumbang as a pirate

03:21:23.359 --> 03:21:25.520
fortress for the better part of a

03:21:25.520 --> 03:21:28.960
decade, using it as a base to raid the

03:21:28.960 --> 03:21:31.200
wealthy shipping that passed through the

03:21:31.200 --> 03:21:34.560
Malaca Strait and using forged bronze

03:21:34.560 --> 03:21:38.080
seals to create counterfeit licenses and

03:21:38.080 --> 03:21:42.960
aid smuggling into and out of China.

03:21:42.960 --> 03:21:46.399
The Chinese Muslim writer Mahan wrote

03:21:46.399 --> 03:21:49.200
about the situation in his work, A

03:21:49.200 --> 03:21:53.479
Survey of the Ocean Shores.

03:21:53.760 --> 03:21:57.200
Chanzui plundered ships and prayed on

03:21:57.200 --> 03:21:59.840
both native and foreign merchants for

03:21:59.840 --> 03:22:03.239
several years.

03:22:04.960 --> 03:22:07.600
On the northern coast of Borneo, the

03:22:07.600 --> 03:22:10.720
Brune Kingdom had also begun to ignore

03:22:10.720 --> 03:22:14.239
the overlordship of Majapah.

03:22:14.239 --> 03:22:17.680
And by 1405, Western Borneo had also

03:22:17.680 --> 03:22:20.080
drifted away.

03:22:20.080 --> 03:22:23.040
These small kingdoms would instead seek

03:22:23.040 --> 03:22:25.279
protection under the influence of

03:22:25.279 --> 03:22:28.239
another power that was now flexing its

03:22:28.239 --> 03:22:31.040
muscles with increasing confidence on

03:22:31.040 --> 03:22:33.040
the waves.

03:22:33.040 --> 03:22:36.479
That was the rising Ming dynasty of

03:22:36.479 --> 03:22:39.479
China.

03:22:54.800 --> 03:22:58.239
By this time, the Mongol Yuan dynasty

03:22:58.239 --> 03:23:01.120
had collapsed and the Mongols had been

03:23:01.120 --> 03:23:05.279
forcibly thrown out of China. Now, a new

03:23:05.279 --> 03:23:08.800
dynasty known as the Ming had taken its

03:23:08.800 --> 03:23:11.800
place.

03:23:12.000 --> 03:23:15.040
The Ming ruled over a devastated land

03:23:15.040 --> 03:23:17.120
that had suffered immensely over the

03:23:17.120 --> 03:23:20.880
years of Mongol conquest and misrule by

03:23:20.880 --> 03:23:24.479
the Yuan emperors, exacerbated by the

03:23:24.479 --> 03:23:27.920
ravages of the Black Death.

03:23:27.920 --> 03:23:33.000
But now, China was rebuilding.

03:23:33.840 --> 03:23:36.479
Ultimately, the Ming Dynasty has been

03:23:36.479 --> 03:23:38.560
remembered as a paranoid and

03:23:38.560 --> 03:23:41.200
inward-looking state, which virtually

03:23:41.200 --> 03:23:43.680
bankrupted itself with the construction

03:23:43.680 --> 03:23:47.120
of its vast Great Wall in the north,

03:23:47.120 --> 03:23:50.960
sealing itself off from the world.

03:23:50.960 --> 03:23:53.680
But at the start of the 15th century,

03:23:53.680 --> 03:23:57.439
Ming China looked quite different.

03:23:57.439 --> 03:24:00.080
This was partly due to the reign of an

03:24:00.080 --> 03:24:03.120
ambitious and outward-looking ruler

03:24:03.120 --> 03:24:08.120
known as the Yong Lur Emperor.

03:24:24.880 --> 03:24:27.760
The Yonglur emperor was a patron of

03:24:27.760 --> 03:24:30.880
learning and sponsored the writing of a

03:24:30.880 --> 03:24:34.880
great encyclopedia made up of 23,000

03:24:34.880 --> 03:24:38.239
written scrolls in an attempt to record

03:24:38.239 --> 03:24:41.600
all the world's knowledge.

03:24:41.600 --> 03:24:44.319
He was fascinated by everything and

03:24:44.319 --> 03:24:47.920
especially the world outside of China as

03:24:47.920 --> 03:24:52.319
he recorded in his work Ming Taong Baoun

03:24:52.319 --> 03:24:55.040
or the valuable teachings of Emperor

03:24:55.040 --> 03:24:58.399
Yong Lur.

03:24:58.399 --> 03:25:00.640
Whenever I can find the time, I read

03:25:00.640 --> 03:25:03.040
history books and the classics so as to

03:25:03.040 --> 03:25:06.640
avoid idol living. I constantly remind

03:25:06.640 --> 03:25:09.120
myself that the world is so vast and

03:25:09.120 --> 03:25:12.319
state affairs so important that I cannot

03:25:12.319 --> 03:25:15.439
succumb to laziness and complacency for

03:25:15.439 --> 03:25:18.720
even a moment. Once one has succumbed to

03:25:18.720 --> 03:25:21.520
laziness and complacency,

03:25:21.520 --> 03:25:25.960
everything will become stagnant.

03:25:29.760 --> 03:25:32.720
As a result of this fascination with the

03:25:32.720 --> 03:25:35.359
outer world, throughout his reign, he

03:25:35.359 --> 03:25:38.080
sent out a flurry of diplomatic missions

03:25:38.080 --> 03:25:41.520
to all corners of Asia, letting everyone

03:25:41.520 --> 03:25:45.040
know that China was once again open for

03:25:45.040 --> 03:25:48.479
business. And as part of this effort, he

03:25:48.479 --> 03:25:50.800
ordered the construction of a grand

03:25:50.800 --> 03:25:54.560
fleet designed to sail around the region

03:25:54.560 --> 03:25:57.600
and remind the people of every land of

03:25:57.600 --> 03:26:01.800
the might of China.

03:26:08.720 --> 03:26:11.920
To build his fleet, the Yonglur Emperor

03:26:11.920 --> 03:26:14.319
ordered the construction of a vast

03:26:14.319 --> 03:26:18.560
shipyard at a place called Liang or

03:26:18.560 --> 03:26:21.359
Dragon River.

03:26:21.359 --> 03:26:24.239
This sprawling industrial complex was

03:26:24.239 --> 03:26:26.560
built at the point where the Yangti

03:26:26.560 --> 03:26:29.920
River is met by the smaller Chin Wai in

03:26:29.920 --> 03:26:34.279
the Ming capital of Nanjing.

03:26:34.319 --> 03:26:36.720
And it would be the largest shipyard

03:26:36.720 --> 03:26:39.920
anywhere in the world.

03:26:39.920 --> 03:26:43.600
On its seven long large docks, at least

03:26:43.600 --> 03:26:46.319
100 ships could be built at any one

03:26:46.319 --> 03:26:48.560
time.

03:26:48.560 --> 03:26:51.359
To help in his mammoth effort, the

03:26:51.359 --> 03:26:54.720
Yonglur emperor invited more than 20,000

03:26:54.720 --> 03:26:58.239
craftsmen to work here on his ships. And

03:26:58.239 --> 03:27:01.279
timbers of elm, cedar, and campfor were

03:27:01.279 --> 03:27:03.680
brought in enormous quantities to the

03:27:03.680 --> 03:27:07.040
city of Nanjing, transported from inland

03:27:07.040 --> 03:27:10.080
ports down the rivers on flatbottomed

03:27:10.080 --> 03:27:12.000
barges.

03:27:12.000 --> 03:27:14.160
The noise of the shipwrights shouting

03:27:14.160 --> 03:27:16.960
and calling. The thump of the massive

03:27:16.960 --> 03:27:19.520
beams being lifted into place. The

03:27:19.520 --> 03:27:22.560
beating of chisels and hammers on nails.

03:27:22.560 --> 03:27:24.399
All of this would have sounded over the

03:27:24.399 --> 03:27:27.279
rooftops of Nanjing in the early years

03:27:27.279 --> 03:27:30.800
of the 15th century. For China, it was

03:27:30.800 --> 03:27:34.560
the sound of industry and progress. But

03:27:34.560 --> 03:27:37.359
for the power of Majapahit far across

03:27:37.359 --> 03:27:39.840
the sea in the south, it might as well

03:27:39.840 --> 03:27:42.720
have been the sound of nails being

03:27:42.720 --> 03:27:47.080
driven into its coffin.

03:27:50.479 --> 03:27:54.640
By the year 1405, as the regreg civil

03:27:54.640 --> 03:27:58.560
war dragged on in Majapay, the Yonglur

03:27:58.560 --> 03:28:02.160
emperor had completed his grand fleet.

03:28:02.160 --> 03:28:05.279
And now all he needed was an admiral to

03:28:05.279 --> 03:28:07.520
lead it.

03:28:07.520 --> 03:28:11.760
The man he chose was a unic, a giant

03:28:11.760 --> 03:28:15.560
named Jungh.

03:28:17.920 --> 03:28:21.200
In some ways, Jungha was an unlikely

03:28:21.200 --> 03:28:24.479
candidate to become China's most famous

03:28:24.479 --> 03:28:27.200
sailor and admiral.

03:28:27.200 --> 03:28:29.920
For one thing, he had barely any sailing

03:28:29.920 --> 03:28:31.680
experience.

03:28:31.680 --> 03:28:33.680
But he had spent much of his life

03:28:33.680 --> 03:28:36.080
serving the Yonglur Emperor as a

03:28:36.080 --> 03:28:38.319
military commander and had proved

03:28:38.319 --> 03:28:43.359
himself a capable and loyal general.

03:28:43.359 --> 03:28:47.200
Jungha was a Muslim born into a devout

03:28:47.200 --> 03:28:50.800
family in the southwest of China, but he

03:28:50.800 --> 03:28:53.359
had been captured during the wars of the

03:28:53.359 --> 03:28:56.560
preceding decades and had been castrated

03:28:56.560 --> 03:28:59.840
and brought up a unic as a kind of

03:28:59.840 --> 03:29:03.359
military slave.

03:29:03.359 --> 03:29:07.680
One writer named Yuan Jong describes his

03:29:07.680 --> 03:29:10.720
towering stature with perhaps some

03:29:10.720 --> 03:29:13.720
exaggeration.

03:29:14.720 --> 03:29:19.359
He was 7 ft tall and had a waist about 5

03:29:19.359 --> 03:29:22.239
ft in circumference. His cheeks and

03:29:22.239 --> 03:29:24.800
forehead were high, but his nose was

03:29:24.800 --> 03:29:28.239
small. He had glaring eyes, teeth as

03:29:28.239 --> 03:29:31.040
white and well-shaped as shells, and a

03:29:31.040 --> 03:29:34.960
voice as loud as a huge bell. He knew a

03:29:34.960 --> 03:29:37.600
great deal about warfare, and was well

03:29:37.600 --> 03:29:41.399
accustomed to battle.

03:29:44.319 --> 03:29:48.000
On the 11th of July 1405, under the

03:29:48.000 --> 03:29:51.760
command of Admiral Jung Ha, this vast

03:29:51.760 --> 03:29:55.279
fleet set sail

03:29:55.279 --> 03:29:58.000
and it would have made an awe inspiring

03:29:58.000 --> 03:30:01.000
site.

03:30:01.279 --> 03:30:04.800
It comprised a total of 317

03:30:04.800 --> 03:30:08.080
vessels of the latest design, including

03:30:08.080 --> 03:30:11.279
at least 60 vast treasure ships that

03:30:11.279 --> 03:30:15.200
were among the largest in the world.

03:30:15.200 --> 03:30:17.279
By some sources, these could have

03:30:17.279 --> 03:30:21.359
measured more than 120 m in length and

03:30:21.359 --> 03:30:25.120
50 in breadth, making them still among

03:30:25.120 --> 03:30:27.840
the largest wooden sailing ships built

03:30:27.840 --> 03:30:30.479
anywhere in the world.

03:30:30.479 --> 03:30:33.680
These vessels were each fitted with 24

03:30:33.680 --> 03:30:37.040
cast bronze cannons and were beautifully

03:30:37.040 --> 03:30:40.239
decorated too with their prows carved

03:30:40.239 --> 03:30:43.840
with animal heads, dragons, phoenixes

03:30:43.840 --> 03:30:50.120
and eagles all painted in bright colors.

03:30:54.080 --> 03:30:56.560
Like the ancient Greeks, Egyptians,

03:30:56.560 --> 03:30:59.200
Phoenicians, and Romans, the Chinese

03:30:59.200 --> 03:31:01.200
painted eyes on the fronts of their

03:31:01.200 --> 03:31:04.319
vessels so that the ships seemed to take

03:31:04.319 --> 03:31:07.920
on a life of their own and see their way

03:31:07.920 --> 03:31:11.760
through mists and stormy seas.

03:31:11.760 --> 03:31:14.720
On board these hundreds of ships were a

03:31:14.720 --> 03:31:19.200
total of 28,000 men, including sailors

03:31:19.200 --> 03:31:22.720
and soldiers, but also diplomats,

03:31:22.720 --> 03:31:25.680
astronomers, linguists, interpreters,

03:31:25.680 --> 03:31:29.040
and doctors, as well as carpenters, and

03:31:29.040 --> 03:31:31.760
ship builders for if the vessels needed

03:31:31.760 --> 03:31:35.200
repairing while at sea.

03:31:35.200 --> 03:31:38.000
On one stone tablet that the admiral

03:31:38.000 --> 03:31:41.600
later erected in Fujian, he describes

03:31:41.600 --> 03:31:45.479
this great voyage.

03:31:45.920 --> 03:31:49.439
We have traversed more than 100,000 lee

03:31:49.439 --> 03:31:52.479
of immense water spaces and have beheld

03:31:52.479 --> 03:31:55.760
in the ocean huge waves like mountains

03:31:55.760 --> 03:31:59.120
rising sky high. And we have set eyes on

03:31:59.120 --> 03:32:02.800
barbarian regions far away hidden in a

03:32:02.800 --> 03:32:06.080
blue transparency of light vapors. While

03:32:06.080 --> 03:32:10.399
our sails loftily unfurled like clouds

03:32:10.399 --> 03:32:13.840
day and night, continued their course as

03:32:13.840 --> 03:32:17.120
rapidly as a star traversing those

03:32:17.120 --> 03:32:20.600
savage waves.

03:32:23.840 --> 03:32:26.479
Although outfitted with cannons, the

03:32:26.479 --> 03:32:28.800
treasure ships were not primarily

03:32:28.800 --> 03:32:32.479
warships. They were in fact vast cargo

03:32:32.479 --> 03:32:35.840
vessels. Their holds filled to the brim

03:32:35.840 --> 03:32:40.160
with Chinese silks, cotton, tea, wine,

03:32:40.160 --> 03:32:44.319
oil, iron, and candles along with other

03:32:44.319 --> 03:32:47.840
luxuries. All intended for trade with

03:32:47.840 --> 03:32:50.239
the strange lands they would encounter

03:32:50.239 --> 03:32:52.560
along the way.

03:32:52.560 --> 03:32:54.479
From these lands they brought back

03:32:54.479 --> 03:32:57.920
spices, gemstones and even in the year

03:32:57.920 --> 03:33:01.600
1414 a live giraffe which had been

03:33:01.600 --> 03:33:04.160
brought to Bengal by some African

03:33:04.160 --> 03:33:07.600
delegates from Malindi.

03:33:07.600 --> 03:33:09.359
Impressed at the sight of the treasure

03:33:09.359 --> 03:33:11.920
fleet, these men had gifted one of these

03:33:11.920 --> 03:33:14.319
animals to the Chinese who brought it

03:33:14.319 --> 03:33:18.640
home to no little amazement.

03:33:18.640 --> 03:33:21.600
The Yonglur emperor was no stranger to

03:33:21.600 --> 03:33:24.960
receiving exotic animals as gifts. And

03:33:24.960 --> 03:33:26.720
there was even a part of his palace

03:33:26.720 --> 03:33:30.000
devoted to keeping and caring for them.

03:33:30.000 --> 03:33:33.680
Elephants and rhinoceroses from Champa,

03:33:33.680 --> 03:33:37.040
bears from Siam, parrots and peacocks

03:33:37.040 --> 03:33:41.439
from Java, and ostriches from Aiden.

03:33:41.439 --> 03:33:44.319
But of all these, it was the giraffe

03:33:44.319 --> 03:33:47.279
that he asked his court artists to

03:33:47.279 --> 03:33:50.279
paint.

03:33:52.960 --> 03:33:56.080
Alongside the vast treasure ships sailed

03:33:56.080 --> 03:33:58.560
a countless array of different support

03:33:58.560 --> 03:34:01.920
vessels, some carrying horses and

03:34:01.920 --> 03:34:06.640
troops, others warships for defense.

03:34:06.640 --> 03:34:09.840
Other boats were floating water tankers,

03:34:09.840 --> 03:34:12.080
ensuring the thousands of personnel

03:34:12.080 --> 03:34:14.880
wouldn't go thirsty on long voyages

03:34:14.880 --> 03:34:18.359
between ports.

03:34:18.399 --> 03:34:20.399
The ships communicated between one

03:34:20.399 --> 03:34:24.640
another using large flags, signal bells,

03:34:24.640 --> 03:34:27.760
a drum, and gongs

03:34:27.760 --> 03:34:30.880
along with 10 lanterns that could signal

03:34:30.880 --> 03:34:32.880
at night.

03:34:32.880 --> 03:34:35.279
They even carried carrier pigeons to

03:34:35.279 --> 03:34:38.960
communicate over longer distances.

03:34:38.960 --> 03:34:41.439
The ultimate destination of the treasure

03:34:41.439 --> 03:34:44.720
fleet was the city of Kolicode in the

03:34:44.720 --> 03:34:47.520
modern Indian state of Kerala. But the

03:34:47.520 --> 03:34:50.239
fleet was ordered to stop at every large

03:34:50.239 --> 03:34:53.200
port and kingdom on the way to

03:34:53.200 --> 03:34:55.520
demonstrate the might of the Ming

03:34:55.520 --> 03:34:58.479
Emperor.

03:34:58.479 --> 03:35:01.920
It was in 1406 that the Ming fleet

03:35:01.920 --> 03:35:05.760
arrived in Java while the regreg civil

03:35:05.760 --> 03:35:11.319
war was reaching its bloody height

03:35:22.880 --> 03:35:25.920
when the Chinese treasure fleet arrived

03:35:25.920 --> 03:35:27.279
in Java.

03:35:27.279 --> 03:35:29.279
They might have expected to encounter

03:35:29.279 --> 03:35:32.479
the scenes of wealth and prosperity that

03:35:32.479 --> 03:35:35.920
had been recorded by previous visitors,

03:35:35.920 --> 03:35:38.640
but they would find instead a troubled

03:35:38.640 --> 03:35:43.120
land devastated by civil war. The

03:35:43.120 --> 03:35:45.840
treasure ships anchored off the coast

03:35:45.840 --> 03:35:48.479
and a group of Chinese soldiers and

03:35:48.479 --> 03:35:51.920
merchants came ashore in western Java

03:35:51.920 --> 03:35:54.160
hoping to trade.

03:35:54.160 --> 03:35:57.600
But the western king Vikramina,

03:35:57.600 --> 03:36:00.319
the husband of Haim Wuruk's daughter,

03:36:00.319 --> 03:36:03.120
believed that his rival in the east had

03:36:03.120 --> 03:36:05.840
brought the Chinese to intervene in the

03:36:05.840 --> 03:36:07.840
civil war.

03:36:07.840 --> 03:36:10.080
While the Chinese visitors were trading

03:36:10.080 --> 03:36:13.120
in the marketplace, King Vikrama's

03:36:13.120 --> 03:36:15.840
soldiers swept down on them from all

03:36:15.840 --> 03:36:17.520
sides.

03:36:17.520 --> 03:36:20.160
The cries of the Javanese warriors and

03:36:20.160 --> 03:36:22.239
the screams of the dying would have

03:36:22.239 --> 03:36:25.279
joined the pops and bangs of cannons

03:36:25.279 --> 03:36:27.279
that would have sounded all around the

03:36:27.279 --> 03:36:29.120
marketplace.

03:36:29.120 --> 03:36:32.080
The acrid smell of gunpowder and blood

03:36:32.080 --> 03:36:35.040
would have lingered on the air. When the

03:36:35.040 --> 03:36:37.040
smoke cleared,

03:36:37.040 --> 03:36:40.080
170 Chinese merchants and sailors were

03:36:40.080 --> 03:36:43.520
dead, and the rest had fled back to

03:36:43.520 --> 03:36:46.840
their ships.

03:36:47.439 --> 03:36:50.560
Admiral Jungha had enough soldiers with

03:36:50.560 --> 03:36:53.040
him that he could have invaded Java in

03:36:53.040 --> 03:36:56.080
response. And perhaps like the Mongols

03:36:56.080 --> 03:36:58.399
more than a 100red years earlier, he

03:36:58.399 --> 03:37:00.800
could have decisively tipped the balance

03:37:00.800 --> 03:37:03.520
in this civil war.

03:37:03.520 --> 03:37:06.800
But he was a pragmatic man, and he

03:37:06.800 --> 03:37:10.960
decided to tread a more considered path.

03:37:10.960 --> 03:37:13.359
He treated his wounded on board the

03:37:13.359 --> 03:37:16.399
ships and sent envoys back to the

03:37:16.399 --> 03:37:21.279
Yonglur emperor asking him what to do.

03:37:21.279 --> 03:37:24.319
In the time of Hayam Wuruk 30 years

03:37:24.319 --> 03:37:27.359
earlier, China had steered clear of

03:37:27.359 --> 03:37:30.160
conflict with the powerful Majapah

03:37:30.160 --> 03:37:33.279
Empire, sending money and goods in order

03:37:33.279 --> 03:37:37.680
to avoid a war. But now Majapah was

03:37:37.680 --> 03:37:40.399
weakened and divided.

03:37:40.399 --> 03:37:43.520
This time it was King Vikramma who would

03:37:43.520 --> 03:37:46.479
send a graveling apology to the Chinese

03:37:46.479 --> 03:37:50.880
court. And the Ming Shilu or Records of

03:37:50.880 --> 03:37:53.680
the Ming dynasty records what the

03:37:53.680 --> 03:37:58.120
emperor said in reply.

03:37:58.880 --> 03:38:02.560
There is no doubt as to your guilt. You

03:38:02.560 --> 03:38:05.279
acted on the basis of greed and anger

03:38:05.279 --> 03:38:08.319
and you have acted against heaven. Is

03:38:08.319 --> 03:38:10.960
there anything more serious than this?

03:38:10.960 --> 03:38:13.520
Just as I was about to raise an army to

03:38:13.520 --> 03:38:15.760
punish you, I have seen that you are

03:38:15.760 --> 03:38:19.200
capable of repenting your mistakes, and

03:38:19.200 --> 03:38:21.840
I have thus leniently stopped the

03:38:21.840 --> 03:38:25.840
dispatch of troops. But what of the 170

03:38:25.840 --> 03:38:28.479
people who died innocently?

03:38:28.479 --> 03:38:32.399
You must immediately pay 60,000 leang of

03:38:32.399 --> 03:38:35.600
gold as compensation for their lives and

03:38:35.600 --> 03:38:39.120
to atone for your crime.

03:38:44.000 --> 03:38:47.439
A year later, a Javanese ship arrived in

03:38:47.439 --> 03:38:50.479
China with only a sixth of the sum of

03:38:50.479 --> 03:38:52.720
gold that the Chinese emperor had

03:38:52.720 --> 03:38:55.920
demanded along with a letter explaining

03:38:55.920 --> 03:38:58.319
that the bankrupt kingdom could not

03:38:58.319 --> 03:39:01.600
afford to pay anymore.

03:39:01.600 --> 03:39:04.080
The Chinese emperor responded

03:39:04.080 --> 03:39:07.080
magnanimously.

03:39:08.080 --> 03:39:10.319
What I want from those people who live

03:39:10.319 --> 03:39:13.200
far away is that they acknowledge their

03:39:13.200 --> 03:39:16.080
guilt. But I do not want to enrich

03:39:16.080 --> 03:39:19.920
myself with their gold.

03:39:19.920 --> 03:39:22.720
The point had been made and the

03:39:22.720 --> 03:39:27.200
humiliation of Majapah was total.

03:39:27.200 --> 03:39:32.200
Everyone in the region took notice.

03:39:32.319 --> 03:39:34.239
In 1424,

03:39:34.239 --> 03:39:37.359
Chinese records show that when one king

03:39:37.359 --> 03:39:40.640
in Sumatra died, his son sent out a

03:39:40.640 --> 03:39:43.600
letter asking permission to succeed him

03:39:43.600 --> 03:39:47.439
as king. And he sent it not to the kings

03:39:47.439 --> 03:39:51.760
of Majapah in Java, but to the Chinese

03:39:51.760 --> 03:39:55.439
emperor in the Ming court.

03:39:55.439 --> 03:39:58.560
This shows just how far the star of

03:39:58.560 --> 03:40:02.560
Majapahit had fallen and how the might

03:40:02.560 --> 03:40:07.319
of China was on the rise.

03:40:25.680 --> 03:40:28.720
Although Admiral Jungh had declined to

03:40:28.720 --> 03:40:31.120
fight on this occasion, the treasure

03:40:31.120 --> 03:40:33.600
fleet was more than capable of doing

03:40:33.600 --> 03:40:36.880
battle on the seas. And alongside their

03:40:36.880 --> 03:40:40.319
main diplomatic and merkantile mission,

03:40:40.319 --> 03:40:42.880
its admiral had been given some less

03:40:42.880 --> 03:40:45.359
peaceful tasks to complete on their

03:40:45.359 --> 03:40:47.600
voyage.

03:40:47.600 --> 03:40:50.560
Chief among these was a mission to

03:40:50.560 --> 03:40:53.520
destroy the pirate fortress that still

03:40:53.520 --> 03:40:56.399
held out at the Sumatran port of

03:40:56.399 --> 03:40:59.760
Palumbang which had risen up due to the

03:40:59.760 --> 03:41:03.760
weakness of the Majapahit Empire.

03:41:03.760 --> 03:41:07.279
The Mingshi or history of Ming describes

03:41:07.279 --> 03:41:10.720
how the pirate chief Chen Zooi had been

03:41:10.720 --> 03:41:14.000
playing a clever double game, attempting

03:41:14.000 --> 03:41:18.000
to mllify the Ming Emperor.

03:41:18.000 --> 03:41:20.080
In the fourth year of the Yong Lay

03:41:20.080 --> 03:41:22.560
reign, the pirate chieftain of the old

03:41:22.560 --> 03:41:25.840
port, Chenhu Yi, sent his son to the

03:41:25.840 --> 03:41:28.720
Ming court. However, although he sent

03:41:28.720 --> 03:41:31.120
tributes to the court, he was plundering

03:41:31.120 --> 03:41:33.920
the seas and thus obstructing the

03:41:33.920 --> 03:41:36.000
comingings and goings of the tributes

03:41:36.000 --> 03:41:39.000
envoys.

03:41:39.200 --> 03:41:41.600
On its way home through the straits of

03:41:41.600 --> 03:41:45.200
Malaca, the enormous treasure fleet took

03:41:45.200 --> 03:41:47.600
its chance.

03:41:47.600 --> 03:41:50.479
They sailed along the mangrove crusted

03:41:50.479 --> 03:41:54.479
coast of Sumatra towards Palumbang which

03:41:54.479 --> 03:41:59.359
the Chinese called the old port.

03:41:59.359 --> 03:42:01.200
We can only imagine the site that

03:42:01.200 --> 03:42:04.479
greeted the pirates of Palamang as the

03:42:04.479 --> 03:42:07.120
hundreds of colorful ships bore down on

03:42:07.120 --> 03:42:10.920
them on the horizon.

03:42:11.120 --> 03:42:14.000
When they arrived at the port city, they

03:42:14.000 --> 03:42:16.160
demanded the surrender of the pirate

03:42:16.160 --> 03:42:20.000
chief Chen Zooi. According to the Ming

03:42:20.000 --> 03:42:23.040
Shilu or records of the Ming dynasty,

03:42:23.040 --> 03:42:25.359
the pirate chief attempted to use

03:42:25.359 --> 03:42:29.359
deception to gain the upper hand.

03:42:29.359 --> 03:42:31.439
When he arrived at the old port of

03:42:31.439 --> 03:42:34.560
Palimang, he came across Ju Yi and

03:42:34.560 --> 03:42:37.279
others and sent people to bring them to

03:42:37.279 --> 03:42:40.319
negotiate their pacification. Juu Yi and

03:42:40.319 --> 03:42:42.640
the others feigned surrender but

03:42:42.640 --> 03:42:45.120
secretly plotted to attack the Imperial

03:42:45.120 --> 03:42:48.080
army. Jeng Hur and the others found out

03:42:48.080 --> 03:42:51.359
about this and marshalling the troops

03:42:51.359 --> 03:42:55.080
prepared their defenses.

03:42:56.960 --> 03:42:59.279
The ensuing battle would be the first

03:42:59.279 --> 03:43:01.680
test of the power of the Yonglur

03:43:01.680 --> 03:43:04.319
Emperor's fleet.

03:43:04.319 --> 03:43:06.640
The Ming ships would have rammed into

03:43:06.640 --> 03:43:09.760
the pirate vessels, hurled gunpowder

03:43:09.760 --> 03:43:13.359
bombs from catapults, and fired special

03:43:13.359 --> 03:43:16.319
kinds of fireworks filled with scraps of

03:43:16.319 --> 03:43:20.479
paper designed to spread fire and terror

03:43:20.479 --> 03:43:24.160
and ignite enemy sails.

03:43:24.160 --> 03:43:26.640
They would have also sent volleys of

03:43:26.640 --> 03:43:30.080
flaming arrows flying towards the pirate

03:43:30.080 --> 03:43:32.319
ships.

03:43:32.319 --> 03:43:35.600
The result was a resounding victory for

03:43:35.600 --> 03:43:39.720
the Ming treasure fleet.

03:43:42.319 --> 03:43:45.760
The pirate Jui suffered a great defeat.

03:43:45.760 --> 03:43:48.399
Over 5,000 of the bandit gang were

03:43:48.399 --> 03:43:51.279
killed while 10 of the bandit ships were

03:43:51.279 --> 03:43:54.640
burnt and seven were captured. Further,

03:43:54.640 --> 03:43:57.439
two counterfeit bronze seals were seized

03:43:57.439 --> 03:44:00.640
and three prisoners, including Ju Yi,

03:44:00.640 --> 03:44:03.040
were taken alive. When they arrived at

03:44:03.040 --> 03:44:05.840
the capital in chains, it was ordered

03:44:05.840 --> 03:44:08.000
that all of the prisoners were to be

03:44:08.000 --> 03:44:11.000
beheaded.

03:44:12.319 --> 03:44:15.120
With this pirate threat crushed, the

03:44:15.120 --> 03:44:18.160
Ming Chinese quickly moved to establish

03:44:18.160 --> 03:44:20.720
a governor of the area to prevent a

03:44:20.720 --> 03:44:24.239
resurgence of any piracy.

03:44:24.239 --> 03:44:27.520
The man they chose, a Muslim named Xi

03:44:27.520 --> 03:44:31.199
Jinqing, had once been an official of

03:44:31.199 --> 03:44:35.319
the Majapet Empire.

03:44:35.439 --> 03:44:37.760
The old port pacification

03:44:37.760 --> 03:44:40.720
superintendency was established and it

03:44:40.720 --> 03:44:43.920
was ordered that Xi Jinqing be appointed

03:44:43.920 --> 03:44:47.040
as the pacification superintendent.

03:44:47.040 --> 03:44:50.000
A seal, a title patent, headwear and a

03:44:50.000 --> 03:44:53.040
belt, patented fine silks and silk

03:44:53.040 --> 03:44:57.600
gauses were conferred upon him.

03:44:57.600 --> 03:45:00.160
While the rulers of Majapay had their

03:45:00.160 --> 03:45:02.160
backs turned, fighting amongst

03:45:02.160 --> 03:45:05.199
themselves, the Ming Chinese had swept

03:45:05.199 --> 03:45:08.640
in and stamped their seal of authority

03:45:08.640 --> 03:45:12.920
on the Malaca Strait.

03:45:21.439 --> 03:45:24.080
To strengthen this grip over the narrow

03:45:24.080 --> 03:45:27.120
and crucial waterway, the Chinese would

03:45:27.120 --> 03:45:29.680
also bring under their wing the young

03:45:29.680 --> 03:45:32.880
city of Malaca, which had recently been

03:45:32.880 --> 03:45:36.479
growing in wealth and importance.

03:45:36.479 --> 03:45:40.080
Malaca was a hub for another tide of

03:45:40.080 --> 03:45:43.279
change that was now sweeping through the

03:45:43.279 --> 03:45:46.239
archipelago.

03:45:46.239 --> 03:45:49.199
That was the steady spread of the

03:45:49.199 --> 03:45:53.640
religion of Islam.

03:46:04.880 --> 03:46:08.080
Islam had long had a presence in the

03:46:08.080 --> 03:46:10.880
Indonesian archipelago and had arrived

03:46:10.880 --> 03:46:13.760
with traders who traveled back and forth

03:46:13.760 --> 03:46:16.640
across the Indian Ocean, bringing nutmeg

03:46:16.640 --> 03:46:19.840
and cloves to the markets of Egypt and

03:46:19.840 --> 03:46:21.520
Arabia.

03:46:21.520 --> 03:46:24.000
But now this young religion began to

03:46:24.000 --> 03:46:28.840
make advances in all directions.

03:46:29.040 --> 03:46:32.080
The European traveler Marco Polo

03:46:32.080 --> 03:46:34.640
remarked on the change already underway

03:46:34.640 --> 03:46:37.680
on the island of Sumatra when he passed

03:46:37.680 --> 03:46:42.920
through the town of Perlac in 1292.

03:46:44.880 --> 03:46:46.800
The people of Pearlac used to be

03:46:46.800 --> 03:46:49.520
idoltors, but owing to contact with

03:46:49.520 --> 03:46:52.479
Sariss merchants who continually resort

03:46:52.479 --> 03:46:55.040
here in their ships, they have all been

03:46:55.040 --> 03:46:59.120
converted to the law of Muhammad.

03:47:05.600 --> 03:47:07.680
Part of the reason for the spread of

03:47:07.680 --> 03:47:10.479
Islam on the archipelago was the

03:47:10.479 --> 03:47:12.640
prestige and protection that the

03:47:12.640 --> 03:47:15.760
religion brought.

03:47:15.760 --> 03:47:18.560
One example of this in action is the

03:47:18.560 --> 03:47:20.479
king Parameasara,

03:47:20.479 --> 03:47:23.040
the ruler of Singapura, who had been

03:47:23.040 --> 03:47:26.319
besieged by Majapahit under the reign of

03:47:26.319 --> 03:47:29.520
Hayamuruk and had fled north to the

03:47:29.520 --> 03:47:33.439
coast of the Malaka Strait.

03:47:33.439 --> 03:47:37.359
There he had founded the city of Malaca.

03:47:37.359 --> 03:47:39.520
And in order to add an heir of

03:47:39.520 --> 03:47:42.800
legitimacy to his new rule, Paramasara

03:47:42.800 --> 03:47:45.680
seems to have ditched his original Hindu

03:47:45.680 --> 03:47:48.800
Buddhist name and adopted a new Persian

03:47:48.800 --> 03:47:52.960
one, calling himself Sultan Iscander Sha

03:47:52.960 --> 03:47:55.439
instead.

03:47:55.439 --> 03:47:58.080
Muslim traders preferred where possible

03:47:58.080 --> 03:48:01.199
to trade with other Muslims who were

03:48:01.199 --> 03:48:03.600
more likely to share their languages of

03:48:03.600 --> 03:48:06.720
Arabic or Persian, keep the same trading

03:48:06.720 --> 03:48:09.920
and prayer hours, and shared a common

03:48:09.920 --> 03:48:13.040
moral code. And so this connection

03:48:13.040 --> 03:48:17.439
helped Malaca to rapidly expand.

03:48:17.439 --> 03:48:20.319
The new city's strategic location, right

03:48:20.319 --> 03:48:22.880
on the narrow sea corridor, meant the

03:48:22.880 --> 03:48:25.920
Ming Chinese were also very interested

03:48:25.920 --> 03:48:28.399
to bring its rulers under their

03:48:28.399 --> 03:48:31.680
patronage and protection.

03:48:31.680 --> 03:48:34.479
When Admiral Jung Hur arrived at the

03:48:34.479 --> 03:48:37.680
port town of Malaka, he left a stone

03:48:37.680 --> 03:48:40.800
tablet inscribed with a poem that

03:48:40.800 --> 03:48:42.960
officially declared it under the

03:48:42.960 --> 03:48:47.080
protection of China.

03:48:48.880 --> 03:48:52.160
The vast southwestern sea reaches unto

03:48:52.160 --> 03:48:55.040
the middle kingdom. Its waves cresting

03:48:55.040 --> 03:48:58.000
high as the heavens, watering the earth

03:48:58.000 --> 03:49:01.439
the same way for countless eons.

03:49:01.439 --> 03:49:03.840
Washed by sunlight, bathed in the

03:49:03.840 --> 03:49:07.040
moonlight, rain swept cracks and dewy

03:49:07.040 --> 03:49:09.840
rocks in its midst luxuriate with

03:49:09.840 --> 03:49:11.359
vegetation.

03:49:11.359 --> 03:49:14.239
And in such a place, people live in

03:49:14.239 --> 03:49:17.439
harmony. Its righteous king, paying his

03:49:17.439 --> 03:49:20.239
respects to imperial power, wishes his

03:49:20.239 --> 03:49:22.080
country to be treated as one of our

03:49:22.080 --> 03:49:24.960
imperial domains and to follow the

03:49:24.960 --> 03:49:28.560
Chinese way. So here, writ large on

03:49:28.560 --> 03:49:32.239
everlasting stone, we do proclaim your

03:49:32.239 --> 03:49:35.760
loyalty. Posterity will smile upon your

03:49:35.760 --> 03:49:39.279
deed as time passes, and your sons and

03:49:39.279 --> 03:49:41.920
grandsons will have limitless good

03:49:41.920 --> 03:49:44.920
fortune.

03:49:46.399 --> 03:49:49.840
In this, the Chinese were right. The

03:49:49.840 --> 03:49:52.479
port town of Malaca would grow under

03:49:52.479 --> 03:49:54.880
Ming protection to become the largest

03:49:54.880 --> 03:49:59.279
and most important in the whole region.

03:49:59.279 --> 03:50:02.479
When Jungh returned a few years later,

03:50:02.479 --> 03:50:04.960
he would build a fort at Malaca to

03:50:04.960 --> 03:50:07.920
protect it. And in return, the people of

03:50:07.920 --> 03:50:10.479
the city would ensure that this crucial

03:50:10.479 --> 03:50:13.439
waterway would be controlled by China

03:50:13.439 --> 03:50:16.960
and China alone.

03:50:16.960 --> 03:50:18.960
Wealth and trade that would have once

03:50:18.960 --> 03:50:22.080
flowed through the ports of Java now

03:50:22.080 --> 03:50:24.560
passed through the new trading hub of

03:50:24.560 --> 03:50:28.080
Mala instead.

03:50:28.080 --> 03:50:31.199
From this hub of commerce, the influence

03:50:31.199 --> 03:50:34.399
of Islam would spread all across the

03:50:34.399 --> 03:50:36.960
islands.

03:50:36.960 --> 03:50:39.359
For the kings of Java who ruled

03:50:39.359 --> 03:50:41.600
according to legitimacy derived from

03:50:41.600 --> 03:50:43.840
their connection to the Buddha and the

03:50:43.840 --> 03:50:47.840
god Shiva, each new convert reduced

03:50:47.840 --> 03:50:51.880
their overall power.

03:50:52.640 --> 03:50:55.600
Subsequent voyages by Jung Hur's

03:50:55.600 --> 03:50:58.479
treasure fleets would sail as far west

03:50:58.479 --> 03:51:01.520
as the straight of Hormuz, the city of

03:51:01.520 --> 03:51:05.359
Mecca and Moadishu and Mombasa on the

03:51:05.359 --> 03:51:08.080
East African coast.

03:51:08.080 --> 03:51:11.279
But eventually the Ming would turn away

03:51:11.279 --> 03:51:15.800
from oceangoing exploration.

03:51:24.399 --> 03:51:27.279
When the adventurous Yong Lur emperor

03:51:27.279 --> 03:51:29.920
died, he was replaced by more

03:51:29.920 --> 03:51:32.399
inward-looking rulers who focused

03:51:32.399 --> 03:51:35.040
instead on the construction of the Great

03:51:35.040 --> 03:51:37.760
Wall in the north.

03:51:37.760 --> 03:51:40.399
At one point, the Ming even outlawed the

03:51:40.399 --> 03:51:43.680
construction of large ships, dismantling

03:51:43.680 --> 03:51:46.319
some and perhaps even burning some

03:51:46.319 --> 03:51:49.359
vessels in harbor.

03:51:49.359 --> 03:51:52.160
But the decades when the vast treasure

03:51:52.160 --> 03:51:55.040
fleets had sailed the seas left a

03:51:55.040 --> 03:51:57.680
lasting impression on every culture that

03:51:57.680 --> 03:51:59.680
they touched,

03:51:59.680 --> 03:52:02.880
and the damage done to the image of

03:52:02.880 --> 03:52:07.960
Javanese power was immense.

03:52:11.040 --> 03:52:14.239
Eventually, the regreg civil war would

03:52:14.239 --> 03:52:17.760
come to an end in Java and the western

03:52:17.760 --> 03:52:21.520
king Vikramina Haim Wuruk's son-in-law

03:52:21.520 --> 03:52:24.080
would be victorious.

03:52:24.080 --> 03:52:26.960
Despite his humiliating and bankrupting

03:52:26.960 --> 03:52:29.520
experience of angering the Chinese

03:52:29.520 --> 03:52:32.319
emperor, he managed to close in on his

03:52:32.319 --> 03:52:35.279
enemies in the eastern court. And in the

03:52:35.279 --> 03:52:38.160
final bloody confrontation, the western

03:52:38.160 --> 03:52:41.120
forces broke through the walls of the

03:52:41.120 --> 03:52:43.439
eastern palace.

03:52:43.439 --> 03:52:46.880
The lord of Fraabumi fled in the night

03:52:46.880 --> 03:52:49.760
and escaped by boat.

03:52:49.760 --> 03:52:52.960
He was hunted down and beheaded and his

03:52:52.960 --> 03:52:55.439
severed head was brought back to the

03:52:55.439 --> 03:52:59.720
capital of Majapahit.

03:52:59.760 --> 03:53:03.120
The civil war was over and the kingdom

03:53:03.120 --> 03:53:06.800
was united once more. But the conflict

03:53:06.800 --> 03:53:10.720
had exacted a terrible cost.

03:53:10.720 --> 03:53:13.279
In only 2 years of fighting, the

03:53:13.279 --> 03:53:16.399
manpower of Majapahit had been severely

03:53:16.399 --> 03:53:19.439
depleted. Its treasury was on the verge

03:53:19.439 --> 03:53:22.880
of bankruptcy and its influence had been

03:53:22.880 --> 03:53:25.680
drastically curtailed right at the point

03:53:25.680 --> 03:53:28.399
when powerful rivals were rising in the

03:53:28.399 --> 03:53:31.439
north and the religion of Islam was

03:53:31.439 --> 03:53:35.040
spreading from port to port.

03:53:35.040 --> 03:53:38.399
The center of the mandala of power had

03:53:38.399 --> 03:53:42.399
now shifted irrevocably away from Java.

03:53:42.399 --> 03:53:45.439
And the age of Majapahit's Empire of the

03:53:45.439 --> 03:53:49.120
Islands would slowly but surely come to

03:53:49.120 --> 03:53:52.439
an end.

03:53:59.920 --> 03:54:02.800
While Majapahit lost much of its

03:54:02.800 --> 03:54:05.439
overseas empire through the beginning of

03:54:05.439 --> 03:54:08.880
the 15th century, it still remained the

03:54:08.880 --> 03:54:12.479
preeeminent power on the island of Java.

03:54:12.479 --> 03:54:15.359
But steadily, its loss of regional

03:54:15.359 --> 03:54:19.359
status began to erode its power even in

03:54:19.359 --> 03:54:22.760
its heartlands.

03:54:23.439 --> 03:54:28.000
When King Vikram Vodina died in 1429,

03:54:28.000 --> 03:54:30.319
his daughter Suittita took to the

03:54:30.319 --> 03:54:32.479
throne.

03:54:32.479 --> 03:54:34.479
She was prepared to rule in the

03:54:34.479 --> 03:54:37.199
tradition of the great Javanese queens

03:54:37.199 --> 03:54:40.560
who had preceded her a century earlier.

03:54:40.560 --> 03:54:43.680
Diaragatry and Tribuano Vijaya

03:54:43.680 --> 03:54:47.199
Tungadevi. But for a number of reasons,

03:54:47.199 --> 03:54:52.760
her rule would be beset by problems.

03:54:53.199 --> 03:54:56.399
Chief among these was a terrible famine

03:54:56.399 --> 03:54:59.439
that descended on Java around the year

03:54:59.439 --> 03:55:01.199
1426

03:55:01.199 --> 03:55:04.399
caused by a drought.

03:55:04.399 --> 03:55:06.560
But the only source for this is the

03:55:06.560 --> 03:55:09.760
chronicle of the Paraton

03:55:09.760 --> 03:55:12.160
and by this point its reports are

03:55:12.160 --> 03:55:15.680
becoming sparse and scarce and contain

03:55:15.680 --> 03:55:19.239
little detail.

03:55:25.199 --> 03:55:27.439
Next, there was a period of food

03:55:27.439 --> 03:55:30.239
shortage that was very long in the year

03:55:30.239 --> 03:55:34.680
of the serpents biting people.

03:55:34.720 --> 03:55:37.040
Unfortunately for historians, the

03:55:37.040 --> 03:55:40.239
decline of royal power in Java also

03:55:40.239 --> 03:55:43.040
resulted in a disruption of the major

03:55:43.040 --> 03:55:46.239
sources that we have relied on up to

03:55:46.239 --> 03:55:47.920
this point.

03:55:47.920 --> 03:55:51.600
Narrative texts like the paraton or book

03:55:51.600 --> 03:55:54.880
of kings were crucial sources during the

03:55:54.880 --> 03:55:58.399
golden age of Majapahit. But as we enter

03:55:58.399 --> 03:56:01.279
the 15th century, the text becomes

03:56:01.279 --> 03:56:04.239
increasingly obscure and difficult to

03:56:04.239 --> 03:56:05.920
understand.

03:56:05.920 --> 03:56:08.640
The chronicles notes get shorter

03:56:08.640 --> 03:56:10.720
concerning only earthquakes and

03:56:10.720 --> 03:56:13.920
eruptions and the deaths of kings and

03:56:13.920 --> 03:56:18.160
they come further and further apart.

03:56:18.160 --> 03:56:20.960
The final three pages of the Javanese

03:56:20.960 --> 03:56:24.239
Book of Kings are just a few scraps of

03:56:24.239 --> 03:56:26.800
seemingly unrelated information

03:56:26.800 --> 03:56:30.479
separated by decades with its final note

03:56:30.479 --> 03:56:34.600
coming in 1481.

03:56:41.120 --> 03:56:44.239
Then a volcanic eruption occurred in the

03:56:44.239 --> 03:56:47.279
wake of Watu Ganung in the Saka action

03:56:47.279 --> 03:56:51.319
of the sky sea echore

03:56:51.600 --> 03:56:54.239
perhaps in an attempt to alleviate the

03:56:54.239 --> 03:56:56.960
effects of the drought. Suitta had

03:56:56.960 --> 03:57:00.640
constructed a vast reservoir named Kolam

03:57:00.640 --> 03:57:03.600
Seagaran just to the north of the city

03:57:03.600 --> 03:57:05.760
of Majapahit.

03:57:05.760 --> 03:57:10.640
This great pool was 800 m by 500 and

03:57:10.640 --> 03:57:15.120
ringed all around by banks of red brick.

03:57:15.120 --> 03:57:17.279
Whether or not this alleviated the

03:57:17.279 --> 03:57:20.319
famine, we will never know. But it shows

03:57:20.319 --> 03:57:22.880
the drastic situation that the empire

03:57:22.880 --> 03:57:25.680
was facing around this time under

03:57:25.680 --> 03:57:28.399
pressure from the environment, from

03:57:28.399 --> 03:57:31.120
internal divisions, and increasingly

03:57:31.120 --> 03:57:34.960
from powerful rivals.

03:57:34.960 --> 03:57:38.479
When Suhita died in 1447,

03:57:38.479 --> 03:57:41.680
her brother Ka Vagaya ruled for only

03:57:41.680 --> 03:57:43.600
four years.

03:57:43.600 --> 03:57:47.040
He was followed by a further four kings,

03:57:47.040 --> 03:57:50.399
all of whom ruled for only a short time,

03:57:50.399 --> 03:57:52.880
and the relationships between them are

03:57:52.880 --> 03:57:55.880
unclear.

03:57:56.640 --> 03:57:59.439
The kingdom erupted in civil war again

03:57:59.439 --> 03:58:01.600
in the 1470s.

03:58:01.600 --> 03:58:03.600
And in 1478,

03:58:03.600 --> 03:58:06.080
one pretender broke through the defenses

03:58:06.080 --> 03:58:09.279
of Majapahit and killed his brother who

03:58:09.279 --> 03:58:12.399
sat on the throne.

03:58:12.399 --> 03:58:15.760
That year in Java would be given a name

03:58:15.760 --> 03:58:18.319
that seems to convey the mood in the

03:58:18.319 --> 03:58:22.800
kingdom at the time. Sir Elanging Bumi,

03:58:22.800 --> 03:58:25.520
which has been translated as vanished

03:58:25.520 --> 03:58:30.640
and lost is the order of the world.

03:58:30.640 --> 03:58:33.680
Upon his victory, this new king had

03:58:33.680 --> 03:58:36.960
inscribed a series of stone inscriptions

03:58:36.960 --> 03:58:39.840
that made dire warnings of the fate that

03:58:39.840 --> 03:58:42.800
would befall any who failed to support

03:58:42.800 --> 03:58:46.199
his rule.

03:58:48.000 --> 03:58:50.880
They will end up in the realm of Yama,

03:58:50.880 --> 03:58:53.520
the king of the dead.

03:58:53.520 --> 03:58:55.920
They will be beaten by Yama's army for

03:58:55.920 --> 03:58:58.239
years innumerable.

03:58:58.239 --> 03:59:01.439
They will fall in the cauldron of hell.

03:59:01.439 --> 03:59:04.399
They will not be reborn.

03:59:04.399 --> 03:59:06.399
So, not only will they end up in hell,

03:59:06.399 --> 03:59:09.040
but they will stay there. And even if

03:59:09.040 --> 03:59:11.680
they are reborn, they will be reborn

03:59:11.680 --> 03:59:15.800
under miserable circumstances.

03:59:17.359 --> 03:59:19.920
It seems clear from these inscriptions

03:59:19.920 --> 03:59:22.880
that the new king didn't feel at all

03:59:22.880 --> 03:59:26.399
secure on the throne.

03:59:26.399 --> 03:59:28.640
Throughout this period of political

03:59:28.640 --> 03:59:32.080
instability, the situation for Majapay

03:59:32.080 --> 03:59:34.800
would be made increasingly worse by the

03:59:34.800 --> 03:59:37.680
rise of a new kind of power on the

03:59:37.680 --> 03:59:40.319
coasts of Java.

03:59:40.319 --> 03:59:43.920
That is the everinccreasing influence of

03:59:43.920 --> 03:59:47.560
Muslim traders

04:00:07.279 --> 04:00:11.120
with the powerful rival of Mal. Laka now

04:00:11.120 --> 04:00:14.640
exerting its influence. Muslim merchants

04:00:14.640 --> 04:00:17.040
had become wealthier and more

04:00:17.040 --> 04:00:21.199
influential in Java than ever before.

04:00:21.199 --> 04:00:24.560
And in the vacuum left by royal power,

04:00:24.560 --> 04:00:27.120
these wealthy merchants became

04:00:27.120 --> 04:00:30.800
politically powerful too.

04:00:30.800 --> 04:00:33.680
Now more and more people on the coasts

04:00:33.680 --> 04:00:36.560
all around the archipelago began to

04:00:36.560 --> 04:00:39.279
flirt with the idea of this new

04:00:39.279 --> 04:00:40.960
religion.

04:00:40.960 --> 04:00:44.319
The Portuguese traveler Tom Perez

04:00:44.319 --> 04:00:47.359
describes the steady advance of Islamic

04:00:47.359 --> 04:00:50.720
power in Java at the expense of the

04:00:50.720 --> 04:00:56.199
Hindu Buddhists who he calls heathens.

04:00:57.920 --> 04:00:59.840
At the time when there were heathens

04:00:59.840 --> 04:01:02.399
along the sea coast of Jaba, many

04:01:02.399 --> 04:01:06.080
merchants used to come. Paris, Arabs,

04:01:06.080 --> 04:01:09.439
Gujaratis, Bengales, Malaise and other

04:01:09.439 --> 04:01:10.960
nationalities.

04:01:10.960 --> 04:01:13.920
There being many Moors among them. They

04:01:13.920 --> 04:01:16.160
began to trade in the country and to

04:01:16.160 --> 04:01:18.000
grow rich.

04:01:18.000 --> 04:01:20.720
They succeeded in way of making mosques

04:01:20.720 --> 04:01:24.080
and mulas came from outside.

04:01:24.080 --> 04:01:26.319
In some places the heathen Japanese

04:01:26.319 --> 04:01:29.040
lords themselves turned muhamadan and

04:01:29.040 --> 04:01:31.199
these merchant moors took possession of

04:01:31.199 --> 04:01:34.600
these places.

04:01:36.800 --> 04:01:39.279
The growing influence of these coastal

04:01:39.279 --> 04:01:43.040
traders would culminate in 1475

04:01:43.040 --> 04:01:45.760
with the foundation of a true Muslim

04:01:45.760 --> 04:01:49.600
kingdom on the island of Java. A power

04:01:49.600 --> 04:01:52.479
that would call itself the sultenate of

04:01:52.479 --> 04:01:55.279
Denmark.

04:02:01.680 --> 04:02:04.800
A port town looking north into the Java

04:02:04.800 --> 04:02:07.520
Sea, Denmark had been founded in the

04:02:07.520 --> 04:02:10.800
late 15th century, possibly by Chinese

04:02:10.800 --> 04:02:13.439
merchants, and its people had built a

04:02:13.439 --> 04:02:16.239
grand mosque there, combining elements

04:02:16.239 --> 04:02:21.560
of Muslim and Javanese architecture.

04:02:22.000 --> 04:02:25.520
The ruler of Damak was a man named Raden

04:02:25.520 --> 04:02:28.239
Pata who was a vassel swearing

04:02:28.239 --> 04:02:31.439
allegiance to Majapahit.

04:02:31.439 --> 04:02:34.399
But he soon declared independence and

04:02:34.399 --> 04:02:39.319
claimed the title of Sultan.

04:02:39.840 --> 04:02:43.199
As Majapahed declined, the Sultanate of

04:02:43.199 --> 04:02:46.479
Demach would expand.

04:02:46.479 --> 04:02:49.439
It conquered the coastal region of Tuban

04:02:49.439 --> 04:02:51.439
by 1527

04:02:51.439 --> 04:02:54.000
and was spreading in land as far as

04:02:54.000 --> 04:02:58.160
Malang by 1546.

04:02:58.160 --> 04:03:02.000
For the dwindling power of Majapet, this

04:03:02.000 --> 04:03:06.359
was the final death nail.

04:03:18.319 --> 04:03:20.800
Due to the slow petering out of royal

04:03:20.800 --> 04:03:24.080
chronicles in Java, we have few details

04:03:24.080 --> 04:03:26.960
about what exactly happened to lead to

04:03:26.960 --> 04:03:31.120
the eventual destruction of Majapahit.

04:03:31.120 --> 04:03:33.359
But at this point, we are able to turn

04:03:33.359 --> 04:03:36.720
to the writings of some outside visitors

04:03:36.720 --> 04:03:40.920
to the island of Java.

04:03:44.239 --> 04:03:46.800
Around 1513,

04:03:46.800 --> 04:03:49.520
about 100 years after the end of the

04:03:49.520 --> 04:03:52.800
Regreg War, the Portuguese traveler Tom

04:03:52.800 --> 04:03:57.160
Perez visited Java.

04:03:57.920 --> 04:04:00.399
He wrote in glowing terms about the

04:04:00.399 --> 04:04:02.640
beauty of the landscape and the

04:04:02.640 --> 04:04:05.920
abundance of the island. But he found

04:04:05.920 --> 04:04:09.520
the power of Majapahit already a shadow

04:04:09.520 --> 04:04:13.120
of its former glory. As he recounts in

04:04:13.120 --> 04:04:16.359
his memoirs,

04:04:16.720 --> 04:04:19.600
they say that the island of Jaba used to

04:04:19.600 --> 04:04:21.840
rule as far as the spice islands on the

04:04:21.840 --> 04:04:24.720
eastern side and over a great part of

04:04:24.720 --> 04:04:27.840
the west. and that it had almost all the

04:04:27.840 --> 04:04:30.479
islands of Somatra under its dominion

04:04:30.479 --> 04:04:32.319
and all the islands known to the

04:04:32.319 --> 04:04:34.080
Japanese

04:04:34.080 --> 04:04:37.600
and that it had all this for a long time

04:04:37.600 --> 04:04:41.520
passed until about a 100 years ago when

04:04:41.520 --> 04:04:44.399
its power began to diminish and it came

04:04:44.399 --> 04:04:48.279
to its present state.

04:04:49.680 --> 04:04:52.720
Perez also alludes to some degree of

04:04:52.720 --> 04:04:56.239
political instability in Java. According

04:04:56.239 --> 04:04:59.040
to his account, the power of its kings

04:04:59.040 --> 04:05:01.359
had diminished so that they were now

04:05:01.359 --> 04:05:04.239
little more than a figurehead with the

04:05:04.239 --> 04:05:07.120
Mahapati or prime minister appearing to

04:05:07.120 --> 04:05:11.319
wield greater power.

04:05:11.760 --> 04:05:13.840
Because the Japanese have lost a great

04:05:13.840 --> 04:05:16.080
part of their lands, the kings do not

04:05:16.080 --> 04:05:18.399
command, nor are they taken into

04:05:18.399 --> 04:05:21.520
account, but only the viceroy and chief

04:05:21.520 --> 04:05:24.640
captain. This man is known and honored

04:05:24.640 --> 04:05:27.439
like the real king. All the lords of

04:05:27.439 --> 04:05:31.439
Java obey him. Him they honor. This

04:05:31.439 --> 04:05:33.920
governor commands in everything. He

04:05:33.920 --> 04:05:36.640
holds the king of Java in his hands. He

04:05:36.640 --> 04:05:39.359
orders him to be given food.

04:05:39.359 --> 04:05:43.199
The king has no voice in anything, nor

04:05:43.199 --> 04:05:47.319
is he of any importance.

04:05:48.640 --> 04:05:51.199
Alongside this weakening of royal

04:05:51.199 --> 04:05:54.720
authority came the fragmentation of the

04:05:54.720 --> 04:05:56.319
kingdom.

04:05:56.319 --> 04:05:58.960
Local lords became steadily more

04:05:58.960 --> 04:06:02.640
powerful with some even breaking away.

04:06:02.640 --> 04:06:06.160
And now the Muslim sultenates began to

04:06:06.160 --> 04:06:10.160
taste blood in the water.

04:06:21.199 --> 04:06:24.800
The sultan of the city of Demach, Raden

04:06:24.800 --> 04:06:27.920
Pa, knew that only one thing stood

04:06:27.920 --> 04:06:30.720
between him and ultimate power on the

04:06:30.720 --> 04:06:33.439
island of Java.

04:06:33.439 --> 04:06:36.319
That was the lingering remnants of

04:06:36.319 --> 04:06:39.319
Majapahit.

04:06:39.439 --> 04:06:42.399
After only a few years, he gathered his

04:06:42.399 --> 04:06:45.920
forces and marched on the now isolated

04:06:45.920 --> 04:06:48.479
city.

04:06:48.479 --> 04:06:51.680
The later Muslim epic verse chronicle,

04:06:51.680 --> 04:06:54.560
the Babad Tana Jawi, recounts what

04:06:54.560 --> 04:06:58.080
happened next in heroic terms as the

04:06:58.080 --> 04:07:01.199
Muslim forces bore down on the once

04:07:01.199 --> 04:07:05.279
great capital city.

04:07:05.279 --> 04:07:08.080
Then they agree to gather together all

04:07:08.080 --> 04:07:10.640
Muslims with their arms. Then they set

04:07:10.640 --> 04:07:12.720
out to Majapahed.

04:07:12.720 --> 04:07:15.120
The number of troops was immeasurable.

04:07:15.120 --> 04:07:18.800
The city of Majapahed was encircled.

04:07:18.800 --> 04:07:22.560
Many inhabitants submitted to Raden Pa.

04:07:22.560 --> 04:07:27.080
Nobody dared to meet him in battle.

04:07:27.840 --> 04:07:30.720
Marching under blue and yellow banners,

04:07:30.720 --> 04:07:33.359
they soon arrived at the walls of

04:07:33.359 --> 04:07:36.359
Majapahit.

04:07:36.399 --> 04:07:39.199
The later Muslim chronicles imitated

04:07:39.199 --> 04:07:42.800
elements of previous Javanese legends

04:07:42.800 --> 04:07:45.199
and claimed that the last king of

04:07:45.199 --> 04:07:48.479
Majapahit was so aed at the sight of the

04:07:48.479 --> 04:07:51.439
army approaching the city that he simply

04:07:51.439 --> 04:07:53.920
ascended to heaven right there on the

04:07:53.920 --> 04:07:56.800
spot and the city was captured

04:07:56.800 --> 04:07:59.800
peacefully.

04:07:59.840 --> 04:08:03.040
At the moment Prabhu Bra with Jaya

04:08:03.040 --> 04:08:05.600
ascended to heaven, something like a

04:08:05.600 --> 04:08:07.680
fireball was seen coming out of the

04:08:07.680 --> 04:08:10.080
palace of Maja,

04:08:10.080 --> 04:08:12.640
it flashed like a bolt of lightning and

04:08:12.640 --> 04:08:15.680
sounded like a terrifying thunderclap.

04:08:15.680 --> 04:08:18.800
It fell down in Binda.

04:08:18.800 --> 04:08:21.840
Radan Pa entered the palace. He was

04:08:21.840 --> 04:08:24.000
astonished that he did not encounter a

04:08:24.000 --> 04:08:28.000
single person. He wept in his heart,

04:08:28.000 --> 04:08:30.720
then left the palace and returned to

04:08:30.720 --> 04:08:34.840
Bintara with his troops.

04:08:36.640 --> 04:08:38.720
But we can assume that the end of

04:08:38.720 --> 04:08:42.080
Majapahit was not as peaceful as these

04:08:42.080 --> 04:08:45.439
later chronicers make out.

04:08:45.439 --> 04:08:48.720
The historian Herald Vanderinda imagines

04:08:48.720 --> 04:08:51.760
an extreme version of the scenes that

04:08:51.760 --> 04:08:54.760
unfolded.

04:08:55.279 --> 04:08:58.080
The soldiers met almost no resistance

04:08:58.080 --> 04:09:00.319
and within an hour they had taken

04:09:00.319 --> 04:09:03.359
control of the royal palace.

04:09:03.359 --> 04:09:06.560
It was a massacre. Priests were drowned

04:09:06.560 --> 04:09:10.319
in lotus ponds. Stable boys were stabbed

04:09:10.319 --> 04:09:12.239
as they tried to protect the king's

04:09:12.239 --> 04:09:13.760
horses.

04:09:13.760 --> 04:09:16.080
Everything was burned to the ground. The

04:09:16.080 --> 04:09:18.800
royal residences, the watchtower, the

04:09:18.800 --> 04:09:20.800
pavilion with its intricate wood

04:09:20.800 --> 04:09:23.600
carvings, the army barracks, the

04:09:23.600 --> 04:09:27.040
elephant stalls, and the library.

04:09:27.040 --> 04:09:30.800
By noon, all that was left of Maja Pahit

04:09:30.800 --> 04:09:34.760
was a heap of rubble.

04:09:37.199 --> 04:09:39.920
However, there is little evidence of

04:09:39.920 --> 04:09:42.080
widespread burning at the site of the

04:09:42.080 --> 04:09:43.120
city.

04:09:43.120 --> 04:09:46.800
and no heaps of bodies or mass graves

04:09:46.800 --> 04:09:49.439
have ever been found.

04:09:49.439 --> 04:09:52.479
But what's clear is that at this point,

04:09:52.479 --> 04:09:54.800
human habitation at the city of

04:09:54.800 --> 04:10:00.520
Majapahit largely came to an end.

04:10:03.520 --> 04:10:06.880
Its people fled and all of its houses

04:10:06.880 --> 04:10:10.720
and workshops, its temples and palaces

04:10:10.720 --> 04:10:15.960
were left to fade and crumble.

04:10:16.080 --> 04:10:19.439
For many ordinary people, life simply

04:10:19.439 --> 04:10:22.720
went on. But it must have been a time of

04:10:22.720 --> 04:10:26.880
great upheaval and confusion.

04:10:26.880 --> 04:10:30.479
The Javanese text, the Niti Shastra,

04:10:30.479 --> 04:10:33.359
records one vision of the end of the

04:10:33.359 --> 04:10:36.239
world that must have captured the mood

04:10:36.239 --> 04:10:40.000
of many on the island of Java as their

04:10:40.000 --> 04:10:46.439
world came to an end and another began.

04:10:47.120 --> 04:10:49.600
The signs of the approaching end of this

04:10:49.600 --> 04:10:52.560
world will be all kinds of depravity

04:10:52.560 --> 04:10:56.479
among mankind. That is to say, the wise

04:10:56.479 --> 04:10:59.680
will turn foolish. The holy men will

04:10:59.680 --> 04:11:02.640
become worldly. Children will abandon

04:11:02.640 --> 04:11:05.760
their parents. Princes will lose their

04:11:05.760 --> 04:11:07.520
empires.

04:11:07.520 --> 04:11:10.960
The little will become great and commit

04:11:10.960 --> 04:11:12.720
depradations.

04:11:12.720 --> 04:11:16.399
In short, everything will be in

04:11:16.399 --> 04:11:19.399
confusion.

04:11:31.760 --> 04:11:34.479
From this moment on, the Sultanate of

04:11:34.479 --> 04:11:37.359
Demach would be the most powerful force

04:11:37.359 --> 04:11:41.279
on the island of Java and the age of the

04:11:41.279 --> 04:11:43.760
Hindu Buddhist kingdoms on the island

04:11:43.760 --> 04:11:47.199
would come to an end.

04:11:47.199 --> 04:11:50.080
Most remaining Hindus and Buddhists

04:11:50.080 --> 04:11:53.279
would flee east and took refuge on the

04:11:53.279 --> 04:11:56.800
small island of Bali which became a

04:11:56.800 --> 04:12:01.800
sanctuary for their ancient culture.

04:12:02.479 --> 04:12:06.000
Epic Hindu poems like the Bulman Taka

04:12:06.000 --> 04:12:08.720
were largely forgotten on the mainland

04:12:08.720 --> 04:12:14.560
of Java but in Bali they were preserved.

04:12:14.560 --> 04:12:17.840
One verse in this poem describes the

04:12:17.840 --> 04:12:21.279
destruction wrought by a demon king on

04:12:21.279 --> 04:12:24.319
the religious sanctuaries of a kingdom.

04:12:24.319 --> 04:12:26.239
And we might find it a fitting

04:12:26.239 --> 04:12:30.000
description for the final days of Java's

04:12:30.000 --> 04:12:35.000
last Hindu Buddhist sanctuaries.

04:12:35.760 --> 04:12:39.040
Heaven is being destroyed and hermitage

04:12:39.040 --> 04:12:41.600
is swept away because of the swarming

04:12:41.600 --> 04:12:43.199
demons.

04:12:43.199 --> 04:12:45.760
The hermits have left, have abandoned

04:12:45.760 --> 04:12:48.319
all and fled far away, constantly

04:12:48.319 --> 04:12:50.080
pursued

04:12:50.080 --> 04:12:52.640
the miserable wretches.

04:12:52.640 --> 04:12:54.640
Their bodies are lying about in the

04:12:54.640 --> 04:12:57.920
monasteries with their bark clothing and

04:12:57.920 --> 04:13:02.279
woven bags flung away.

04:13:03.279 --> 04:13:06.159
With its people gone, the city of

04:13:06.159 --> 04:13:08.800
Majapay would have been swiftly

04:13:08.800 --> 04:13:11.840
reclaimed by the fast growing forest

04:13:11.840 --> 04:13:15.239
around it.

04:13:16.319 --> 04:13:18.880
The sophisticated drainage system that

04:13:18.880 --> 04:13:21.520
its engineers had spent generations

04:13:21.520 --> 04:13:24.640
perfecting that channels the slooes and

04:13:24.640 --> 04:13:27.199
great reservoirs would have begun to

04:13:27.199 --> 04:13:29.840
silt up within a decade without

04:13:29.840 --> 04:13:33.120
maintenance. The water with nowhere left

04:13:33.120 --> 04:13:36.319
to go would have pulled and spread,

04:13:36.319 --> 04:13:39.279
turning streets into marshland and

04:13:39.279 --> 04:13:42.479
marshland into swamp.

04:13:42.479 --> 04:13:44.880
The red bricks that gave the ruins of

04:13:44.880 --> 04:13:48.640
Majapahit its distinctive character were

04:13:48.640 --> 04:13:52.000
fired from the volcanic clay of the Bras

04:13:52.000 --> 04:13:54.960
River plane. And in the wet heat of

04:13:54.960 --> 04:13:59.199
Java, they didn't last long.

04:13:59.199 --> 04:14:02.479
Mosses would take hold first, then

04:14:02.479 --> 04:14:06.720
lychans and ferns. The mortar softened

04:14:06.720 --> 04:14:10.159
and dissolved. The strangler figs and

04:14:10.159 --> 04:14:13.040
banyan trees would move in next,

04:14:13.040 --> 04:14:15.600
clambering over the red brick courtyards

04:14:15.600 --> 04:14:19.120
and ceremonial gateways of the Majapahit

04:14:19.120 --> 04:14:22.640
capital. their roots clenching the walls

04:14:22.640 --> 04:14:26.239
in their grasp and steadily but surely

04:14:26.239 --> 04:14:29.439
pulverizing the brick.

04:14:29.439 --> 04:14:32.479
Slower growing teak and mahogany trees

04:14:32.479 --> 04:14:35.680
would arrive next, shading the crumbling

04:14:35.680 --> 04:14:38.800
walls of Majapahit beneath their

04:14:38.800 --> 04:14:40.479
canopies.

04:14:40.479 --> 04:14:43.760
As all this went on, the great rumblings

04:14:43.760 --> 04:14:47.040
of Java's volcanoes would have conspired

04:14:47.040 --> 04:14:51.199
to hide the ruins even further.

04:14:51.199 --> 04:14:53.840
More than 10 major eruptions of the

04:14:53.840 --> 04:14:57.760
nearby Arjuno Wellerang and Anjas Moro

04:14:57.760 --> 04:15:00.319
volcanoes took place in the centuries

04:15:00.319 --> 04:15:03.199
that followed. Each one burying the site

04:15:03.199 --> 04:15:07.520
of Majapahit in ever more ash until some

04:15:07.520 --> 04:15:11.040
of its structures lay as much as 4 m

04:15:11.040 --> 04:15:14.239
beneath the surface of the earth.

04:15:14.239 --> 04:15:16.479
In the year 1849,

04:15:16.479 --> 04:15:19.120
a Dutch traveler called Walter Robert

04:15:19.120 --> 04:15:22.080
Van Hovl passed through the site of the

04:15:22.080 --> 04:15:25.760
old city and described the overgrown

04:15:25.760 --> 04:15:30.439
ruins that still remained.

04:15:31.760 --> 04:15:34.000
The entire ruins were shrouded in a dark

04:15:34.000 --> 04:15:37.439
forest and covered with shrs and trees.

04:15:37.439 --> 04:15:39.520
Majestic Banyan trees have rooted their

04:15:39.520 --> 04:15:41.760
roots between the stones and pushed

04:15:41.760 --> 04:15:44.399
walls apart, raising their crowns high

04:15:44.399 --> 04:15:46.399
above the ruins.

04:15:46.399 --> 04:15:48.640
That is why nowadays the Javanese also

04:15:48.640 --> 04:15:52.159
call the place Waning Lang or Banyan

04:15:52.159 --> 04:15:55.159
Gate.

04:16:02.960 --> 04:16:06.000
The Muslim sultenates that destroyed

04:16:06.000 --> 04:16:08.960
Majapahit would not remain the most

04:16:08.960 --> 04:16:13.279
powerful force in Java for long.

04:16:13.279 --> 04:16:15.920
The next century would see the arrival

04:16:15.920 --> 04:16:19.600
of other seaborn powers that would soon

04:16:19.600 --> 04:16:22.479
form their ownthaloscracies

04:16:22.479 --> 04:16:25.760
or empires of the sea.

04:16:25.760 --> 04:16:28.880
These were the powers of European

04:16:28.880 --> 04:16:31.359
colonialism.

04:16:31.359 --> 04:16:35.279
In 1511, the port town of Malaka was

04:16:35.279 --> 04:16:38.720
seized by the Portuguese and from there

04:16:38.720 --> 04:16:41.439
their influence would spread all over

04:16:41.439 --> 04:16:44.760
the archipelago.

04:16:45.040 --> 04:16:48.399
Soon other European powers would arrive

04:16:48.399 --> 04:16:50.800
and they would all begin to influence

04:16:50.800 --> 04:16:53.600
the fracturous political life of the

04:16:53.600 --> 04:16:56.399
island of Java and introduce the

04:16:56.399 --> 04:16:59.359
beginnings of an ideology more seductive

04:16:59.359 --> 04:17:02.880
and powerful than any religion, the

04:17:02.880 --> 04:17:06.560
force of capitalism.

04:17:06.560 --> 04:17:09.199
The Sultanates of Java would soon come

04:17:09.199 --> 04:17:11.600
under the sway of a massive

04:17:11.600 --> 04:17:14.560
international conglomerate and one of

04:17:14.560 --> 04:17:17.279
the first joint stock companies in the

04:17:17.279 --> 04:17:21.600
world, the Dutch East India Company.

04:17:21.600 --> 04:17:25.600
In 1598, a Dutch fleet of eight ships

04:17:25.600 --> 04:17:28.399
under Jacob Van Neck became the first

04:17:28.399 --> 04:17:31.120
from the Netherlands to reach the spice

04:17:31.120 --> 04:17:34.319
islands of Maluku.

04:17:34.319 --> 04:17:38.080
In doing so, they bypassed the Javanese

04:17:38.080 --> 04:17:40.960
merchants who had long dominated the

04:17:40.960 --> 04:17:42.960
trade.

04:17:42.960 --> 04:17:45.680
When these Dutch ships returned to

04:17:45.680 --> 04:17:48.640
Europe in the year 1599,

04:17:48.640 --> 04:17:52.560
laden with cloves, nutmeg, and mace, the

04:17:52.560 --> 04:17:55.840
expedition yielded an enormous profit of

04:17:55.840 --> 04:17:59.439
around 400%.

04:17:59.439 --> 04:18:02.960
One Dutch observer would reportedly make

04:18:02.960 --> 04:18:05.760
the following remark upon seeing the

04:18:05.760 --> 04:18:10.040
arrival of this fleet.

04:18:10.159 --> 04:18:12.640
As long as Holland has been Holland,

04:18:12.640 --> 04:18:15.279
there have never arrived ships as richly

04:18:15.279 --> 04:18:18.920
laden as these.

04:18:19.439 --> 04:18:22.479
The age of European colonialism in

04:18:22.479 --> 04:18:27.040
Southeast Asia had now begun.

04:18:27.040 --> 04:18:28.720
Between6602

04:18:28.720 --> 04:18:30.880
and 1796,

04:18:30.880 --> 04:18:33.600
the Dutch East India Company dispatched

04:18:33.600 --> 04:18:36.640
almost a million Europeans to Asia

04:18:36.640 --> 04:18:40.640
aboard nearly 5,000 ships, dwarfing the

04:18:40.640 --> 04:18:42.960
traffic of its nearest rival, the

04:18:42.960 --> 04:18:45.840
British East India Company, returning

04:18:45.840 --> 04:18:49.680
with more than 2.5 million tons of Asian

04:18:49.680 --> 04:18:54.000
goods and enslaved people.

04:18:54.000 --> 04:18:56.319
Throughout

04:18:56.319 --> 04:18:58.880
this colonial period, which would

04:18:58.880 --> 04:19:02.080
ultimately see Java become a European

04:19:02.080 --> 04:19:05.040
colony, the legacy of the ancient

04:19:05.040 --> 04:19:09.120
Javanese kingdoms was largely ignored or

04:19:09.120 --> 04:19:11.840
intentionally obscured.

04:19:11.840 --> 04:19:14.880
The Dutch in particular had no desire to

04:19:14.880 --> 04:19:17.439
see the people of their new colonies

04:19:17.439 --> 04:19:20.239
rally around the memory of any ancient

04:19:20.239 --> 04:19:23.040
kingdoms and mostly declined to

04:19:23.040 --> 04:19:25.199
investigate the ruins that could be

04:19:25.199 --> 04:19:29.120
found dotted around Java.

04:19:29.120 --> 04:19:32.880
The erasia was so extensive that in his

04:19:32.880 --> 04:19:35.520
history of the Indian archipelago

04:19:35.520 --> 04:19:38.880
published in 1820, the British writer

04:19:38.880 --> 04:19:42.000
John Crawford was able to write the

04:19:42.000 --> 04:19:44.159
following.

04:19:44.159 --> 04:19:46.080
The theory of a great monarchy and of an

04:19:46.080 --> 04:19:48.080
antecedent state of high civilization

04:19:48.080 --> 04:19:50.239
and improvement has been forged by the

04:19:50.239 --> 04:19:52.560
national vanity of the Javanese

04:19:52.560 --> 04:19:55.199
unsupported by a shadow of proof and

04:19:55.199 --> 04:19:57.439
contradicted by unquestionable internal

04:19:57.439 --> 04:20:00.439
evidence.

04:20:02.560 --> 04:20:06.399
But some memory of Majapahit's glory

04:20:06.399 --> 04:20:10.399
lived on in the minds of Java's people

04:20:10.399 --> 04:20:13.600
in their songs, their poetry, their

04:20:13.600 --> 04:20:16.640
shadow puppet plays, and in the

04:20:16.640 --> 04:20:19.120
manuscripts they kept in their

04:20:19.120 --> 04:20:22.120
libraries.

04:20:24.479 --> 04:20:26.399
In 1894,

04:20:26.399 --> 04:20:29.520
in a typical expansion of European power

04:20:29.520 --> 04:20:32.319
in East Asia, the Dutch colonialist

04:20:32.319 --> 04:20:35.120
government intervened on the island of

04:20:35.120 --> 04:20:39.040
Lombok to the west of Bali to depose its

04:20:39.040 --> 04:20:43.920
king, a man named Aung Ketut Karangasam,

04:20:43.920 --> 04:20:46.880
who was a renowned collector of ancient

04:20:46.880 --> 04:20:49.199
texts.

04:20:49.199 --> 04:20:51.760
After a protracted war in which the

04:20:51.760 --> 04:20:54.479
local people resisted fiercely, the

04:20:54.479 --> 04:20:57.760
Maharaja's palace was finally stormed by

04:20:57.760 --> 04:21:00.880
Dutch marines on the 19th of November

04:21:00.880 --> 04:21:03.880
1894.

04:21:03.920 --> 04:21:06.800
The Dutch poured into the palace and

04:21:06.800 --> 04:21:10.319
began a slaughter in which 2,000 were

04:21:10.319 --> 04:21:12.479
massacred.

04:21:12.479 --> 04:21:16.319
The Maharaja was captured and died a few

04:21:16.319 --> 04:21:19.840
months later in a colonial prison.

04:21:19.840 --> 04:21:22.720
During the fighting, Dutch artillery set

04:21:22.720 --> 04:21:25.680
fire to the Maharaja's palace. And while

04:21:25.680 --> 04:21:29.040
its towers burned and its roofs fell in,

04:21:29.040 --> 04:21:31.680
the colonial troops looted the king's

04:21:31.680 --> 04:21:35.520
treasury and carried away more than 130

04:21:35.520 --> 04:21:40.560
kg of gold, 3,000 of silver, and

04:21:40.560 --> 04:21:44.319
countless works of art.

04:21:44.319 --> 04:21:47.199
This would become known as the Lombok

04:21:47.199 --> 04:21:48.880
treasure.

04:21:48.880 --> 04:21:51.600
But among the lutters there was also a

04:21:51.600 --> 04:21:54.479
Dutchman named Yan Lawrence Andre

04:21:54.479 --> 04:21:58.880
Brandes an expert in Sanskrit and old

04:21:58.880 --> 04:22:00.800
Javanese.

04:22:00.800 --> 04:22:03.760
This man had heard that the Maharaja

04:22:03.760 --> 04:22:07.199
Karangasam was an avid scholar and a

04:22:07.199 --> 04:22:11.279
collector of rare manuscripts.

04:22:11.279 --> 04:22:14.560
As the Maharaja's palace burned, this

04:22:14.560 --> 04:22:18.239
man ran to the ruler's library and saved

04:22:18.239 --> 04:22:21.800
what he could.

04:22:23.199 --> 04:22:25.600
While others ran with gold heaped in

04:22:25.600 --> 04:22:28.880
their arms, Brandis frantically gathered

04:22:28.880 --> 04:22:31.680
all of the ancient books he could carry

04:22:31.680 --> 04:22:34.640
and fled before the roof of the palace

04:22:34.640 --> 04:22:37.680
could collapse.

04:22:37.680 --> 04:22:40.479
Much of the Maharaja's collection went

04:22:40.479 --> 04:22:43.199
up in flames, and we will never be able

04:22:43.199 --> 04:22:46.239
to read what was contained within it.

04:22:46.239 --> 04:22:48.800
But what Brandes was able to save was

04:22:48.800 --> 04:22:51.760
packed into a box and sent back to the

04:22:51.760 --> 04:22:55.319
colonial capital.

04:22:57.520 --> 04:23:00.399
Inside he would later find the only

04:23:00.399 --> 04:23:04.319
existing copy of the poem the desavana

04:23:04.319 --> 04:23:06.880
written by the self- aacing scribe

04:23:06.880 --> 04:23:11.680
propanka some 500 years earlier.

04:23:11.680 --> 04:23:14.479
In the pages of that work the voice of

04:23:14.479 --> 04:23:17.359
the poet could once more bring to life

04:23:17.359 --> 04:23:20.399
the description of its great king on his

04:23:20.399 --> 04:23:23.600
journey around the island. the lives and

04:23:23.600 --> 04:23:27.439
concerns of the people of medieval Java.

04:23:27.439 --> 04:23:31.040
And at least in words, the kingdom of

04:23:31.040 --> 04:23:36.920
Majapet could live once more.

04:23:59.840 --> 04:24:02.399
I'd like to end this episode with an

04:24:02.399 --> 04:24:06.640
extract from an old Javanese poem called

04:24:06.640 --> 04:24:10.319
the Shiva Ratri Kalpa or the night

04:24:10.319 --> 04:24:14.239
ritual of Shiva written during the years

04:24:14.239 --> 04:24:18.800
of the decline of the Majapahit kingdom.

04:24:18.800 --> 04:24:22.640
In this passage, a hunter named Lugdaka

04:24:22.640 --> 04:24:25.199
stumbles upon the ruins of an ancient

04:24:25.199 --> 04:24:29.279
temple and like Thomas Stamford Raffles

04:24:29.279 --> 04:24:32.239
centuries later, would be struck by the

04:24:32.239 --> 04:24:35.680
strange melancholy of these places where

04:24:35.680 --> 04:24:40.479
once so many lives passed, now overgrown

04:24:40.479 --> 04:24:43.800
with jungle.

04:24:47.359 --> 04:24:50.159
As you listen, imagine how it would feel

04:24:50.159 --> 04:24:53.520
to watch the palaces and temples of the

04:24:53.520 --> 04:24:56.800
kingdom of Majapah crumbling into the

04:24:56.800 --> 04:24:59.920
earth as its people left and its

04:24:59.920 --> 04:25:04.319
reservoirs ran dry. Imagine wandering

04:25:04.319 --> 04:25:07.120
beneath the shade of that teak forest

04:25:07.120 --> 04:25:09.760
and watching the roots of banyan and

04:25:09.760 --> 04:25:13.199
silk cotton trees slowly bind their way

04:25:13.199 --> 04:25:15.199
over the ruins

04:25:15.199 --> 04:25:18.640
as the layers of ash fell from the sky

04:25:18.640 --> 04:25:21.760
season after season and covered the

04:25:21.760 --> 04:25:23.920
works of man.

04:25:23.920 --> 04:25:27.040
Imagine turning away and setting off

04:25:27.040 --> 04:25:31.760
into the forest as the sun finally set

04:25:31.760 --> 04:25:36.520
on Java's golden age.

04:25:40.800 --> 04:25:43.680
A great temple complex from ancient

04:25:43.680 --> 04:25:47.600
times rose near a mountain stream, and

04:25:47.600 --> 04:25:50.399
the path there was lonely.

04:25:50.399 --> 04:25:53.199
The curved trunks of the water elephants

04:25:53.199 --> 04:25:55.840
had fallen and crumbled, and for lack of

04:25:55.840 --> 04:25:59.520
care, its wall had almost tumbled down.

04:25:59.520 --> 04:26:02.319
The monster heads seemed to be weeping

04:26:02.319 --> 04:26:04.399
as their covered faces were overgrown

04:26:04.399 --> 04:26:07.279
with creepers, and as though sad and

04:26:07.279 --> 04:26:10.000
weary, the temple guardians lay rolled

04:26:10.000 --> 04:26:12.640
over on the ground.

04:26:12.640 --> 04:26:14.640
The pavilions in its courtyard were in

04:26:14.640 --> 04:26:16.159
ruins.

04:26:16.159 --> 04:26:17.760
Some of the buildings were now only

04:26:17.760 --> 04:26:20.080
wreckage, while others were rotting

04:26:20.080 --> 04:26:23.199
away. Their roofs were broken and had

04:26:23.199 --> 04:26:25.840
fallen in, and beyond repair their

04:26:25.840 --> 04:26:28.640
pillars stood a skew, swaying back and

04:26:28.640 --> 04:26:30.640
forth.

04:26:30.640 --> 04:26:32.640
Heartending was the spectacle of the

04:26:32.640 --> 04:26:34.159
reliefs.

04:26:34.159 --> 04:26:37.520
Young maidens in stone stood, gazing

04:26:37.520 --> 04:26:41.120
skywards, full of sorrow, because now no

04:26:41.120 --> 04:26:44.640
wandering poets ever came to visit them.

04:26:44.640 --> 04:26:47.680
The tower temple soared on high and its

04:26:47.680 --> 04:26:49.760
pinnacles served as a gathering place

04:26:49.760 --> 04:26:53.439
for weeds. The sides were cracked,

04:26:53.439 --> 04:26:55.760
overgrown by a shady fig tree which

04:26:55.760 --> 04:26:58.640
spread luxurantly.

04:26:58.640 --> 04:27:00.640
All the statues were cracked by a

04:27:00.640 --> 04:27:03.920
fearsome tangle of vines, and only the

04:27:03.920 --> 04:27:06.479
main deity within was immovably in

04:27:06.479 --> 04:27:09.520
place, standing firm in the center of

04:27:09.520 --> 04:27:12.720
its pedestal. Pandan trees hung down

04:27:12.720 --> 04:27:15.920
over the rocks with an air of sadness

04:27:15.920 --> 04:27:18.800
quite wrapped in the mist.

04:27:18.800 --> 04:27:20.960
How they longed to be visited by the

04:27:20.960 --> 04:27:22.960
thunder which would bring with it the

04:27:22.960 --> 04:27:25.439
rushing of the rain.

04:27:25.439 --> 04:27:28.000
As if in sorrow they let their petals

04:27:28.000 --> 04:27:30.720
droop. Petals on which someone had

04:27:30.720 --> 04:27:32.960
jotted down some words in a moment of

04:27:32.960 --> 04:27:34.960
inspiration.

04:27:34.960 --> 04:27:37.920
For is this not an admirable place for a

04:27:37.920 --> 04:27:42.920
wandering poet to weave his verses.

04:27:58.960 --> 04:28:01.199
Thank you once again for listening to

04:28:01.199 --> 04:28:04.640
the Fall of Civilizations podcast.

04:28:04.640 --> 04:28:06.720
I'd like to thank my voice actors for

04:28:06.720 --> 04:28:09.920
this episode. Henry Stenhouse, Michael

04:28:09.920 --> 04:28:13.600
Antonis, Alexandra Bolton, Simon

04:28:13.600 --> 04:28:16.800
Jackson, Catherine James, Tom Marshall

04:28:16.800 --> 04:28:20.640
Lee, Chris Harvey, Jack Jacobs, Nick

04:28:20.640 --> 04:28:25.040
Denton, Amrit Sandu, Paul Cassell, Tim

04:28:25.040 --> 04:28:29.439
Stevenson, and Amin Tahare.

04:28:29.439 --> 04:28:32.720
Readings in old and middle Javanese were

04:28:32.720 --> 04:28:36.479
performed by Feris Sanaya and Kada

04:28:36.479 --> 04:28:38.800
Adita.

04:28:38.800 --> 04:28:40.960
I'd also like to thank my historical

04:28:40.960 --> 04:28:45.120
adviser for this episode Dr. Alex West.

04:28:45.120 --> 04:28:47.199
Major sources used in the writing of

04:28:47.199 --> 04:28:50.640
this episode were Majapahit by Harold

04:28:50.640 --> 04:28:53.120
Vanerinda, the Indianized States of

04:28:53.120 --> 04:28:56.000
Southeast Asia edited by Obalta F. Fella

04:28:56.000 --> 04:28:59.040
and translated by Sue Brown Cohen. When

